x_comment('x_generateFormulasForElements-TermGenls',"(#$generateFormulasForElements-TermGenls TERM SET) means that if a specialization of TERM is a valid term in the search query results, then elements of SET ( a set or collection), INS, should have the appropriate formulas generated for them.  This predicate is used in the CAE query search.  The appropriate formula, at this point is determined by whether INS is a collection or a predicate.  If INS is a collection, then (#$isa ?X INS) is the appropriate formula.  If INS is a predicate with arity N, then (INS ?VAR1, ..., VARN) is an appropriate formula, along with any well-formed other substitutions of other elements of SET into that formula, provided SET is an extensional set.") :- x_cid(a65b16505ecc5f).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505ecc5f,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
