x_comment(x_Decibel," When referring to measurements of power or intensity, when applied to a number or other #$NumericInterval (pair of numeric-intervals), #$Decibel returns ten times the base-10 logarithm of its argument (the interval between its two arguments) divided by the implicit reference value.  \n<p>\nDecibels are commonly used to measure sound pressure levels.   When referring to measurements of sound pressure (or amplitude), when applied to a number or other #$NumericInterval (pair of numeric-intervals), #$Decibel returns the instance of #$IntervalOnNumberLine that is twenty times the base-10 logarithm of its argument (the interval between its two arguments) divided by the implicit reference value. The commonly used reference sound pressure in air is pref = 20 micropascals (rms). In underwater acoustics, the reference sound pressure is pref = 1 micropascal (rms).") :- x_cid(a65b16505ecf24).
