x_comment('x_SurfaceLayer-TopSurface',"The collection of all top surface layers of objects which entirely cover the tops of the objects, e.g., table top surfaces, or the surface of a body of water.  It excludes undersides.  The 'top' surface is the highest-up surface of the uppermost parts of a SpatialThing when it is in its normal position; if the top is curved, like the back of a pig, the top surface includes the skin over the backbone and an indefinite amount of surrounding skin. The top surface of a body of water (like a lake) is the surface exposed to the air. (See also #$EntireSurfaceLayer.)") :- x_cid(a65b16505ed1c2).
