xc_mapping_rows(a65b16505ed69f,[]).
x_comment('x_InanimateObject-NonNatural',"A collection of tangible things.  An instance of #$InanimateObject-NonNatural is a tangible which was created during a #$PurposefulAction by an #$Agent-PartiallyTangible (or a group of #$Agent-PartiallyTangibles working together) whether or not that creation was intended.  If the creation was intended the thing created is an instance of the more specific collection, #$Artifact.\n<p>\nLet's consider some positive and negative examples.\n<p>\nIn addition to the obvious human #$Artifacts (buildings, tools, textiles, power lines), this collection includes #$Artifacts made by #$NonPersonAnimals, such as bird nests, termite mounds, and beaver dams.  By-products (see #$byProducts) of #$PurposefulActions, such as wood chips created when chopping down a tree and slag created when obtaining metal from #$MineralOre, are instances of #$InanimateObject-NonNatural but not of #$Artifact.  For more details on what is included in the concept #$Artifact, examine its comment.\n<p>\nNegative examples include bodily excretions (see #$ExcretionSubstance), most instances of tracks made while walking through mud or snow (both being instances of #$InanimateObject-Natural, and spoken words (being intangible).") :- x_cid(a65b16505ed6a0).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505ed6a0,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16505ed6a0,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part07.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16505ed6a0,7760).
xc_kb_names(a65b16505ed6a0,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16505ed6a0,[]).
