x_comment(x_usesCommunicationConventionForWork,"A ternary predicate. (#$usesCommunicationConvention INFO_STRUCT CC CW) means that the #$InformationStore, INFO_STRUCT, uses the #$CommunicationConvention, CC, to represent the #$ConceptualWork, CW.  For example, the original version of the Iliad uses the #$AncientGreekLanguage as a #$CommunicationConvention, while a modern translation into Tagalog uses the #$TagalogLanguage and, when written, uses the #$WesternEuropeanWriting #$orthography as another #$CommunicationConvention. See also #$usesCommConventionForInfo, which relates an #$AspatialInformationStore, a #$CommunicationConvention and an #$InformationBearingThing.") :- x_cid(a65b16505ed6c0).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505ed6c0,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16505ed6c0,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part07.krf').
