x_comment(x_feelsTowardsPersonType,"(#$feelsTowardsPersonType AGENT PERSONTYPE\n  QUANT) says that AGENT\n  has the quantity of feeling QUANT\n  towards PERSONTYPE.  This predicate is useful\n  in conveying notions of #$Prejudice and \n   preference -- notions for which \n   #$feelsTowardsObjectToDegree are not especially \n    well-suited; having feelings towards a \ngroup is by no means identical to having \nfeelings towards each member of that group.\n  Examples of how to use this predicate: To say that\n   the KKK feels a great deal of hostility towards\n  people of African descent, one can say\n '(#$feelsTowardsPersonType #$KuKluxKlan\n   #$EthnicGroupOfNewWorldBlacks\n   (#$MediumToVeryHighAmountFn #$Hostility)) .'  To say\n  that each individual Klansmen is so hostile, we can use\n  the rule, '(#$implies (#$hasMembers \n   #$KuKluxKlan ?HICK) (#$feelsTowardsPersonType\n ?HICK #$EthnicGroupOfNewWorldBlacks\n (#$MediumToVeryHighAmountFn #$Hostility))).'  See the\n  #$salientAssertions to get a sense of how\n  feelings towards a group relate to the \n   individual members of that group.") :- x_cid(a65b16505ed6d3).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505ed6d3,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
