x_comment(x_EmptyTimeInterval,"The collection of all 'empty' time intervals (whether continuous or discontinuous).  Elements are always intangible, abstract  relevant-event-free intervals of time.  An instance of #$EmptyTimeInterval is 'empty' of relevant or salient #$Events;  what is relevant or salient depends on the context.  In a StoryMt a piece of time where nothing notable happens is an instance of #$EmptyTimeInterval.  In a physics context, the background buzz of atoms may be relevant events, whereas that would not be relevant during a non-state-change of an electronic device, or a boring wait for a train.  See also #$TimeInterval.\n<p>\nThus #$EmptyTimeInterval does NOT represent a time interval of duration zero (see #$TimePoint), but rather a (possibly long discontinuous) interval of 'empty time', which, analogous to 'empty space' (see #$FreeSpaceRegion), is an\ninterval of time in which nothing happens. Just as with space, where a region is empty only for some limited period of time, so too is it likely that an #$EmptyTimeInterval only makes sense for some limited region of space and limited context of relevant actions.") :- x_cid(a65b16505ed6dd).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505ed6dd,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
