x_comment(x_typeHasStyle,"(#$typeHasStyle TYPE STYLE) means that every instance of collection, TYPE, has (in some sense) STYLE.  This is one of the broadest predicates that can be used to ascribe a style to a type of thing.  This is not equivalent to (#$relationAllInstance #$hasStyle TYPE STYLE).  This latter\nassertion entails that every instance of Type is an instance of STYLE.  This is a somewhat weaker relation.  Consider the relation between a type of music and its\ngenre: (#$typeHasStyle #$ReggaeMusic #$MusicalComposition-Reggae) holds but ReggaeMusic is \na specialization of #$Music which is a specialization of #$InformationBearingThing.  #$InformationBearingThing is disjoint from MusicalComposition of which #$MusicalComposition-Reggae is a specialization.  Hence, (#$relationAllInstance #$hasStyle #$ReggaeMusic #$MusicalComposition-Reggae) is false.  Avoid using this predicate in favor of more specific ones.") :- x_cid(a65b16505ed6e3).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505ed6e3,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16505ed6e3,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part07.krf').
