x_comment(x_physicalReferentOf,"This binary predicate is used to assert that a particular\n\n#$PartiallyTangible object or #$PhysicalEvent is the 'physical\n\nreferent' used to 'pin down' a particular #$SpatialThing. If a\n\n#$SpatialThing 'exists' in the empirically observable universe, i.e.,\n\nif it is a #$SpatialThing-Localized, then it must be localized in\n\nvirtue either of some physical reference point or of some other\n\n#$Intangible #$SpatialThing-Localized.  A spatial system, like the\n\n#$GeodeticCoordinateSystem, must ultimately 'ground out' in 'physical\n\nentities' that are either #$PartiallyTangible, like the\n\n#$RoyalObservatory-Greenwich, or that are #$PhysicalEvents, like the\n\n#$RotationOfEarth.  This predicate is very broad: it could, for\n\nexample, be used to represent the case where a boundary stone is used\n\nto mark a property boundary, the case where the rotation of the earth\n\nlocalizes the geographic poles, and the case of the\n\n#$RoyalObservatory-Greenwich being used to 'ground' the\n\n#$GeodeticCoordinateSystem.  Borderline cases include cases where\n\nborders are instantiated by physical objects, the way the Rio Grande\n\ninstantiates part of the US-Mexico border or the way the ridge of\n\nEverest instantiates part of the Nepal-Tibetan border.  Non-examples\n\ninclude cases where one #$Intangible #$SpatialThing-Localized is used\n\nto localize another: for example, the case where the geographic poles\n\nare used to localize the #$EarthsEquator.") :- x_cid(a65b16505ed6ef).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505ed6ef,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16505ed6ef,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part07.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16505ed6ef,7947).
xc_kb_names(a65b16505ed6ef,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16505ed6ef,[]).
x_comment(x_BlankSurface,"A subcollection of #$SurfaceRegion-Tangible, each instance is a surface not written or printed on.") :- x_cid(a65b16505ed6f0).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505ed6f0,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16505ed6f0,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part07.krf').
