x_comment(x_tradeBalanceInWithDuring,"(#$tradeBalanceInWithDuring REGION1 PRODUCT-TYPE REGION2 THING MONEY) means that the instance of #$MonetaryValue MONEY is a measure of the difference between the value of the instances of the #$ProductType PRODUCT-TYPE exported by the #$GeographicalRegion REGION1 to the #$GeographicalRegion REGION2 during the temporal extent of the #$TemporalThing THING and the value of the instances of PRODUCT-TYPE imported by REGION1 from REGION2 during the temporal extent of THING.  (THING will often be a calendar time period.)  Thus if the value of REGION1's exports of PRODUCT-TYPE to REGION2 is greater than the value of its imports of PRODUCT-TYPE from REGION2 during the temporal extent of THING, REGION1 will have a positive trade balance in PRODUCT-TYPE with REGION2.  If the value of its imports of PRODUCT-TYPE from REGION2 exceeds that of its exports, it will have a negative trade balance in PRODUCT-TYPE with REGION2.  This latter case can be expressed using a #$UnitOfMoney function with a negative number as its argument.") :- x_cid(a65b16505ed6f8).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505ed6f8,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16505ed6f8,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part07.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16505ed6f8,7998).
xc_kb_names(a65b16505ed6f8,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16505ed6f8,[]).
x_comment(x_GeographicalSpaceRegionFn,"(#$GeographicalSpaceRegionFn OBJECT) denotes the location in  in geographical space of OBJECT, an instance of #$GeographicalThing.  This function denotes a portion of the geographical surface of reference  (see #$GeographicalSpaceRegion) on which OBJECT is projected, i.e. this function  does *not* denote the spatial extent of object, but a surface projection. The spatial extent in a tridimensional space at a given time is denoted by #$SpaceOccupiedByFn. In order to  denote the instance of #$GeographicalRegion at which OBJECT stands in the context of geography, see #$GeographicalSpaceRegionFn and its corresponding predicate. See  #$exactlyLocatedAt-SurfaceGeographical, the predicate corresponding to #$GeographicalSpaceRegionFn.") :- x_cid(a65b16505ed6f9).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505ed6f9,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16505ed6f9,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part07.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16505ed6f9,7999).
xc_kb_names(a65b16505ed6f9,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16505ed6f9,[]).
x_comment(x_CredibilityStatus,"This attribute denotes the default amount of trust or faith that one agent puts in the statements, predictions, and promises of another.  Of course, agents can be credible in certain contexts and not others -- to specify the credibility of a particular instance of\n\n#$Communicating, see #$credibilityToAgent.") :- x_cid(a65b16505ed6fa).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505ed6fa,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16505ed6fa,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part07.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16505ed6fa,8000).
xc_kb_names(a65b16505ed6fa,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16505ed6fa,[]).
x_comment(x_UnreifiableFunction,"A specialization of #$Function-Denotational instances of which are such  that their values are not reified in the Cyc system.  More precisely, an instance of #$UnreifiableFunction is such that closed \"NATs\" (see  #$CycLNonAtomicTerm) built from its standard CycL name are _not_ instances of  #$HLReifiedDenotationalTerm.   Constrast with #$ReifiableFunction.  Usually it is more efficient to make functions reifiable; but it is not desirable  to reify every non-atomic term, such as those built from (names of)  instances of #$MathematicalFunctionOnScalars.  For example, it would be cumbersome to reify every term of the form (#$Inch N) that happened to appear in a CycL assertion.") :- x_cid(a65b16505ed6fb).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505ed6fb,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16505ed6fb,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part07.krf').
