x_comment(x_subjectivelyEvaluatesIndividualToThing,"This predicate can be used to assert that an agent has made a certain essentially subjective assessment or value judgment about a particular individual in relation to a topic.  (#$subjectivelyEvaluatesIndividualToThing AGENT INDIV TOPIC EVAL) means that the AGENT projects upon INDIV the #$EvaluativeQuantity (q.v.) EVAL in regard to the TOPIC.  As the evaluation in question is essentially subjective, the above formula of course does not entail either (i) that INDIV actually has the feature it is subjectively thought to have (or some \"objective\" counterpart thereof) or (ii) that any other given agent would also attribute EVAL to INDIV.  Indeed, outside of contexts explicitly defined so as to represent some particular agent's point of view (e.g. some sentient agent's inner mental world or the world-view espoused by a particular religion), it arguably makes no sense to attribute an #$EvaluativeQuantity to an individual directly.  ") :- x_cid(a65b16505ed709).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505ed709,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16505ed709,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part07.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16505ed709,8018).
xc_kb_names(a65b16505ed709,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16505ed709,[]).
x_comment(x_MSTrustedSitesZoneFn,"One of a series of functions used to represent Microsoft's \"Internet Security Zone\" concept. The function takes as its argument an instance of #$ThingTypeByCapability-Passive, which describes some action which it is possible to perform on certain computers, and allows one to state that that action may be initiated from the \"Trusted Sites Zone\". The result of this function is therefore also a (qualified) instance of #$ThingTypeByCapability-Passive. The term \"Trusted Sites Zone\" refers to sites which have been explicitly defined for that computer as Trusted\". For the meaning of this term, please consult #$MicrosoftInc documentation.") :- x_cid(a65b16505ed70a).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505ed70a,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16505ed70a,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part07.krf').
