xc_mapping_rows(a65b16505ed70a,[]).
x_comment(x_harmfulProposition,"The predicate #$harmfulProposition is used to state a condition that, if true, would (normally) diminish an agent's chances of success in a particular effort.  (#$harmfulProposition ENDEAVOR PROP GVP) means that if the #$ELSentence-Assertible PROP is true, then AGENT (who is referred to in PROP) will (normally) be hindered in achieving the #$PurposefulAction ENDEAVOR.   GVP is a #$GenericValuePredicate whose role is to suggest how damaging such an occurrence would be to the success of ENDEAVOR.  For example, in a basketball game, it's normally very detrimental if one or more of the team's players is shorter than the average adult.  Thus, for any particular game, a #$highToVeryHighAmountOf disadvantage is indicated if the following #$harmfulProposition (expressed in #$CycL) is true: (#$heightOfObject PLAYER-X (#$RelativeGenericValueFn #$heightOfObject #$HumanAdult #$veryLowAmountOf)). (Rohrbaugh, 2/1998)") :- x_cid(a65b16505ed70b).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505ed70b,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
