x_comment(x_totalSolutesInAqueousSolution,"(#$totalSolutesInAqueousSolution SOLUTION SET-OF-SUBST) holds just in case water is the solvent in SOLUTION and each major solute present in SOLUTION is in SET-OF-SUBST.  SET-OF-SUBST includes both molecular substance types and strong electrolytes -- which appear only as separate ions in the solution.  Normally, it is implicit in the expression \"a .10M HCl solution\" that the solution contains no solutes other than HCl. We can make that assumption explicit by asserting: (#$totalSolutesInAqueousSolution SOLUTION-A (#$TheSet #$HydrogenChloride)).  Note that #$totalSolutesInAqueousSolution allows one to enumerate only the complete accounting of the major solutes in a sample -- #$totalSolutesInAqueousSolution is asserted to be #$completeExtentEnumerable (q.v.).") :- x_cid(a65b16505ed728).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505ed728,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
