x_comment(x_resultNotIsa,"The predicate is used to indicate that any value returned by a particular denotational function may not be an instance of a certain collection. (#$resultNotIsa FUNC COL) means that FUNC returns a value that is not an instance of COL for any sequence of arguments for which it is defined.  Thus, where FUNC is defined for the sequence ARG1, ..., ARGn, (#$resultIsa FUNC COL) implies (#$not (#$isa (FUNC ARG1...ARGn) COL)).  See also #$resultIsa and #$resultDisjointWith.") :- x_cid(a65b16505ed729).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505ed729,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
