xc_mapping_rows(a65b16505ed74a,[]).
x_comment('x_Revolution-Political',"A specialization of #$ChangeOfGovernment.  Each instance of #$Revolution-Political is an event in which the previous government of a country or subregion of a country is replaced by a new regime, through political and military actions performed at least in large part by people who ahd been living under the old regime.  This collection includes the full notion of a revolution from the #$EscalationOfHostilities (which may vary from historian to historian), including the actual instance of #$War, and ending with the creation of a new instance of #$RegionalGovernment.\n<p>\nIn short, a #$Revolution-Political is a successful instance of #$Insurgency.") :- x_cid(a65b16505ed74b).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505ed74b,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16505ed74b,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part07.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16505ed74b,8114).
xc_kb_names(a65b16505ed74b,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16505ed74b,[]).
x_comment('x_conditionallyIndependent-GivenSet',"A predicate used for probability statements.  (#$conditionallyIndependent-GivenSet PROPOSITION1 PROPOSITION2 SETOFPROPOSITIONS) means that, in the applicable #$Microtheory,  PROPOSITION1 and PROPOSITION2 are conditionally independent of each other given the truth of all the propositions in the set SETOFPROPOSITIONS.  That is, given the truth of the propositions in the set, the truth or falsehood of either of the two propostion arguments does not increase or decrease the #$derivedProbability that the other is true.  They are, in a sense, irrelevant to each other when the propositions in SETOFPROPOSITIONS is known to be true.  In most microtheories, generally, the #$conditionallyIndependent-GivenSet statement means that when all we know in the #$Microtheory are its accessible #$domainAssumptions, and the assertions in SETOFPROPOSITIONS, then the truths of the two formulae are probabilistically independent.  See also #$conditionalProbability and #$conditionallyIndependent.  To declare two propositions independent given a single proposition (which could be a conjunction), use #$conditionallyIndependentSentences.  This definition makes no presumption as to determinism versus nondeterminism, nor as to whether probability is only in the mind of some beholder.  The definition allows for any of several different systems of deriving the probability of one assertion from the probabilities of, or conditional probabilities relating, other assertions.") :- x_cid(a65b16505ed74c).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505ed74c,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16505ed74c,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part07.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16505ed74c,8117).
xc_kb_names(a65b16505ed74c,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16505ed74c,[]).
x_comment(x_ToxicitySlot,"A specialization of #$QuantitySlot. Instances are predicates that relate an instance of #$PartiallyTangible to their #$Toxicity with respect to a particular route, such as inhalation, skin-contact, or eye-absorption.") :- x_cid(a65b16505ed74d).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505ed74d,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
