x_comment(x_subRegions,"(#$subRegions SUPER SUB) means that SUPER and SUB are both (effectively) two-dimensional regions (see #$SurfaceRegion) and that SUB lies wholly within SUPER (see #$inRegion). SUPER might or might not completely surround SUB.  To relate two instances of #$GeopoliticalEntity in this same way, use the predicate #$geopoliticalSubdivision (if it applies).  For other instances of #$GeographicalRegion, use #$geographicalSubRegions.") :- x_cid(a65b16505ed74f).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505ed74f,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16505ed74f,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part07.krf').
