x_comment(x_nonFocalSubjectOfInvestigation,"#$nonFocalSubjectOfInvestigation is a more specialized form of the predicate #$topicRole.  It relates an instance of #$Investigation to an instance of #$SomethingExisting.  Like #$topicRole it is intended to relate an entity to an event where that entity is part of the content of some mental state of some agent in the role of #$deliberateActors in that event.  In this case, it means that during the course of the #$CriminalInvestigation, the object is a non-focal subject of the investigation (constrast with #$subjectOfInvestigation). For instance, during a particular sub-event of a search for a missing person a detective discovers that the missing person has a vacation home based on looking at the subject's #$AddressBook and decides that the house is worth looking into.  The missing person would play the role of #$subjectOfInvestigation, the #$AddressBook would play the role of #$evidence, and the vacation house would play the role of #$nonFocalSubjectOfInvestigation.") :- x_cid(a65b16505ed766).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505ed766,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
