x_comment(x_Artifact,"A specialization of #$InanimateObject.  Each instance of #$Artifact is an at least partially tangible thing which was intentionally created by an #$Agent-PartiallyTangible (or a group of #$Agent-PartiallyTangibles working together) to serve some purpose or perform some function.  In order to create an instance of #$Artifact, it is not necessary that an #$Agent-PartiallyTangible create the matter out of which the #$Artifact is composed; rather, an #$Agent-PartiallyTangible can create an instance of #$Artifact by assembling or modifying existing matter.  Examples of #$Artifacts include a wooden flute that's been whittled from a tree branch, a sawhorse that's been put together out of boards and nails, and a coin that's been minted by embossing or by melting liquid silver into a mold.  In addition to the obvious human artifacts (buildings, tools, textiles, power lines), the collection #$Artifact also includes certain sorts of things made by #$Animals, such as bird nests, termite mounds, and beaver dams. Artifacts without any tangible parts are excluded from the collection #$Artifact; they are included in the collection #$Artifact-Intangible.") :- x_cid(a65b16505ed775).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505ed775,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16505ed775,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part07.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16505ed775,8183).
xc_kb_names(a65b16505ed775,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16505ed775,[]).
x_comment(x_succeedingValueOfMunsellHue,"#$succeedingValueOfMunsellHue is used to establish the color\nsequence of the instances of #$MunsellHue. The hues do not form a\n#$CollectionWithAnEventLikeOrder, and require a special relation to\ncapture the fact that the sequence is circular. No further assertions\nshould be made with this predicate. Please see #$MunsellHue for\nfurther information.") :- x_cid(a65b16505ed776).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505ed776,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
