x_comment(x_EquipmentTypeForStructuredActivityTypeFn,"(#$EquipmentTypeForStructuredActivityFn ACTIVITY_TYPE) denotes a collection of equipment types whose elements are used in performances of instances of ACTIVITY_TYPE (a subset of #$DevisedStructuredActivity].  There are two sufficient conditions for a given collection being an instance of this collection.  One such condition applies to device collections whose major, predominant, or primary function is to play the role of #$deviceUsed in performances of instances of ACTIVITY_TYPE (see #$primaryFunction-DeviceType).  Another such condition applies to device collections which are always used in performances of instances of ACTIVITY_TYPE (see #$eventTypeUsesDeviceType).  For example, (#$EquipmentTypeForStructuredActivityFn #$CardGame) denotes ``equipment for playing cards''.  Thus, because #$PlayingCard and #$AutomaticCardShuffler have #$CardGame as one of their main functions, Cyc should infer that these two device types are instances of (#$EquipmentTypeForStructuredActivityFn #$CardGame).") :- x_cid(a65b16505ed78b).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505ed78b,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
