x_comment(x_keIrrelevantPrecisionSuggestionFrom,"(#$keIrrelevantPrecisionSuggestionFrom ?COL1 ?COL2) states that the constant ?COL1 should never be offered as a precision suggestion from the constant ?COL2. (See #$CycPrecisionSuggestor.) ?COL1 may, however, be offered as a precision suggestion from any other constant that it is normally offered as a precision suggestion from.  For example, #$Queen-HeadOfState should NOT be offered as a precision suggestion from the constant #$FemalePerson, though it is a direct specialization of this constant and would normally be offered in this case.  We do not want to make #$Queen-HeadOfState #$keIrrelevantPrecisionSuggestion, though, because we DO want to offer it as a precision suggestion for #$Monarch-HeadOfState (of which #$Queen-HeadOfState is a direct spec).  Therefore, (#$keIrrelevantPrecisionSuggestionFrom #$Queen-HeadOfState #$FemalePerson) would be a reasonable assertion.") :- x_cid(a65b16505ed78e).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505ed78e,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
