x_comment(x_BeauxArtsArchitecturalStyle,"The #$BeauxArtsArchitecturalStyle is a neo-Greek-Roman style of building design developed in Europe that became popular in the late 19th and early 20th Centuries for large buildings, especially in #$France, and the #$UnitedStatesOfAmerica. It is characterized by the use of symmetric arrangements of columns, ornate pediments, elaborate domes, and Greek and Roman style details.  The U.S. federal and many states' #$StateCapitolBuildings are in the #$BeauxArtsArchitecturalStyle.  It passed out of style in the early 20th Century.") :- x_cid(a65b16505ed7a1).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505ed7a1,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
