x_comment(x_BalletCompany,"The collection of organizations whose #$actsInCapacity-MainFunction is to produce and present theatrical entertainment in the form of instances of #$BalletDancePerformance. Ballerinas and their male counterparts are essential employee-members of instances of #$BalletCompany. Since instances of #$BalletCompany are primarily engaged in the business of producing instances of #$BalletDancePerformance (i.e., instances of #$DramaticPerformance, and thus events which take place in front of an audience, in a theatre, and in which the predominant activity is ballet dancing), a ballet school would not be an instance of #$BalletCompany since the #$actsInCapacity-MainFunction of a ballet school is teaching ballet, not performing. (Of course, most ballet companies are affiliated with ballet schools, which schools generally have the same name - e.g., the American Ballet Theatre (company) and the School of the American Ballet - as the ballet company. But there is a distinction between the two.)") :- x_cid(a65b16505ed7a4).
