x_comment(x_fieldsOfPlantType,"(#$fieldsOfPlantType PLANTS FIELDS) means that FIELDS is the\n\ncollection of fields of instances of PLANTS. This predicate relates a type\n\nof plant to the collection of fields where this type of plant is\n\npredominante. Note in particular that althought FIELDS includes some\n\ncultivated fields [see #$AgriculturalFacility] it also includes wilderness\n\nareas covered with grass or weed [see #$Field-Land]. For instance, (#$FieldFn\n\n#$GrapeVine) is the collection of fields of #$GrapeVine and\n\n(#$fieldsOfPlantType #$GrapeVine (#$FieldFn #$GrapeVine)). See the\n\ncorresponding function #$FieldFn.") :- x_cid(a65b16505ed7a8).
