x_comment('x_predicateTypeSummaryForThing-Set',"An instance of #$SummaryPredicate useful for summarizing knowledge about more than one term. (#$predicateTypeSummaryForThing-Set PRED-TYPE SET SENTENCE) means that SENTENCE's arg0 slot is occupied by an instance PRED of PRED-TYPE and that all of the terms in the set of terms SET occupy other argument positions in SENTENCE. For example, (#$predicateTypeSummaryForThing-Set #$LikesPredicate (#$TheSet #$JenniferSullivan   #$Cynthia) (#$likesAsFriend #$JenniferSullivan #$Cynthia)) is true, and means that some instance of #$LikesPredicate occurs as the arg0 in (#$likesAsFriend #$JenniferSullivan #$Cynthia), and that all of the terms in the set denoted by (#$TheSet #$JenniferSullivan   #$Cynthia) also occur in (#$likesAsFriend #$JenniferSullivan #$Cynthia). This predicate is particularly useful for asking queries with the first and second argument slots bound and the third slot open.  For example,  asking (#$predicateTypeSummaryForThing-Set OrganismRequirementsPredicate (#$TheSet (#$AdultFn #$Dog) (#$AdultFn #$Cat)) ?SENTENCE) will mean the system will find any assertions whose arg0 is an instance of OrganismRequirementsPredicate that also contain the terms (#$AdultFn #$Dog) and (#$AdultFn #$Cat).  See also #$predicateTypeSummaryForThing.") :- x_cid(a65b16505ed7bb).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505ed7bb,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16505ed7bb,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part07.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16505ed7bb,8335).
