x_comment(x_temporalExtentInMt,"A ternary #$TemporalPredicate that relates each #$TemporalThing to the #$TimeInterval that it occupies in some particular Microtheory.  (#$temporalExtentInMt TEMP TIME MT) means that, in MT, TIME is the time-interval of longest #$duration (q.v.) during which TEMP exists (if TEMP is a #$SomethingExisting) or occurs (if an #$Event) or obtains (if a #$StaticSituation).  If TEMP is itself a time-interval, the above #$temporalExtentInMt sentence holds if and only if TIME is identical to TEMP.\n<p>\nNote that if (#$temporalExtentInMt TEMP TIME MT) holds, TIME is a #$ContinuousTimeInterval (q.v.) if and only if TEMP is #$temporallyContinuousDuring in MT (q.v.).\n<p>\nSee also the corresponding function #$TemporalExtentInMtFn.") :- x_cid(a65b16505ed7c2).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505ed7c2,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16505ed7c2,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part07.krf').
