x_comment(x_actionExpressesFeeling,"(#$actionExpressesFeeling ACT EMOTYPE) means that the particular action ACT actually expresses the doer's feeling of EMOTYPE. Note: additional\n\ncomplications arise in using this in inference, as people can `fake' actions such as laughing, crying, etc., to mislead other people. See also\n\n#$actionExpressesFeelingToward. If one wishes to make statements about tendencies rather than actual expressions, e.g. ``smiling tends to express\n\nhappiness'', see #$actionTypeExpressesFeelingType.") :- x_cid(a65b16505ed7cb).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505ed7cb,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
