x_comment(x_MIPS,"A function and an instance of #$UnitOfCPUCapacity. It is used to represent the standard unit of CPU capacity -- millions of (machine-code) instructions per second. (#$MIPS 34.0) would represent a #$CPUSpeed of around 34 million instructions per second. It has been argued that this benchmark is \"completely pointless\", since no two chips use exactly the same set of instructions, and the same set of instructions can do vastly more work depending on the chip size and the way the processing task has been structured. (For example, on a chip with #$CISCArchitecture, a single instruction may do many things when executed, whereas on a #$RISCArchitecture chip it may do very little but be dealt with more efficiently). Many other benchmarks exist, including #$MFLOPS, VUPS (\"VAX Units of Performance\"), SPEC (for which, see #$SPECint and #$SPECfp), Linpack, etc.") :- x_cid(a65b16505ed7de).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505ed7de,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
