x_comment(x_EbolaVirus,"A specialization of #$Virus. #$EbolaVirus is a member of a family of RNA viruses known as filoviruses. When magnified several thousand times by an electron microscope, these viruses have the appearance of long filaments or threads. Ebola virus was discovered in 1976 and was named for a river in #$DemocraticRepublicOfTheCongo (then Zaire), where it was first detected. Causes #$EbolaHemorrhagicFeverInfections. The natural animal host, if there is one, is currently unknown.") :- x_cid(a65b16505ed802).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505ed802,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
