x_comment(x_ambientTemperature,"A #$PhysicalFeatureBinaryPredicate. The predicate #$ambientTemperature is used to indicate the average temperature in the free space around a particular object.  (#$ambientTemperature OBJ TEMP) means that the space around the tangible object OBJ is at the #$Temperature TEMP.  Used with #$holdsIn (q.v.), #$ambientTemperature expresses the surrounding temperature for a given object at some point in time.  For the temperature of the object itself, use #$temperatureOfObject (q.v.).") :- x_cid(a65b16505ed825).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505ed825,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
