x_comment(x_EconomicSectorType,"A collection of collections.  Each instance of #$EconomicSectorType is a collection of major economic sectors, or general 'super-industries', by function, each of which in turn is the collection of all local or geographically-defined economic sectors that perform such functions.  So the collection #$ManufacturingEconomicSector in general is an instance of #$EconomicSectorType, whereas the the Brazilian manufacturing sector is an instance of #$EconomicSector-Localized.  Every instance of #$EconomicSectorType can have local examples of #$EconomicSector-Localized as its instances.  See also #$IndustryType which is more focused, as well as #$Industry-Localized, #$ProductionIndustryTypeFn, #$IndustryOfRegionFn, and #$MtOfIndustryTypeFn.") :- x_cid(a65b16505ed84b).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505ed84b,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16505ed84b,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part07.krf').
