x_comment(x_OrganizationBySector,"A collection of three disjoint collections, #$GovernmentalOrganization, #$QuasiGovernmentalOrganization and #$PrivateSectorOrganization.  Each instance of #$OrganizationBySector is a set whose elements are distinguished by the sector in which the element #$Organizations operate.  Instances of #$Organizations can be distinguished on the basis of whether they are  governmental (e.g., #$FederalCommunicationsCommission), quasi-governmental (e.g., #$FederalHomeLoanMortgageCorporation), or private sector (e.g., #$IBMInc and #$SierraClub).  This collection differs from #$OrganizationTypeByActivityType in that #$OrganizationTypeByActivityType segregates instances of #$Organization on the basis of the specific type of activity they engage in.  For example, #$ResearchOrganization is an element of the collection of #$OrganizationTypeByActivityType, but not of #$OrganizationBySector.  An instance of #$ResearchOrganization might be an instance of any of the collections, #$GovernmentalOrganization, #$QuasiGovernmentalOrganization, or #$PrivateSectorOrganization.  This collection differs from #$OrganizationTypeByProfitMotive in that #$OrganizationTypeByProfitMotive segregates instances of #$Organization on the basis of whether or not they are motivated by the desire to make a profit for their owners.") :- x_cid(a65b16505ed851).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505ed851,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16505ed851,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part07.krf').
