x_comment(x_HumanTypeByGenericClothingItemSize,"The generic sizes (S, M, L, XL, XXL)  The instances of this collection are collections of people such that everyone wears something in that size.  For example, #$Size-Generic-M is the collection of people who can  wear an article of clothing designated as a medium  It is expected that  these instances will be used with the predicate #$clothingSize.   An example assertion would be (#$clothingSize Item01 #$HumanTypeByMensGenericShirtSize #$Size-Generic-M).  That assertion means that Item01 is a medium in men's shirt sizes.  These can also be used with #$humanMeasurements.  (#$humanMeasurements Bob #$HumanTypeByMensGenericShirtSize #$Size-Generic-M) means that Bob is in the collection of people who wear a generic size medium and he is in that collection at least by virtue of his shirt size.  In other words, it means that Bob wears a medium in men's shirts.") :- x_cid(a65b16505ed87a).
