x_comment(x_Jetty,"A specialization of #$FlowControlDevice. Instances of #$Jetty are constructions that extend into a body of water from the shoreline, and are intended to direct currents. Applications incluse, but are not limited to, regulating river channels, fixing river mouths, and influencing the effects of tides. They are frequently made of timbers, earth and stone, or concrete. When constructed of earth and stone, jetties are only distinct from #$Breakwaters in purpose.") :- x_cid(a65b16505ed895).
