x_comment(x_wordForms,"(#$wordForms WORD PRED STRING) states that STRING is a PRED form of WORD\n\nin the current context, where PRED is an instance of #$SpeechPartPredicate.\n\nFor instance, in the #$EnglishMt and its spec-Mts, (#$wordForms #$Ox-TheWord\n\n#$plural \"oxen\"); (#$wordForms #$Walk-TheWord #$pastTense-Universal \"walked\").\n\nThe code support for this predicate looks up irregular forms stated in\n\nthe KB -- such as (#$plural #$Ox-TheWord \"oxen\") -- and generates regular forms\n\nsuch as \"walked\", which need not be stated in the KB.") :- x_cid(a65b16505ed8b1).
