x_comment(x_verbSemTransPartial,"(#$verbSemTransPartial VERB NUM FRAME TRANS) means that part of the translation of word sense number NUM of VERB, appearing with subcategorization frame FRAME, is TRANS. #$verbSemTransPartial assertions are designed to facilitate the specification of the semantic translations templates for a series of related frames. For example, for the verb 'model', the 'on' prepositional phrases typically indicate what is being modelled, as in  \"But for Private Ryan, DreamWorks canceled a G.I. Joe action figure modeled on Hanks.\". To avoid having to duplicate the information from the #$verbSemTrans assertion for the #$TransitiveNPFrame frame in that for the TransitivePPCompFrame-On frame, #$verbSemTransPartial can be used. For 'model', the #$verbSemTransPartial assertion for #$TransitiveFrameType would specify that the general interpretaiton for the transitive usage, such as (#$and (#$isa :ACTION (#$MakingFn #$Model-Artifact)) (#$performedBy :ACTION :SUBJECT) (#$outputsCreated :ACTION :OBJECT)), whereas the assertion for TransitivePPCompFrame-On, would just need to specify (#$similarTo :OBJECT :OBLIQUE-OBJECT).") :- x_cid(a65b16505ed8bc).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505ed8bc,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16505ed8bc,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part07.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16505ed8bc,8799).
xc_kb_names(a65b16505ed8bc,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16505ed8bc,[]).
x_comment(x_connectedViaFlexibleConnector,"(connectedViaFlexibleConnector OBJ1 OBJ2) means that OBJ1 and OBJ2 are connected via a connector which is flexable.  OBJ1 and OBJ2 can move relative to each other due to deformation of the connector.  This predicate is a specialization of #$connectedTo-SemiRigidly and a generalization of #$flapHingedTo.  Positive exemplars are two objects conected by Velcro (tm), the #$GallBladder's connection to the #$Liver, or the front cover of a #$Book-CW's connection to that book's spine.  Negative examples include a hypodermic needle's connection to the IV tube (the tube is flexible, not the connection), a door's connection to the door #$Frame (parts of the hinge rotate relative to other pars, but the hinge does not deform), and a #$Wheel's connection to an #$Axle (no deformation here, either).") :- x_cid(a65b16505ed8bd).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505ed8bd,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16505ed8bd,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part07.krf').
