x_comment(x_postalCodeBaseText,"(#$postalCodeBaseText LOCATION STRING) means that STRING is the base (non-extended, possibly incomplete) form of the postal code for LOCATION.  For addresses in the United States, STRING would correspond to the 5-digit part of the ZIP code, represented as a character string.  Note that in other parts of the world, the base part of the postal code may consist of letters, numbers, or other symbols as well (e.g., dashes, colons).  See also #$postalCodeOfAddress and #$zipCodeForLocation. The latter assumes that in the context of use (the #$Microtheory in which  relevant assertions are entered), the base part of ZIP  codes will be represented as numbers rather than as character strings.") :- x_cid(a65b16505ed8c1).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505ed8c1,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16505ed8c1,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part07.krf').
