xc_mapping_rows(a65b16505ed8c9,[]).
x_comment(x_hobbyCWPerformedBy,"(#$hobbyCWPerformedBy GAME-CW PRSN) means that the instance of #$DevisedStructuredActivity is a type of hobby activity performed by #$Person PRSN. For example, (#$hobbyCWPerformedBy #$Golf #$BillClinton) means that #$BillClinton has #$Golf as a hobby. This predicate should be used only when PRSN sometimes plays the role of #$performedBy in events that are performances of GAME-CW. For example, if #$MWakoff enjoys watching #$Golf, but doesn't know how to golf, it would be incorrect to assert (#$hobbyCWPerformedBy #$Golf #$MWakoff). Use #$performancesOfWorkAre to relate instances of #$DevisedStructuredActivity to the events which are performances of them. Use #$hobbyScriptPerformedBy to relate an instance of #$ScriptType to an instance of #$Person who performs this activity as a hobby.") :- x_cid(a65b16505ed8ca).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505ed8ca,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
