x_comment(x_ReasoningWithMultiFutureMicrotheory,"Each instance MT of #$ReasoningWithMultiFutureMicrotheory\n\nhas access to the notions of historical possibility and necessity in\n\n#$ReasoningWithMultiFuture-LogicMt.  Such an MT may have\n\n#$mtAlternatives microtheories.  #$mtAlternatives microtheories stand\n\nfor the `same moment' relative to different possible futures at the\n\nmoment.  Thus for each instance PROP of\n\n#$ELSentence-AssertibleWithoutOpenFutureTrace, PROP is true in MT iff it is true in\n\nall MT's #$mtAlternatives, while a formula that is not an instance of\n\n#$ELSentence-AssertibleWithoutOpenFutureTrace may have different truth values in MT's\n\ndifferent #$mtAlternatives.  A subcollection of this collection is\n\n#$ReasoningWithMultiFutureMicrotheory-SingleDateSeries.") :- x_cid(a65b16505ed8d7).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505ed8d7,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
