x_comment(x_hobbyScriptPerformedBy,"(#$hobbyScriptPerformedBy SCRIPT-TYPE PRSN) means that the instance of #$ScriptType SCRIPT-TYPE is a type of hobby activity performed by #$Person PRSN. For example, (#$hobbyScriptPerformedBy #$FigureSkating #$MWakoff) means that #$MWakoff has #$FigureSkating as a hobby. This predicate should be used only when PRSN sometimes plays the role of #$performedBy in events of type SCRIPT-TYPE. For example, if #$MWakoff enjoys watching surfing but doesn't know how to surf, it would be incorrect to assert (#$hobbyScriptPerformedBy #$Surfing #$MWakoff) Use #$hobbyCWPerformedBy to relate an instance of #$DevisedStructuredActivity to an instance of #$Person who has this activity as a hobby.") :- x_cid(a65b16505ed8e6).
