xc_mapping_rows(a65b16505ed8fe,[]).
x_comment(x_exchangers,"The predicate #$exchangers is used to identify the (typically, two) #$Agent-PartiallyTangibles involved in an instance of #$ExchangeOfUserRights.   In such an event, each of the #$exchangers gives up possession of one thing and gains possession of another which was previously possessed by the other agent.  <code>(#$exchangers EXCH AGENT)</code> means that <code>AGENT</code> is one of the parties having such a dual role in the #$ExchangeOfUserRights <code>EXCH</code>.  Every instance of #$ExchangeOfUserRights has two sub-events which are instances of #$TransferringPossession (e.g., a dollar bill goes in one direction and some french fries and a few coins go in the other direction.)  Each of the #$exchangers is both a #$toPossessor (in one of the two #$TransferringPossession sub-events of <code>EXCH)</code> and a #$fromPossessor (in the other sub-event).") :- x_cid(a65b16505ed8ff).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505ed8ff,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16505ed8ff,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part07.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16505ed8ff,8900).
xc_kb_names(a65b16505ed8ff,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16505ed8ff,[]).
x_comment(x_TakingSomething,"A collection of events; a subcollection of #$GainingUserRights.  In an instance of #$TakingSomething, an #$Agent-PartiallyTangible takes an object, in the sense of taking it away or using or exercising access to it.  The agent may or may not have any legal right or authorization to use that object.  In an instance of #$TakingSomething, the taker (the #$toPossessor) must intend and actively (attempt to) acquire the #$objectTaken, so the taking event is intentional and thus, strictly speaking, #$performedBy the taker.") :- x_cid(a65b16505ed900).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505ed900,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16505ed900,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part07.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16505ed900,8901).
xc_kb_names(a65b16505ed900,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16505ed900,[]).
x_comment(x_PostOfficeOrganization,"A collection of local government organizations.  An element of #$PostOfficeOrganization is a particular Post Office organization -- postal station, mailing facility, or branch office -- having a particular location.  Note that this collection includes only government post offices, not non-government commercial shippers who offer various kinds of shipping services, sometimes including Postal services.") :- x_cid(a65b16505ed901).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505ed901,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16505ed901,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part07.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16505ed901,8902).
xc_kb_names(a65b16505ed901,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16505ed901,[]).
x_comment(x_ChangeInUserRights,"A collection of events and a specialization of #$GeneralizedTransfer.  Each instance of #$ChangeInUserRights is an event in which some instance of #$Agent-PartiallyTangible either gains or loses possession of something.   \"Possession\" means having some right to use a thing that one has in hand or otherwise has access to.  Different types of possession (e.g. ownership, rental, borrowings) can be specified by using the appropriate instance(s) of #$SituationTypeByUserRights (q.v.).  Changes in an agent's user rights can come about in various ways: through buying and selling, renting, borrowing or lending, giving, repossession, etc.  Specializations of this collection include #$LosingUserRights, #$GainingUserRights, and #$ExchangeOfUserRights; in the latter collection, there is an alteration in the rights of two (or more) agents to use two (or more) items -- as in a purchase, when one agent gets full use rights to an object by turning over a sum of money to the object's previous owner.  In addition, some changes in user rights are classified explicitly in #$TemporaryChangeOfUserRights (e.g. borrowing, renting), while others are permanent.   Events that involve such changes in user rights all belong in the collection of events, #$ChangeInUserRights.   In any particular #$ChangeInUserRights event, the item which is changing hands is identified as the #$objectOfPossessionTransfer.") :- x_cid(a65b16505ed902).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505ed902,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16505ed902,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part07.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16505ed902,8903).
xc_kb_names(a65b16505ed902,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16505ed902,[]).
x_comment(x_CourseOfStudyFn,"#$CourseOfStudyFn takes as argument any instance of #$Thing and returns the collection of all instances of #$CourseOfStudy in which that thing is (a signficant part of) what is studied.  For example, (#$CourseOfStudyFn #$Philosophy-Ancient) returns the collection of all courses in which material from the field of Ancient Philosophy is studied.  (#$CourseOfStudyFn #$HairCuttingEvent) returns the collection of all courses in which hair cutting is the subject of study.") :- x_cid(a65b16505ed903).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505ed903,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16505ed903,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part07.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16505ed903,8904).
xc_kb_names(a65b16505ed903,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16505ed903,[]).
x_comment('x_keSuggestionPreds-InsIns',"A #$KEFacilitationPredicate and #$RuleMacroPredicate.  <code>(#$keSuggestionPreds-InsIns COL1 BINPRED COL2)</code> means that for every known instance <code>INS1</code> of <code>COL1</code>, it is suggested that there be some instance <code>INS2</code> of <code>COL2</code> such that <code>(BINPRED INS1 INS2)</code> is known in the knowledge base.\n<p>\nFor example,\n<p>\n(#$keSuggestionPreds-InsIns #$DefaultDisjointEdibleStuffType #$typicalTasteOfType #$ObjectTypeByTaste)\n<p>\nmeans that for every known instance <code>ES-TYPE</code> of #$DefaultDisjointEdibleStuffType, it is suggested that there be some instance <code>TASTE</code> of #$ObjectTypeByTaste such that <code>(#$typicalTasteOfType ES-TYPE TASTE)</code> is known in the knowledge base.\n<p>\nSee also #$keSuggestionPredsInverse-InsIns.") :- x_cid(a65b16505ed904).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505ed904,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16505ed904,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part07.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16505ed904,8905).
xc_kb_names(a65b16505ed904,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16505ed904,[]).
x_comment(x_TemporalExtentFn,"A unary #$IndividualDenotingFunction that maps each #$TemporalThing to the #$TimeInterval that it occupies.  (#$TemporalExtentFn TEMP) is the time-interval of longest #$duration (q.v.) during which TEMP exists (if TEMP is a #$SomethingExisting) or occurs (if an #$Event) or obtains (if a #$StaticSituation).  If TEMP is itself a time-interval, (#$TemporalExtentFn TEMP) is identical to TEMP.\n<p>\nNote that (#$TemporalExtentFn TEMP) is a #$ContinuousTimeInterval (q.v.) if and only if TEMP is #$temporallyContinuousDuring (q.v.).\n<p>\nSee also the corresponding predicate #$temporalExtent.") :- x_cid(a65b16505ed905).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505ed905,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16505ed905,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part07.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16505ed905,8914).
xc_kb_names(a65b16505ed905,[]).
