x_comment(x_inConfigurationType,"(#$inConfigurationType OBJECT TYPE) means that OBJECT is one of the objects configured (see #$configuredObjects) in a #$Configuration of TYPE.  (#$inConfigurationType ROPE75 #$KnotConfiguration) means that ROPE75 is in the #$Configuration (or #$Situation) of being in a knot. This predicate is also useful for translating locutions in which shapes are attributed to an object by reference to a shape situation type that the object is in, as in 'All DNA-Molecules are in a helix configuration' or 'The group of people is in a circle': (#$relationAllInstance #$inConfigurationType #$DNAMolecule (#$ShapesConfigurationSituationFn #$Helix)) means that all DNA molecules are in a helix configuration. (#$inConfigurationType GROUPOFPEOPLE (#$ShapesConfigurationSituationFn #$Circular)) means that GROUPOFPEOPLE are in a a circular configuration (or are 'in a circle').") :- x_cid(a65b16505ed906).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505ed906,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
