x_comment(x_OrderedDifferenceWRTPredicate,"The collection of #$DifferenceWRTPredicates in which two things are compared along a dimension which has a partial ordering. Contrast (1) comparing two species with respect to possessing wings with (2) comparing two species with respect to the typical height of its members. Only the latter would be an #$OrderedDifferenceWRTPredicate since heights can be ordered but having wings cannot.  #$OrderedDifferenceWRTPredicates that are defined compositionally have the respect of difference represented explicitly by one or more arguments. Often these arguments will have an instance of either #$PartialOrderAttributeType or #$BinaryAttributePredicate as an argument constraint. In the latter case, the instance of #$BinaryAttributePredicate serving as the argument constraint for the #$OrderedDifferenceWRTPredicate should have an instance of #$PartialOrderAttributeType as its second argument constraint. If the predicate is defined noncompositionally, then the ordering along which things are compared is left implicit (often mentioned only in the constant name). A  positive example of a compositional #$OrderedDifferenceWRTPredicate is #$typesGreaterInQuantity. It is used to represent that one collection has a greater degree of some instance of a #$LinearOrderAttributeType than another collection. A positive example of a noncompositional #$OrderedDifferenceWRTPredicate is #$greaterEffectForSitType-ThanSitType.") :- x_cid(a65b16505ed925).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505ed925,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
