x_comment(x_subDivisionLevelOf,"'(#$subDivisionLevelOf STRUCTURE DIVISION N)' means that DIVISION is one of the #$subStructures of N divisions of the #$GraphicalStructure STRUCTURE.  For example, if a work is divided into chapters and there are no higher level divisions within which the chapters are contained, then (#$subDivisionLevelOf CWSTRUCTURE CHAPTER 0) where CWSTRUCTURE is a #$TextualPCWStructure.  As another example, consider a titled section within a chapter within the first part of a #$TextualPCWStructure (i.e., Section 1 of Chapter 1 of Part I).  A number of different assertions could be made regarding the different parts of the overall #$GraphicalStructure of the text (e.g., (#$subDivisionLevelOf CWSTRUCTURE CHAPTER 1)...(#$subDivisionLevelOf CWSTRUCTURE SECTION 2)...(#$subDivisionLevelOf PART CHAPTER 0)).") :- x_cid(a65b16505ed935).
