x_comment(x_grammaticalRoleWRTRelationMention,"(grammaticalRoleWRTRelationMention RM EM ROLE)  means that EM, an instance of #$EntityMentionHypothesis, fills the grammatical role ROLE wrt. the #$RelationMentionHypothesis RM.  So, for example, given a sentence like \"the cat is on the mat\", we can use (#$grammaticalRoleWRTRelationMention RM1 EM1 #$SubjectRoleMarker) to indicate that the #$EntityMentionHypothesis corresponding to this occurnace of \"the cat\"(EM1) fills the subject role in the #$RelationMentionHypothesis (RM1) associated with this sentence.") :- x_cid(a65b16505ed937).
