x_comment(x_Respect,"An instance of #$EmotionalQuantityType.  Each instance of #$Respect is some agent's feeling of just regard, consideration, or appreciation for the worth of someone or something.  Instances of #$Respect vary depending on the intensity of the feeling, the subject experiencing the feeling, or the object of the feeling.  Specializations of #$Respect include #$Awe, #$Reverence, and #$Admiration.") :- x_cid(a65b16505ed950).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505ed950,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16505ed950,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part07.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16505ed950,9084).
xc_kb_names(a65b16505ed950,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16505ed950,[]).
x_comment('x_CharacterToken-Sounded',"The collection of all sounded tokens of individual\n  abstract characters.  More precisely, #$CharacterToken-Sounded\n  is a specialization of #$CharacterToken each of \n  whose instances is a sound event that represents or \n  realizes a particular instance of #$Character-Abstract in \n  some language or writing system.  Instances can be directly \n  generated by a human voice, a parrot, a loudspeaker \n  (reproducing a ''live'' or recorded signal), or other \n  device, and include certain instances of #$SpokenUtterance-IBT \n  as well as some electronically-generated sounds.\n  Sounded characters are identified (both in theory and in\n  practice) as tokens of particular abstract characters\n  largely by their psychoacoustic contours, though context \n  and creator's intention also figure in.") :- x_cid(a65b16505ed951).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505ed951,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16505ed951,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part07.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16505ed951,9085).
xc_kb_names(a65b16505ed951,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16505ed951,[]).
x_comment(x_businessPartners,"The predicate #$businessPartners indicates that two agents have jointly undertaken some business project; they are combining resources in some way to further their interests.  (#$businessPartners AGENT1 AGENT2) means AGENT1 is in partnership with AGENT2 to engage in business activities.  The partners are instances of #$Agent-PartiallyTangible and may belong to either #$Person or #$Organization.  The partnership may be formally recognized (e.g., a #$Partnership or some other form of business) or informal.") :- x_cid(a65b16505ed952).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505ed952,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16505ed952,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part07.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16505ed952,9099).
xc_kb_names(a65b16505ed952,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16505ed952,[]).
x_comment(x_ProbabilityInterval,"A specialization of #$ContinuousIntervalOnNumberLine (q.v.).  This is the collection of all continuous numeric intervals (both real numbers and proper intervals on the real line) between 0 and 1 inclusive.  Each instance of #$ProbabilityInterval can be used as an argument to #$ProbabilityFn (q.v.) to represent the #$ProbabilityInterval (q.v.) that a sentence is true.") :- x_cid(a65b16505ed953).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505ed953,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16505ed953,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part07.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16505ed953,9100).
