x_comment(x_referenceInWorkTo,"(#$referenceInWorkTo WORK TEXT REFERENT) means that the #$StructurallySpecificWork WORK contains (see #$containsStructure-CW) #$TextString TEXT, which TEXT is a reference that points to REFERENT, an instance of #$IntelligentAgent or an instance of #$StructurallySpecificWork external to WORK.  Not any mention of a person or work is a reference.  The sentence 'Bill Clinton served two terms as the American president.' does not contain a reference in the sense of #$referenceInWorkTo.  #$referenceInWorkTo indicates that a #$TextString formally and purposefully points to some other work or person for the purpose of attribution, support, or location.  For #$TextStrings that refer to other #$TextStrings that are contained within the same #$StructurallySpecificWork, see #$crossReferenceInWorkTo.") :- x_cid(a65b16505ed962).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505ed962,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16505ed962,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part07.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16505ed962,9134).
xc_kb_names(a65b16505ed962,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16505ed962,[]).
x_comment(x_HasDisjunctiveBranching,"This is the collection of #$ScriptedEventTypes that contain\n\n(at least) three scenes BRANCHSCENE, SCENE1, SCENE2 ... where\n\n(#$startsAfterStartOfInSituationType SCENE1 BRANCHSCENE),\n\n(#$startsAfterStartOfInSituationType SCENE2 BRANCHSCENE) ..., where SCENE1, SCENE2 ...\n\nare temporally incomparable, and where any instantiation of the\n\n#$ScriptedEventType that instantiates BRANCHSCENE must instantiate exactly one of\n\nSCENE1, SCENE2 ....") :- x_cid(a65b16505ed963).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505ed963,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
