x_comment(x_agentTypeSufficientForTruthWRTRole,"(#$agentTypeSufficientForTruthWRTRole BINARY-ROLE-PRED AGENT-TYPE SENTENCE) holds just in case SENTENCE is a sentence that describes some state of affairs in which an agent plays some particular role, BINARY-ROLE-PRED, and that agent's being an instance of AGENT-TYPE is sufficient for the truth of SENTENCE.  For instance, a particular movie theater may charge only five dollars if the ticket purchaser is a member of a particular film club.  In that case, a sufficient condition on the truth of the statement that the purchase price of a ticket is five dollars is that the purchaser is a member of that film club.  In CycL we might represent an example of this as \n\n<code>\n <pre>\n(#$agentTypeSufficientForTruthWRTRole #$buyer (#$MemberFn AustinFilmClub)\n   (#$relationAllInstance #$purchasePrice \n     (#$SubcollectionOfWithRelationToFn  #$EntertainmentPerformanceTicket\n       #$publisherOfIBO #$AmcCourthousePlaza8-CinemaOrganization) \n     (#$Dollar-UnitedStates 5)))\n</pre>\n</code>\n\nWe read the above in English as \"the purchase price of tickets issued from Amc Courthouse Plaza8 Cinema is five dollars if the buyer is a member of the Austin film club\"\n\n.") :- x_cid(a65b16505ed96d).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505ed96d,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16505ed96d,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part07.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16505ed96d,9157).
xc_kb_names(a65b16505ed96d,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16505ed96d,[]).
x_comment(x_EquipmentTypeForOccupationTypeFn,"(#$EquipmentTypeForOccupationTypeFn PROFESSION-TYPE) denotes the collection of equipment types that are salient to elements of PROFESSION-TYPE conducting their job.  For example, 'spy equipment' may be referred to as (#$EquipmentTypeForOccupationTypeFn #$Spy).  A related term is #$EquipmentTypeForEventTypeFn.  For example 'intelligence gathering equipment' can be denoted by (#$EquipmentTypeForEventTypeFn #$IntelligenceGathering).") :- x_cid(a65b16505ed96e).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505ed96e,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
