x_comment(x_similarInValueOnRelation,"This predicate relates two things in terms of some BinaryPredicate that relates them to similar instances of a given collection of collections. (#$similarInValueOnRelation T1 T2 BINPRED) means that there are similar collections COL1 and COL2, such that (BINPRED T1 COL1) and (BINPRED T2 COL2).  The minimum notion of similarity is that COL1 and COL2 be instances of the same \"faceting\" sort of collection.  For instance, #$HighMountainousRegion and #$HillyRegion are both instances of the collection #$RegionTypeByHilliness.  Furthermore, if the collection type to which they belong is ordered (see #$CollectionWithAnEventLikeOrder), then COL1 and COL2 should be \"close\" together in the ordering.  For instance #$HillyRegion is closer to #$HighMountainousRegion than #$FlatRegion in the ordering on #$RegionTypeByHilliness.  So, it is likely that a region, REG1, such that (#$terrainType REG1 #$HighMountainousRegion) stands in #$similarInValueOnRelation via #$terrainType to a region, REG2, such that (#$terrainType REG2 #$HillyRegion).  But not likely that it stands in such a relation to an instance of #$FlatRegion.  See also #$resemblesInValue.") :- x_cid(a65b16505ed985).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505ed985,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16505ed985,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part07.krf').
