x_comment(x_keRelevantPrecisionValueForSlotOnType,"An instance of #$KEFacilitationPredicate used to constrain the pragmatic relevance of the values of certain properties for things of a given type. Specifically, (keRelevantPrecisionValueForSlotOnType BINPRED TYPE SIZE) indicates that we should regard an instance of TYPE as having a known value for the property expressed by the #$QuantitySlot BINPRED only when the instance of #$ScalarInterval that is its value has an #$intervalSize no greater than SIZE.\n<p>\nFor example, we would reasonably claim to <i>know</i> the age of a particular dog Fido if we can prove that (#$age Fido (#$YearsDuration 6)), but not if we could prove merely that (#$age Fido (YearsDuration 1 19)) -- which is most likely true, of course, since it is so of most dogs. But this is fact about (knowledge about) dogs or animals in general. So: (#$keRelevantPrecisionValueForSlotOnType #$age #$Animal (#$YearsDuration 1)) would express this constraint.") :- x_cid(a65b16505ed9aa).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505ed9aa,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16505ed9aa,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part07.krf').
