x_comment(x_TheVertexList,"#$TheVertexList is a function similar to #$TheList.  The salient differences between the two are that #$TheVertexList (i) returns a list of length at least three, (ii) returns a list of instances of #$Point, (iii) no three consecutive list members are #$collinearPoints, neither are the next to last member, last member, and first member #$collinearPoints, nor are the last member, first member, and second member #$collinearPoints.  These odd restrictions are needed since the result of #$TheVertexList is intended to correspond to the vertices of an instance of #$Polygon where the order of the list corresponds to the order of the vertices when the perimeter is traversed in a counter-clockwise direction.  The first restriction above is required since polygons have at least three sides, while the last condition reflects the convention that no three consecutive vertices are #$collinearPoints.") :- x_cid(a65b16505ed9b1).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505ed9b1,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
