x_comment(x_socialParticipants,"An #$ActorSlot (q.v.) and a specialization of #$actors with respect to social events. (#$socialParticipants SOCIAL-EVENT AGENT) means that the #$Agent-Generic AGENT participates --- in some social role --- in the #$SocialOccurrence SOCIAL-EVENT.  In every culture there is a wide variety of such relations of social participation, thus #$socialParticipants has many specializations. Some #$SocialOccurrences have very elaborate role structures (e.g. a lawsuit in 1990's America), and some are fairly simple (e.g. rudely bumping into someone). Some example specializations are #$bride, #$interviewee and #$tourParticipants.  Note that AGENT's participation in SOCIAL-EVENT need not be deliberate or intentional: one can sleep through a meeting and a newborn baby can attend a picnic.  For social participation that is expressly deliberate, see the specialization #$deliberateSocialParticipants.") :- x_cid(a65b16505ed9b9).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505ed9b9,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
