x_comment(x_followingOrEqualValueOnScale,"A generalization of #$followingValueOnScale (q.v.) that is used to compare the positions or \"ranks\" of quantities/attributes/properties that are on the same scale.  More precisely, <code>(#$followingOrEqualValueOnScale VALUE1 VALUE2 SCALE)</code> means that <code>VALUE1</code> and <code>VALUE2</code> are both instances of the #$CollectionWithAnEventLikeOrder (q.v.) <code>SCALE</code>, and that <code>VALUE2</code> is \"greater than or equal to\" (i.e. comes no earlier than) <code>VALUE1</code> in the ordering scheme conventionally associated with <code>SCALE</code>.\n<p>\nTypically, <code>VALUE1</code> and <code>VALUE2</code> will either (i) both be instances of #$Quantity (q.v.) or (ii) both be instances of #$FirstOrderCollection (q.v.) such that they correspond to properties of individuals.  In case (i), <code>SCALE</code> will be a #$TotallyOrderedQuantityType and, if <code>VALUE1</code> and <code>VALUE2</code> are not identical, <code>(#$followingValue VALUE1 VALUE2)</code> will also hold.\n<p>\nFor example, all of these hold:\n<p>\n<pre>\n  (#$followingOrEqualValueOnScale #$MildlyToxic #$MildlyToxic #$Toxicity)\n\n  (#$followingOrEqualValueOnScale\n    #$Corporal-Rank #$Sergeant-Rank #$USArmyRank) \n\n  (#$followingOrEqualValueOnScale \n    #$TwoDimensionalThing\n    #$PolyDimensionalThing\n    #$SpatialThingTypeByDimensionality)  .") :- x_cid(a65b16505ed9bd).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505ed9bd,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16505ed9bd,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part07.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16505ed9bd,9303).
