x_comment(x_eventTypesOverlapInEvent,"(#$eventTypesOverlapInEvent FIRST SECOND MAIN) means that during an instance, M-INS, of MAIN, any instance of SECOND that is a subevent (#$subEvents) of M-INS will start during some instance of FIRST which is a subevent of MAIN.  For instance, during hockey games, ice cleaning occurs during the intermission so we could assert (#$eventTypesOverlapInEvent Intermission IceCleaning #$PlayingOf-HockeyGame). Note that (#$eventTypesOverlapInEvent FIRST MAIN SECOND) does _not_ imply either that (i) each instance of MAIN has a subevent of type FIRST or of type SECOND, or, given an instance of MAIN, MAIN-INST, that does have a subevent of type FIRST, that (ii) it's having such a subevent entails it having a subevent of type SECOND. See also #$startsDuringInSituationType and #$startsDuringInScript-Ternary for application to scripts.") :- x_cid(a65b16505ed9c2).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505ed9c2,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
