x_comment(x_boundaryClusterOfSpaceRegion,"A quaternary #$SpaceRegionPredicate that relates a given space region (see #$HomogeneousExtendedSpaceRegion) to triples of #$Points that are clustered around its boundary.\n<p>\nMore precisely, <code>(#$boundaryClusterOfSpaceRegion INTERIOR-POINT BOUNDARY-POINT EXTERIOR-POINT REGION)</code> holds if and only if all of the following conditions are satisfied: (i) <code>INTERIOR-POINT</code> is in the interior of <code>REGION</code> (see #$incidentInInteriorOfSpaceRegion); (ii) <code>BOUNDARY-POINT</code> is in the boundary of <code>REGION</code> (see #$incidentInBoundaryOfSpaceRegion); (iii) <code>EXTERIOR-POINT</code> is in the exterior of <code>REGION</code> (see #$incidentInExteriorOfSpaceRegion); and (iv) both <code>INTERIOR-POINT</code> and <code>EXTERIOR-POINT</code> are arbitrarily close to <code>BOUNDARY-POINT</code> (see #$arbitrarilyClosePoints).") :- x_cid(a65b16505ed9c4).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505ed9c4,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16505ed9c4,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part07.krf').
