x_comment(x_quoteIn,"(#$quoteIn WORK TEXT) means that TEXT is an instance of #$TextString whose first and last characters are quotation marks and which is contained within (see #$containsStructure-CW) the #$StructurallySpecificWork WORK.   #$quoteIn is the least specific of the predicates which speak to the presence of something within quotation marks within a #$GraphicalStructure.  Use of this predicate simply indicates that there is a #$TextString enclosed within quotation marks; it does not imply any particular use of those quotations marks (e.g., the #$TextString within quotation marks could be the direct quote of an individual or work external to WORK, the quotation marks could indicate a foreign word or phrase, or the quotation marks could indicate the speech of a character within a #$FictionalPCW).  To indicate quotations of external agents or the speech of a character within a fictional work, use the more precise #$quotationOfExternalAgent or #$speechOfCharacter.") :- x_cid(a65b16505ed9c9).
