x_comment(x_goalRoleSlot,"#$goalRoleSlot is a simple but powerful means of\nrepresenting a desire to play a role in an instance of some kind of\n#$Situation.  This predicate relates a #$GoalSituation to a\n#$BinaryRolePredicate.  (#$goalSituationType GOAL-SITUATION\nDESIRED-SITUATION-TYPE) means that at least one #$Agent-PartiallyTangible (such agents\nare identified by #$goalAgent) has a goal, desire, want or need to\nplay a role (this role is identified by #$goalRoleSlot) in some\ninstance of DESIRED-SITUATION-TYPE.  For example (#$goalSituationType\n`GoalSituation001' #$TakingAShower) means that during\n`GoalSituation001' any #$goalAgent for `GoalSituation001' wants to\nplay some role in #$TakingAShower.  If (#$goalRoleSlot\n`GoalSituation002' #$performedBy) is also asserted, then this\nspecifies that any #$goalAgent for `GoalSituation001' wishes to play\nthe role of #$performedBy in some element of #$TakingAShower.  In\nother words, \"someone wishes to take a shower\".  If one wishes to\nassert that \"Fred wishes to take a shower.\" then one would add the\nassertion (#$goalAgent `GoalSituation002' `Fred').  Compared with\n#$goalSituationSuccessIf, this predicate has limitations in terms of\nexpressivity.  However, it has more inferencing power.  See (VersusFn\n(TheSet goalSituationType goalRoleSlot) goalSituationSuccessIf) for more\non the expressivity/tradeoff tradeoff issue.") :- x_cid(a65b16505ed9d0).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505ed9d0,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
