x_comment('x_grossDomesticProduct-Nominal',"(#$grossDomesticProduct-Nominal GE THING MONEY) means that the instance of #$MonetaryValue MONEY is a measure of the value of the #$GeopoliticalEntity GE's total domestic production of goods and services (its gross domestic product) during the temporal extent of the #$TemporalThing THING, and that the value of the currency (#$UnitOfMoney) in terms of which MONEY is specified is that which prevailed during the temporal extent of THING.  A country would be a typical instance of GE.  THING will often be a time period -- for example, a calendar year such as (#$YearFn 1997) or a calendar quarter such as (#$QuarterFn 4 (#$YearFn 1997)); but it may also be, for instance, a particular #$Event.  For example, (#$grossDomesticProduct-Nominal COUNTRY (#$YearFn 1997) (#$Dollar-UnitedStates NR)) means that COUNTRY's gross domestic product for 1997 was $NR in 1997 US dollars.  See also #$grossDomesticProduct.") :- x_cid(a65b16505ed9d8).
