x_comment(x_TemporalPredicate,"A specialization of #$ObjectPredicate (q.v.).  Each instance of #$TemporalPredicate is used either to say something about the relative positions of two or more temporal things in time, to ascribe a temporal property to something, or to compare time-quantities.  As such, each temporal predicate has at least one (and often two or more) of its argument-places constrained (by #$argIsa) either to take instances of #$TemporalThing or to take instances of #$Time-Quantity.\n<p>\nAn important specialization of #$TemporalPredicate is #$BinaryTemporalRelationPredicate (q.v.).  Examples of temporal predicates that are not in that specialization include #$startsDurationAfterEndingOf, #$temporallyContinuousDuring, #$longerDurationThan, and #$holdsIn.") :- x_cid(a65b16505ed9ea).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505ed9ea,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
