x_comment(x_predicateTypeSummaryForThing,"An instance of #$SummaryPredicate useful for summarizing knowledge about THING with respect to #$PredicateTypes. (#$predicateTypeSummaryForThing PRED-TYPE THING SENTENCE) means that #$CycLSentence-Assertible SENTENCE has PRED (an instance of PRED-TYPE) in its arg0 slot and it has the term THING in some slot other than arg0.  For example, (#$predicateTypeSummaryForThing #$LikesPredicate #$JenniferSullivan  (#$likesAsFriend #$JenniferSullivan #$Cynthia)) is true, and means that some instance of #$LikesPredicate occurs as the arg0 in (#$likesAsFriend #$JenniferSullivan #$Cynthia), and that #$JenniferSullivan also occurs in (#$likesAsFriend #$JenniferSullivan #$Cynthia).  This predicate is particularly useful for asking queries with the first and second argument slots bound and the third slot open.  For example, asking (#$predicateTypeSummaryForThing OrganismRequirementsPredicate (#$AdultFn #$Dachshund) ?SENTENCE) will mean the system will find any assertions whose arg0 is an instance of OrganismRequirementsPredicate that also contain the term (#$AdultFn #$Dachshund). Cf. #$predicateTypeSummaryForThing-Set.") :- x_cid(a65b16505ed9ec).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505ed9ec,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
