x_comment(x_calendarDayOfDate,"(#$calendarDayOfDate CALENDAR-DAY DATE) means that CALENDAR-DAY is the day of DATE. For example, (#$calendarDayOfDate (#$DayFn 14 (#$MonthFn #$June (#$YearFn 1972))) (#$SecondFn 54 (#$MinuteFn 48 (#$HourFn 10 (#$DayFn 14 (#$MonthFn #$June (#$YearFn 1972))))))) means that (#$DayFn 14 (#$MonthFn #$June (#$YearFn 1972))) is the day of the date (#$SecondFn 54 (#$MinuteFn 48 (#$HourFn 10 (#$DayFn 14 (#$MonthFn #$June (#$YearFn 1972)))))). Cf. #$dayNumberOfDate.") :- x_cid(a65b16505eda19).
