x_comment('x_GeographicalPlace-OneByOneQuadrangle',"A subcollection of\n\n#$GeographicalPlace-2D. Instances of #$GeographicalPlace-OneByOneQuadrangle are \n\none degree of latitude high by one degree of longitude wide portions of \n\nthe geographical surface of reference. They can be used to indicate partial \n\ngeographical location of two or three dimensional things within the context \n\nof a geography. See #$genericallyLocatedAt-SurfaceGeographical. They can also be \n\nused to specify the exact extent of an object when specifying an area of \n\ninterest of a particular context (using #$exactlyLocatedAt-Spatial, \n\n#$mtSpatialUniverse-2D).") :- x_cid(a65b16505eda1a).
