x_comment(x_FiniteSpatialThing,"A specialization of #$SpatialThing.  Each instance of #$FiniteSpatialThing is a spatial thing that measures a finite #$Distance in all of its dimensions (see #$extensionParametersOfObject).  A finite line (see #$LinearObject-Finite) has finite length; an finite surface has a finite length and finite \"width\"; and an finite three-dimensional spatial thing has finite length, finite \"width\", and finite \"height\".\n<p>\nA finite spatial thing might be tangible or intangible.  Cf. #$InfiniteSpatialThing.") :- x_cid(a65b16505eda38).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505eda38,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
