x_comment(x_monumentHonors,"A binary predicate which relates instances of #$MemorialMarker to instances of #$Agent-PartiallyTangible (note that each such instance may be an individual or a group). (#$monumentHonors MONUMENT HONOREE(S)) means that MONUMENT is a #$MemorialMarker constructed to honor or commemorate HONOREE(S), and to cause people who perceive MONUMENT to remember and respect HONOREE(S). As an instance of #$Agent-PartiallyTangible, HONOREE(S) must not be an event or a physical object. (For honoring these, see the more general #$artifactHonors).  Usually, but not always, the MONUMENT is built by someone other than HONOREE(S) (but some people build monuments to themselves).  If HONOREE(S) is living when MONUMENT is built, HONOREE(S) may be present at an #$Event of announcing, inaugurating or unveiling the MONUMENT; see #$eventHonors.") :- x_cid(a65b16505eda42).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505eda42,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16505eda42,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part07.krf').
