x_comment(x_ProtestantPerson,"The collection of people who adhere to a faith in\n\n#$ProtestantReligion. The basic tenet of Protestantism is the non-mandatory\n\nrole of the #$Priest as an intercessionary between a believer and #$GodOfAbrahamIsaacAndJacob,\n\nor between a believer and the proper interpretation of the holy texts (such as\n\nthe #$Bible). As a divergence from #$Catholicism, Protestants generally believe in\n\na school of Christianity that differs in some key\n\nrespects. Among the chief differences are: #$CatholicPerson shows more devotion\n\nto #$Mary-MotherOfJesus, and has a belief in\n\n#$Transubstantiation -- the process whereby bread is turned into the body of \n\n#$JesusChrist). Some subclasses of #$ProtestantPerson view the latter as being\n\nof symbolic import only (e.g., #$AnglicanReligion), while followers of the #$LutheranReligion\n\nschool believe in #$Transubstantiation as a transformation, but deny the\n\nnecessary role of the #$Priest as an agent of this transformation.") :- x_cid(a65b16505eda47).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505eda47,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
