x_comment(x_IndustryType,"A collection of collections.  Each instance of #$IndustryType is a general industry, by function, which is the collection of all local or geographically-defined industries (instances of #$Industry-Localized) that perform that function.  So the funeral industry in general is an instance of #$IndustryType, whereas the Ohio funeral industry is an instance of #$Industry-Localized (as is the worldwide funeral industry whose 'locale' is just large).  Every instance of #$IndustryType can have local examples of #$Industry-Localized as its instances.  See also #$ProductionIndustryTypeFn, #$IndustryOfRegionFn, and #$MtOfIndustryTypeFn.") :- x_cid(a65b16505eda61).
