x_comment(x_amountForGenValueColAndPred,"(#$amountForGenValueColAndPred VALUE PRED COL GVP) means that\nVALUE is the amount which is in the range of the quantity expressed by the \nNART '(#$RelativeGenericValueFn PRED COL GVP)'.  Consider this example, Assertion A: (#$amountForGenValueColAndPred (#$Foot-UnitOfMeasure 6.5) #$heightOfObject #$BasketballPlayer #$highAmountOf).  This means that 6.5 feet is subsumed by (GenValueFn #$heightOfObject #$BasketballPlayer #$highAmountOf).  The NART itself is the quantity of height that is had by basketball players we consider \"tall\".  So, such an assertion entails that 6.5 feet is tall for a basketball player.  In other words, 6.5 is a high value on the slot #$heightOfObject for any #$BasketballPlayer.") :- x_cid(a65b16505eda62).
