x_comment(x_similarWRTPartType,"This predicate relates pairs of things to the kinds of physical parts they have in common and which are instantiated similarly in each.  (#$similarWRTPartType THING1 THING2 PART-TYPE) means that THING1 and THING2 both have parts that are instances of PART-TYPE and these parts are similar to each other.  For instance, (#$similarWRTPartType MUSCLE-CAR1 MUSCLE-CAR2 #$GasolineEngine) means that MUSCLE-CAR1 and MUSCLE-CAR2 both have instances of #$GasolineEngine as parts and these engines are similar to each other.  Obviously, judgements of similarity are going to be highly context dependent.  To relate things in terms of attributes that they share, see #$resemblesInQuantity and #$identicalInQuantity.  To discuss part similarity at a type level, see #$typesSimilarWRTPartType.") :- x_cid(a65b16505eda8c).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505eda8c,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
