x_comment(x_relationExistsAllMany,"A ternary #$RuleMacroPredicate (q.v.)that can be used to state that a given binary predicate stands in a certain relationship with two collections.  (#$relationExistsAllMany BINPRED COL1 COL2) means that for every instance INST of COL2, there are many (see #$Many-Quant) instances INST(i) of COL1 such that (BINPRED INST(i) INST).  It is equivalent to (and can thus be used in effect as shorthand for) the more complex form:\n<p>\n(#$implies\n(#$isa ?INST COL2)\n(#$thereExistRange #$Many-Quant ?INST-I\n(#$and\n(#$isa ?INST COL1)\n(BINPRED ?INST-I ?INST)))) .\n<p>\nFor example, `(#$relationExistsAllMany #$soldAt #$PostageStamp #$PostOfficeOrganization)' means many postage stamps are sold at each post office.  Cf. #$relationAllExistsMany, and see #$NoteAboutUseOfRuleMacroPredicates.") :- x_cid(a65b16505eda92).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505eda92,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
