x_comment('x_num-GenQuantRelnTo',"An instance of #$GeneralizedQuantifierRelation (q.v.). (#$num-GenQuantRelnTo RELN COL THING NUM) is true if for exactly NUM instances X of COL (RELN X THING) holds.  For example, \n\n (#$num-GenQuantRelnTo #$objectFoundInLocation #$Pizzeria  #$CityOfAustinTX 5) means that there are exactly five pizzerias in Austin, Tex.  The second argument place of this predicate is constrained to instances of #$SetOrCollection -- the more specific #$relationExistsCountInstance (the second argument place of which is constrained to instances of #$Collection) should be used instead of #$num-GenQuantRelnTo whenever possible.") :- x_cid(a65b16505eda9e).
