x_comment('x_instrument-Generic',"The predicate #$instrument-Generic is used to link a particular event to any of the objects which play an instrumental role in it.  <code>(#$instrument-Generic EVENT OBJECT)</code> means that the instance of #$PartiallyTangible <code>OBJECT</code> plays an intermediate causal role in the #$Event <code>EVENT</code>, facilitating the occurrence of <code>EVENT</code>, and thereby serving some purpose of some #$Agent-PartiallyTangible.  This can happen in at least two ways: either the 'doer' of <code>EVENT</code> acts on <code>OBJECT</code>, which in turn acts on something else (as when someone uses a hammer to pound in a nail) or the 'doer' of <code>EVENT</code> acts on something, making it possible for <code>OBJECT</code> to act on that thing (as when someone puts wet clothes out in the sun to dry).  Typically, an #$instrument-Generic is not significantly altered by playing that role in an event.  #$deviceUsed is an important specialization of #$instrument-Generic (where <code>OBJECT</code> is an instance of #$PhysicalDevice).") :- x_cid(a65b16505edaad).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505edaad,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
