x_comment('x_InformationDesignation-MissionCritical',"An instance of #$AttributeValue.  #$InformationDesignation-MissionCritical\ncan be used to designate when an instance of #$AspatialInformationStore\nis critical to the success of some mission.  This attribute is most useful\nfor specifying what information is critical to a given mission within\nthe mission context, i.e. the instance of #$Microtheory representing\nthe mission.  For example, if MISSION_MT is an instance of #$Microtheory\nrepresenting some military mission, say, and INFO is some instance of\n#$AspatialInformationStore critical to the success of MISSION_MT, say\nthe precise location of a command ship, then one could represent this\nby asserting, in MISSION_MT, (#$designationOfInformation INFO\n#$InformationDesignation-MissionCritical).  This attribute is also useful\nin rules when one wants to use a clause stating that some instance of\n#$AspatialInformationStore is critical\nto some mission without specifying the mission.  See also the predicates\n#$designationOfInformation and #$missionCriticalInformation.") :- x_cid(a65b16505edab2).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505edab2,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
