x_comment(x_StoutBeer,"A black form of #$Beer (contrast with #$LagerBeer and #$AleBeer) that originated in the British Isles, and is now most recognizably associated with #$IrishRepublic. #$StoutBeer contains a bitterness derived from malted hops, good #$StoutBeer is served chilled, several degrees below room temperature. #$StoutBeers are typically black colored, containing a mixture of #$CarbonDioxide and #$Nitrogen. #$StoutBeers typically possess a distinctively white, creamy froth or 'head'. Even the most ardent #$StoutBeer drinkers find stout to be too heavy for summer consumption, and switch to #$LagerBeer or #$AleBeer in the summer months.") :- x_cid(a65b16505edafb).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505edafb,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16505edafb,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part07.krf').
