x_comment('x_disconnects-Underspecified',"(#$disconnects-Underspecified LEFT RIGHT) states that a\n\ndisconnection or separation of an underspecified nature is made\n\nbetween the ideas/things LEFT and RIGHT.  A disconnection might be\n\ngeographical (e.g., if LEFT is a person and RIGHT is a place, as in\n\n'Bill left town'), physical (e.g., LEFT and RIGHT are people who\n\n'become distant' or divorce), mental (e.g., LEFT is a person and\n\nRIGHT is an abstract state, as in 'IBM came out of its slump') or\n\npartially tangible (e.g., LEFT is a person, RIGHT is a coma, as in\n\n'Bill came out of his coma'). Conceptual disconnection is the mirror\n\noperation of #$connects-Underspecified.") :- x_cid(a65b16505edafd).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505edafd,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16505edafd,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part07.krf').
