x_comment(x_ListOfVertices,"A specialization of #$List. Each instance of #$ListOfVertices is a list of #$Points whose length is at least three, and which contains no three consecutive (including rotationally-consecutive) members that are #$collinearPoints.  (Note that there are two \"rotationally-consecutive\" triples in such a list: (i) the sublist consisting of the second-to-last, last, and first members of the list and (ii) the sublist consisting of the last, first, and second members of the list.)\n<p>\nEach #$ListOfVertices <code>POINTLIST</code> of length <code>N</code> is a list of the vertices of some (actually, many) two-dimensional geometrical figure(s) whose boundary is the closed #$LineString that \"connects-the-dots\" between the consecutive points in <code>POINTLIST</code>.  If all the points in <code>POINTLIST</code> happen to lie in the same #$Plane (see #$coplanarPoints) and the closed line-string they define is geometrically simple (see #$LocallyEuclideanSpatialThing), then <code>POINTLIST</code> is a list of the vertices of a unique <code>N</code>-sided #$Polygon.") :- x_cid(a65b16505edb05).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505edb05,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16505edb05,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part07.krf').
