x_comment(x_DestructivePotential,"#$DestructivePotential is a collection of attributes representing\n\nscalar indices of the destructive potential of an #$Event or a\n\n#$SomethingExisting.  The thing whose destructive potential is being\n\ngauged may be a particular weather event, like a tornado or a\n\nhurricane, or a situation, like an international arms build-up.  It\n\nmay be also be a weapon.  In any case, #$DestructivePotential is\n\nmeasured primarily by looking at the #$DegreeOfDamage caused by a\n\ntypical instance or typical use of the thing whose\n\n#$DestructivePotential is being specified, or by that thing's 'generic' use of other instrumentalities. Note that it makes sense in certain context to cite the #$DestructivePotential of an #$Agent-PartiallyTangible, such as a #$Country.") :- x_cid(a65b16505edb1b).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505edb1b,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16505edb1b,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part07.krf').
