x_comment(x_timeSpan,"A #$TemporalPredicate and #$MeasurableQuantitySlot (qq.v.) that relates a temporal thing to the total elapsed time (see #$Time-Quantity) from its start to its end.  (#$timeSpan TEMPTHING TIME) means that TIME is the total elapsed time from when TEMPTHING started to exist (if a #$SomethingExisting) or happen (if an #$Event) or obtain (if a #$StaticSituation) to when TEMPTHING ceased to exist or ended.\n<p>\nNote that if TEMPTHING is #$temporallyContinuousDuring, its #$timeSpan is the same as its #$duration (q.v.): the length of time during which it actually existed or happened or obtained.  But if TEMPTHING is discontinuous, its time-span is strictly greater than its duration.  For example, the playing of the 2004 Super Bowl game has a time-span of several hours, but a duration of just one hour.") :- x_cid(a65b16505edb32).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505edb32,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16505edb32,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part07.krf').
