x_comment(x_surfaceFeatureOfObject,"(#$surfaceFeatureOfObject OBJ ATT) means that the 'salient' surface of OBJ has the attribute ATT.  Which surface is 'salient' is a function of context in the broad sense of the term context.  If OBJ is a 'one-sided' object (see #$OneSidedVsTwoSidedObjectNote) such as a cave or room in a building (see #$Cavity) then the salient surface is the inside surface of OBJ.  For elements of #$ConvexTangibleObject, the outside surface is salient.  Thus, we can assert that, e.g., (#$surfaceFeatureOfObject Cavity001 #$Concave).  Thus,  'Joe is wet' and 'The cave is wet', are easily translated into (#$surfaceFeatureOfObject Joe #$Wet) or (#$surfaceFeatureOfObject Cave001 #$Wet).") :- x_cid(a65b16505edb38).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505edb38,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16505edb38,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part07.krf').
