xc_kb_names(a65b16505edb38,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16505edb38,[]).
x_comment(x_CollapsibleDevice,"A specialization of #$Collapsible and a #$MechanicalDevice (qq.v.).  Each instance of #$CollapsibleDevice is a device that is designed so that its shape (i.e., configuration of its parts) can be changed by collapsing (and uncollapsing) it.  This is a secondary function of some devices so that they can take up less space when they aren't being used for their #$primaryFunction.  (So #$CollapsibleDevices are typically devices that either aren't used often and/or must be kept or carried in a small space.)  Most #$CollapsibleDevices are collapsed in their storage (or unused) state and unfolded during use; e.g., instances of #$SofaBed, #$FoldingChair, and #$FoldingTable, also, #$Eyeglasses and most elements of #$Tent.  \n<p>\nNote: A marginal case, one which is better left outside this collection, is a collapsable front/rear of a car.  While it is a device, and collapsable, most of the things one would wish to state about a typical #$CollapsibleDevice would not be true for the crushable car end.") :- x_cid(a65b16505edb39).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505edb39,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
