x_comment(x_typeFunctionCapable,"(#$typeFunctionCapable TYPE SYSTEMTYPE ROLE) means that\nunder normal background conditions, a normal instance of TYPE can play\nthe functional role (see #$SystemRolePredicate) ROLE with respect to the class\nof #$FunctionalSystem SYSTEMTYPE.  This means, specifically, that for\nsome large and nontrivial set of instances of SYSTEMTYPE, it would be\nunsurprising if Cyc learned that an instance of TYPE played the role\nROLE with respect to any of those instances.  (#$typeFunctionCapable\nTYPE SYSTEMTYPE ROLE) does *not* mean that every instance of TYPE can\nplay the role ROLE in every instance of SYSTEMTYPE: e.g., a particular\ninstance of TYPE could not play ROLE in an instance of SYSTEMTYPE that\nceased to exist before the instance of TYPE had come into being.") :- x_cid(a65b16505edb51).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505edb51,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
