xc_mapping_rows(a65b16505edb55,[]).
x_comment(x_pathogenTypicallyAcquiredBy,"(#$pathogenTypicallyAcquiredBy PATHOTYPE ORGTYPE ACTIONTYPE) means, colloquially, that instances of ORGTYPE commonly acquire instances of PATHOTYPE, along with an associated infection, by performing instances of ACTIONTYPE.   More precisely, it means that if ORG is an instance of ORGTYPE, and (#$susceptibleToDiseaseCausedBy ORGTYPE PATHOTYPE), and ORG is the #$nonDeliberateActors in an instance of ACTIONTYPE, the likelihood that there will exist an infection caused by this action, in which the #$infectingOrganismMob is a mob of instances of PATHOTYPE and of which ORG is the #$infectionHost, is #$highAmountOf.") :- x_cid(a65b16505edb56).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505edb56,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
