x_comment(x_Pseudomonadaceae,"A collection of #$Bacterium in the #$MoneraKingdom.  It includes the #$BiologicalGenus #$Pseudomonas, and other #$BiologicalGenus: Xanthomonas, Frateuria, and Zoogloea.  #$Pseudomonas includes many #$BiologicalSpecies that are human pathogens. These #$ProkaryoticCells are #$Bacterium-MotileByFlagellum by means of one or several polar flagella.  Although these are #$AerobicBacterium with a strictly respiratory type of metabolism with oxygen as the terminal electron acceptor, they may accept nitrate as an alternate electron receptor.  This allows for some growth to occur anaerobically.  This #$BiologicalFamily contains both oxidase-positive or -negative cells, but they are all chemoorganotrophs and catalase-positive.  Some #$BiologicalSpecies are facultative chemolithotrophs.") :- x_cid(a65b16505edb84).
