x_comment('x_grossNationalProduct-Old',"The Gross National Product (GNP) of a nation is the total income of all its citizens and resident corporations, whether obtained from domestic or foreign commercial activities.  The second argument to #$grossNationalProduct-Old is a #$MonetaryRate, usually given in #$BillionDollarsPerYear.  Note:  A nation's #$grossNationalProduct-Old (GDP) is usually considered a better indicator of economic health than its GNP.") :- x_cid(a65b16505edba0).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505edba0,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
