x_comment(x_directionsOfPath,"This predicate can be used to state which directions a\n(non-directed) spatial path such as a two-way street runs in.  \n(#$directionsOfPath PATH DIR1 DIR2) means that PATH runs in a \nrelatively straight line from DIR1 to DIR2 (and vice versa, of \ncourse).  DIR1 and DIR2 must be roughly opposite directions \n(see #$oppositeDirection-Interval).  If PATH is not relatively\nstraight (see #$CenterLineOfPathFn and #$LinearObject-Straight), or\nis an instance of #$DirectedCustomaryPath, the above statement \nwill be false or malformed; so #$directionsOfPath should not \napplied to such paths.") :- x_cid(a65b16505edba9).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505edba9,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
