x_comment(x_hasMembers,"The predicate #$hasMembers relates a particular organization to the agents who are members of that organization.  This predicate indicates `generic' membership, although there may be specialized kinds of membership in the same organization.  (#$hasMembers ORG AGENT) means that AGENT is a member of the #$Organization ORG; typically, membership eligibility is determined by ORG and accepted with AGENT's voluntary affiliation.  In general, a member may be any #$Agent-PartiallyTangible, including other #$Organizations (such as member countries in the United Nations), although only instances of #$Person can be members of instances of #$OrganizationOfPeopleOnly.  The truth of an assertion made with #$hasMembers may be time-dependent and, if so, should be qualified appropriately.  For example, (#$holdsIn (#$YearFn 1975) (#$hasMembers #$UnitedNationsOrganization #$Taiwan-RepublicOfChina)) is true, but (#$holdsIn (#$YearFn 1995) (#$hasMembers #$UnitedNationsOrganization #$Taiwan-RepublicOfChina)) is not.") :- x_cid(a65b16505edbaf).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505edbaf,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16505edbaf,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part07.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16505edbaf,10370).
xc_kb_names(a65b16505edbaf,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16505edbaf,[]).
x_comment(x_QueryMacroPredicate,"The collection of predicates that are shorthand for a complicated removal query.  For instance, #$performsActsOfType-Percentage relates an agent to two collections of acts and a number, NUM, just in case the ratio of the instances of the first collection performed by the agent that are also instances of the second collection is NUM.  The actual CycL for this query is rather complicated and requires two uses of #$extentCardinality and #$TheSetOf.  #$performsActsOfType-Percentage abstracts the important replacable terms from that query as argument places in the predicate allowing the query to be easily modifiable.  Each instance of this collection has one or more rules that define the query.  Such rules may or may not be supported in code.") :- x_cid(a65b16505edbb0).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505edbb0,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
