x_comment(x_importRateThrough,"(#$importRateThrough REGION PRODUCT-TYPE PT RATE) means that the #$GeographicalRegion REGION imports instances of the #$ProductType PRODUCT-TYPE through the instance of #$PartiallyTangible PT (on their way from their origin) at the #$Rate RATE.  PT might, in the case of oil imports, for example, be a #$GeographicalRegion or a #$Pipeline.  Note that since things imported are typically measurable in terms of their monetary value, RATE might in some instances be a #$MonetaryRate; in others it will be, for example, a rate of volume, mass, or number.") :- x_cid(a65b16505edbc5).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505edbc5,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
