x_comment(x_usedOneAtATime,"(#$usedOneAtATime EVENT HEAP) means that in the event EVENT, the things belonging to HEAP are used one at a time. Plausibly, in most uses of this term the event argument will actually be filled by an iterative event, ie., one that is composed of many single subevents of the same type (cf. #$IterativeEventType). The main difference between this predicate and #$iterativeStep: arg2 of #$usedOneAtATime is #$PartiallyTangible (hence we use #$Group), #$iterativeStep can take as its arg2 a wider variety of #$IterationEventByTypes.") :- x_cid(a65b16505edbc6).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505edbc6,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
