x_comment('x_causes-ThingProp',"(#$causes-ThingProp THING PROP) means that THING causes the proposition PROP to become true.  THING may be an #$Agent-PartiallyTangible, a #$Situation, or  a #$ELSentence-Assertible.  This is a very general predicate.  It is almost always better to use a more specialized predicate such as #$causes-PropProp, #$causes-EventEvent, or #$causes-SitProp, particularly in rules.  Nonetheless, #$causes-ThingProp can be useful if one wishes to collect all the possible causes of some proposition be they #$Situations, #$Agent-PartiallyTangibles, other propositions (see #$ELSentence-Assertible).  See #$NoteAboutCausationPredicates for a map of related predicates.") :- x_cid(a65b16505edbcf).
