x_comment('x_Number-General',"A specialization of #$NumericInterval and #$ScalarPointValue (qq.v.).  This is the most general collection of numbers.   Each instance of #$Number-General is a number in some sense of the word, i.e. an element of some mathematical structure with at least reasonably conventional notions of arithmetic and ordering.  Canonical examples include integers, rational numbers, and real numbers.  Some specializations of #$Number-General are #$RealNumber, #$ComplexNumber, #$PrimeNumber, and #$ProbabilityInterval.") :- x_cid(a65b16505edbd0).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505edbd0,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
