xc_mapping_rows(a65b16505edbe9,[]).
x_comment(x_nucleotidesBasePaired,"(#$nucleotidesBasePaired NUCL1 NUCL2) means that there is a hydrogen bond between the nitrogen bases that are the respective components of #$Nucleotides NUCL1 and NUCL2. Normally, only complementary nitrogen bases are base paired (see #$complementaryBaseTypes), but it is possible for two #$NitrogenBases to be base-paired incorrectly, e.g., a hydrogen bond can be formed between two #$NitrogenBases that are not complementary. In  such a case, the #$Nucleotides of which these bases are components are incorrectly base-paired. Use #$basesComplementaryBasePaired and #$nucleotidesComplementaryBasePaired for the relations when the bases are paired correctly.") :- x_cid(a65b16505edbea).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505edbea,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
