x_comment(x_actsInCapacity,"The predicate #$actsInCapacity indicates the capacity in which an agent participates in certain kinds of actions.  (#$actsInCapacity AGENT ROLE SCRIPT-TYPE CAP) means that the agent AGENT plays the role ROLE in instances of SCRIPT-TYPE, and s/he does that role in the capacity CAP.  CAP is a #$CapacityPredicate (q.v.) which describes the AGENT's mode of participation--e.g., as a job, hobby, main function, support function, etc.  Contrast three cases of acts of #$GreetingSomeone, when #$performedBy: (1) instances of #$Receptionist, in their #$actsInCapacity-JobCapacity and as their #$actsInCapacity-MainFunction; (2) instances of #$FlightAttendant, in their #$actsInCapacity-JobCapacity but as a #$SupportFunction; and (3) instances of #$TrainEngineer, in a #$actsInCapacity-HobbyCapacity (though they do it while working, it's not part of their job).") :- x_cid(a65b16505edc0d).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505edc0d,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16505edc0d,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part07.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16505edc0d,10583).
xc_kb_names(a65b16505edc0d,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16505edc0d,[]).
x_comment(x_InfiniteSpatialThing,"A specialization of #$PositiveDimensionalThing.  Each instance of #$InfiniteSpatialThing is a spatial thing that measures an infinite #$Distance (see #$InfiniteScalarInterval) in at least one dimension (see #$extensionParametersOfObject).  An infinite line (see #$LinearObject-Infinite) has an infinite length; an infinite surface has infinite length and/or infinite \"width\"; and an infinite three-dimensional spatial thing has infinite length, infinite \"width\", and/or infinite \"height\".\n<p>\nAn infinite spatial thing might be intangible or (at least in theory) tangible.\nCf. #$FiniteSpatialThing.") :- x_cid(a65b16505edc0e).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505edc0e,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16505edc0e,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part07.krf').
