x_comment(x_correctlyParsedSentence,"(#$correctlyParsedSentence SENTENCE) means that a reviewer who looked at the #$CycLPropositionalSentence SENTENCE felt that the information content of the sentence has been correctly parsed from a text source, given the system's current knowledge.  This is not to say that the content of SENTENCE is *correct* or *true* - for example, (#$isa #$Cynthia #$Married) is correctly parsed from 'Cyndy is married.', but incorrect.  This distinction depends on the context within which the judgement is being made, and is necessarily subjective.  See also #$incorrectlyParsedSentence.") :- x_cid(a65b16505edc35).
