x_comment(x_keRelevantPreds,"A #$KEFacilitationPredicate (q.v.) that is (along with #$keRelevantInverse) the most general of those that relate a collection to a binary predicate.  (#$keRelevantPreds COL BINPRED) means that for any reified instance INST of COL, if there is anything THING such that BINPRED holds between THING and INST, asserting (BINPRED INST THING) in the Cyc Knowledge Base is worth considering and perhaps advisable.  But note: the specializations of #$keRelevantPreds are #$keWeakSuggestionPreds, #$keStrongSuggestionPreds, #$keConsiderationPreds, and #$keStrongConsiderationPreds (qq.v.); and one should use one of these instead of #$keRelevantPreds itself whenever possible.  In fact, #$keRelevantPreds was created mainly for use in situations where one wants to say something general about all of these specializations.") :- x_cid(a65b16505edd00).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505edd00,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
