x_comment(x_queryNeedsThingBoundInPosition,"(#$queryNeedsThingBoundInPosition QUERY THING ARG-POS) means that before QUERY can be run by the inference engine, THING should be substituted for the free variable at ARG-POS in the query sentence.  That is to say, QUERY has a free variable at ARG-POS but the inference engine should never see that variable -- it is supposed to be replaced by THING in application code before being run.  This is useful when an application needs to run a query to find some value, but the query has parameters that need to come from user input or an SKS at runtime (in this case it is probably true that (#$quotedIsa THING #$IndexicalConcept)).") :- x_cid(a65b16505edd6e).
