x_comment(x_NotablyFn,"<code>(#$NotablyFn BIN-PRED)</code> denotes a specialization of <code>BIN-PRED</code>, with the following property:  <code>((#$NotablyFn BIN-PRED) ARG1 ARG2)</code> holds if and only if <code>(BIN-PRED ARG1 ARG2)</code> holds and it is notable that <code>(BIN-PRED ARG1 ARG2)</code> holds.   In other words, if <code>BIN-PRED</code> is a binary relation then <code>(#$NotablyFn BIN-PRED)</code> is the extent of that relation where the relation holds notably. In some cases, this corresponds to the notion of a <i>key</i> relationship. For example (#$suppliers  #$StarbucksCorporation #$Cycorp) holds, but ((#$NotablyFn #$suppliers) #$StarbucksCorporation #$Cycorp) does not. Similarly, ((#$NotablyFn #$makesProductType) #$StarbucksCorporation #$Coffee-Beverage) holds.") :- x_cid(a65b16505eddb7).
