x_comment('x_TripleStoreKS-Generic',"A generic triple store representation.  In this example #$rdf-type is supported.  To hook this up to an actual SPARQL endpoing, edit the following assertions to specify the server address and relative access point and register the source using the SKSManager in the Tools section of the browser\n\n<pre>\n \nIn Mt : (MappingMtFn TripleStoreKS-Generic)\n(serverOfSKS TripleStoreKS-Generic \"servername.domain.top-level-domain\")\n\nIn Mt : (MappingMtFn TripleStoreKS-Generic)\n(relativePathForAPIAccessToSKS TripleStoreKS-Generic \"path/sparql\")\n\nIn Mt : (MappingMtFn TripleStoreKS-Generic)\n(portNumberForSKS TripleStoreKS-Generic 80)\n\nNormally the port will be 80.\n\nAdd mappings to existing Cyc terms via assertions like these:\n\nIn Mt : (MappingMtFn TripleStoreKS-Generic)\n(codeMapping\n       (ReifiedMappingForPredFn rdf-type GenericOWLOntology) \"URI-STRING\" CYCL-TERM)\n\nOr use SchemaObjectFn to wrap URIs you wish to use in your queries,\n\n    (SchemaObjectFn\n   (ReifiedMappingForPredFn rdf-type GenericOWLOntology)\"<URI-STRING>\")\n\n\n</pre>") :- x_cid(a65b16505edeb2).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505edeb2,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
