x_comment('x_ElephantTrunkProcedure-Entire',"The collection of all end-to-end #$ElephantTrunkProcedure aortic replacement surgeries subsuming an instance of ElephantTrunkAortaReplacementStage1-SurgicalProcedure and an instance of #$ElephantTrunkAortaReplacementStage2 as subsituations, in that order.  In an #$ElephantTrunkProcedure-Entire, a surgical incision is first used to replace the aortic valve, the ascending aorta, and the aortic arch, and a dacron tube, the 'elephant trunk', is grafted to the descending aorta and the aorta is wrapped at the diaphragm (the #$ElephantTrunkAortaReplacementStage1-SurgicalProcedure).  Then, in the #$ElephantTrunkAortaReplacementStage2 instance, a stent graft is used to connect the 'elephant trunk' to the wrap graft.  Usually, the #$ElephantTrunkAortaReplacementStage2 is done via a catheter using an endovascular approach from the femoral artery, but in some cases, it may be done surgically instead.") :- x_cid(a65b16505edf83).
