x_comment(x_receiverSensitivity,"<code>(#$receiverSensitivity DEV INTERVAL)</code> means that <code>DEV</code> has a sensitivity of <code>INTERVAL</code>. Receiver sensitivity is the lowest power level at which the receiver can detect an RF signal and demodulate data.  It is measured in decibels, which are what Wikipedia calls \"dimensionless units\", i.e., intervals on a number line, which is why its second argument is an <code>#$IntervalOnNumberLine</code>.") :- x_cid(a65b16505edffb).
