x_comment(x_addFormulaFromConceptToFormulasWithConcept,"(#$addFormulaFromConceptToFormulasWithConcept TERM1 TERM2) means that when generating query fragments from query searches in the relevant context the system should add a formula created with TERM1 to any formulas created by TERM2 or, if TERM2 is a collection, any specializations of TERM2.  Note:  Formulas created with Collections are #$isa formulas.  For example, (#$addFormulaFromConceptToFormulasWithConcept #$patientTreated #$SurgicalProcedure) means that if a query fragment made with a specialization of SurgicalProcedure will show up in the query search results, then a formula made with #$patientTreated in arg0 should be added to that fragment.  Hence from (isa ?X PericardialWindow) we would instead generate and display (and (patientTreated ?X ?PATIENT) (isa ?X PericardialWindow)).  Here is another example. (#$addFormulaFromConceptToFormulasWithConcept #$patientTreated #$vascularProcedureReason).  This would entail that if (#$vascularProcedureReason ?X ?Y) appears, then we should instead generate (and (patientTreated ?X ?PAT) (#$vascularProcedureReason ?X ?Y)).  There is no assumption that the two fragments will share a variable, but the expected cases are that they will share exactly one variable and that normal query combination rules apply.") :- x_cid(a65b16505edfff).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505edfff,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16505edfff,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part07.krf').
