x_comment('x_ProperNamePredicate-Stub',"Instances of #$ProperNamePredicate-Stub are all the lexical predicates that can be used for the purpose of temporarily and rapidly registering the information that a certain STRING is (one of the) name(s) for a certain FORT.  The salient feature of the predicates that are instances of #$ProperNamePredicate-Stub is they should eventually be replaced with assertions using predicates that contain more grammatical information, such as instances of #$ProperNamePredicate-Strict. A prototypical example of such a predicate would be #$termStrings.  These differ from predicates that are merely instances of #$ProperNamePredicate-Loose in that those may be missing grammatical information (and are thus difficult to use in understanding text), but are nevertheless not intended to be removed when assertions with more grammatical information become available.") :- x_cid(a65b16505ee01f).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505ee01f,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16505ee01f,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part07.krf').
