x_comment('x_at-UnderspecifiedLandmark',"(#$at-UnderspecifiedLandmark ACT ATLOC) states that an abstract\nlocational relation holds between ACT and ATLOC, where ATLOC is a\n#$Landmark-Underspecified.  #$at-UnderspecifiedLandmark is an underspecified\nsemantic representation that may be elaborated to represent either a\nspatial example of physical landmarks (as in 'at Dublin') or a\ntemporal use of landmarks ('at 9pm' etc.) or metaphorical landmarks\n('at 6 billion dollars, Bill Gate's wealth is simply staggering', etc.).\nNote the distinction between #$at-UnderspecifiedLandmark and\n#$in-UnderspecifiedContainer: while one can say 'in June', one cannot say\n'at June' (at least not in #$EnglishSpeakingCultureMt where #$TimePoints\nbut not #$CalendarMonths can be conceptualized as\n#$Landmark-Underspecified, and #$CalendarMonths but not #$TimePoints can be\nconceptualized as #$Container-Underspecified).  Likewise, one can say 'at\n9pm' but not 'in 9pm'.") :- x_cid(a65b16505ee037).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505ee037,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16505ee037,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part07.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16505ee037,11831).
