x_comment('x_SportsCompetition-SameCompetitorsThroughout',"The collection of all #$SportsCompetitions in which the same 'top-level' competitors (see #$competingAgents-TopLevel) compete with each other throughout the competition.  Thus, for example, a single #$BaseballGame is a #$SportsCompetition-SameCompetitorsThroughout, because the same #$competingAgents-TopLevel - the same pair of baseball teams - compete with each other for the entire duration of the game.  Likewise, a single inning within said #$BaseballGame is a #$SportsCompetition-SameCompetitorsThroughout for the same reason.  A playoff series that includes the #$BaseballGame is NOT a #$SportsCompetition-SameCompetitorsThroughout, however, precisely because different teams compete with each other in different games within the series.  Another positive example:  a discus throw within the Beijing Olympics.  Another negative exampe:  the Beijing Olympics.") :- x_cid(a65b16505ee06a).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505ee06a,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16505ee06a,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part07.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16505ee06a,11897).
xc_kb_names(a65b16505ee06a,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16505ee06a,[]).
x_comment('x_TeamSportsCompetition-Entire',"The collection of all #$TeamSportsCompetitions which are also #$SportsEvents, i.e., which have pre-defined starting times, and which conclude with an evaluation and ranking of the competing #$SportsTeams.") :- x_cid(a65b16505ee06b).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505ee06b,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16505ee06b,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part07.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16505ee06b,11898).
