xc_mapping_rows(a65b16505ee06b,[]).
x_comment('x_competingAgents-TopLevel',"(#$competingAgents-TopLevel COMPETITION AGENT) means that AGENT is a competitor (#$competingAgents) in COMPETITION and there is no other agent of which AGENT is a part which is also a competitor in COMPETITION.  Thus, for example, consider the #$NewYorkGiants and some #$FootballGame-American GAME such that (#$competingAgents GAME #$NewYorkGiants).  The #$NewYorkGiants is not a part of any larger corporate entity which can also be said to be a #$competingAgents in GAME:  hence, it is true that (#$competingAgents-TopLevel GAME #$NewYorkGiants).  Consider, in contrast, a team member of the #$NewYorkGiants, PLAYER, who plays in GAME.  Because (#$competingAgents GAME #$NewYorkGiants), it is also true that (#$competingAgents GAME PLAYER):  however, because player is a member of the #$NewYorkGiants, it is NOT true that (#$competingAgents-TopLevel GAME PLAYER).") :- x_cid(a65b16505ee06c).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505ee06c,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
