x_comment(x_applicableWhenTypedOnlyWhenSpecialization,"(#$applicableWhenTypedOnlyWhenSpecialization ?VAR COLL CYCL-RULE) means that CYCL-RULE (an asserted rule that has an occurrence of ?VAR in the antecedent) should be pruned by the inference engine if ?VAR is explicitly typed in the problem via #$isa or rdf-type, unless it is typed by some specialization of COLL.  For example,\n\n<pre> \n(applicableWhenTypedOnlyWhenSpecialization ?EVT ThingWithDirectTemporalData\n    (implies\n       (and\n           (rdf-type ?TD EventDate)\n           (cCFDateTimeMax ?TD ?DATE)\n           (cCF-contains ?EVT ?TD)\n           (cCF-contains ?REC ?EVT)\n           (rdf-type ?REC PatientRecord))\n       (maxDateForEvent ?EVT ?DATE)))\n</pre>\nThe above states that if ?EVT is explicitly typed, the above rule should only fire when one of the typing collections is a specialization of ThingWithDirectTemporalData.  You would make an assertion like this  instead of adding a condition to the body of the rule when efficiency concerns dictate we don't want to solve \n\n<pre>\n (and\n  ...\n  (isa ?EVT ?TYPE)\n  (genls ?TYPE <b>COLL</b>)  \n</pre>\n in the traditional way.  Or when directly solving \n\n<pre>\n (isa ?EVT <b>COLL</b>)  \n</pre>\nis difficult or impossible.") :- x_cid(a65b16505ee0b9).
