x_comment(x_generatePredFormulasWithSpecInArg,"(#$generatePredFormulasWithSpecInArg PRED TERM NUM) means that if a specialization of TERM is a valid term in the query search results, then a sentence using PRED with the spec of TERM in the NUM position will be returned.  This overrides #$suppressIsaFormulasForCollections, which might otherwise prevent this formula.  For example, (#$generatePredFormulasWithSpecInArg #$isa #$Animal 2) means that the term #$Person will trigger the return of the sentence (#$isa ?X #$Person).") :- x_cid(a65b16505ee0cb).
