x_comment(x_generatePredFormulasWithInstanceInArg,"(#$generatePredFormulasWithInstanceInArg PRED TERM NUM) means that if an instance of TERM is a valid term in the search query results, then a sentence using PRED with the instance of TERM in the NUM position will be returned.  This overrides #$suppressIsaFormulasForCollections, which might otherwise prevent this formula.  For example, (#$generatePredFormulasWithInstanceInArg #$isa #$Collection 2) means that the term #$Person will trigger the return of the sentence (#$isa ?X #$Person).") :- x_cid(a65b16505ee0cc).
