x_comment(x_doneBy,"A very general #$ActorSlot predicate that relates events to the things that \"do\" them.  <code>(#$doneBy EVENT DOER)</code> means that <code>DOER</code> is a \"doer\" in the event <code>EVENT</code>: some activity on the part of <code>DOER</code> causes or carries out <code>EVENT</code>.  This predicate is agnostic as to whether <code>DOER</code> does <code>EVENT</code> intentionally or not.  Note that <code>DOER</code> need not even be animate or an agent; e.g. the famous volcanic eruption that buried Pompeii was #$doneBy Mt. Vesuvius.  Note also that an event might have more than one doer; consider a chess game.\n<p>\nSee the specializations #$performedBy and #$bodilyDoer for cases in which the \"doer\" is, respectively, an #$Agent-Generic acting deliberately and an #$Organism-Whole behaving non-deliberately.") :- x_cid(a65b16505ee1b8).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505ee1b8,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
