x_comment(x_properPhysicalPortions,"(#$properPhysicalPortions WHOLE PART) means that PART is a representative proper physical part of WHOLE, in the sense that the intrinsic physical properties of WHOLE are also properties of PART.  Proper physical parts of WHOLE which are not representative in this sense should not be related to WHOLE by #$properPhysicalPortions, but rather by #$properPhysicalParts or #$properPhysicalDecompositions (qq.v.).  For example, the SpaghettiSauce001 which is part of SpaghettiDinner001 would not be related to SpaghettiDinner001 by #$physicalPortions, since SpaghettiSauce001 differs from SpaghettiDinner001 in its composition (the latter has constituents -- noodles, parmesan cheese, and so on -- that the former does not have).  On the other hand, a #$physicalPortions of the dinner would include parts of all the constituents of the dinner.") :- x_cid(a65b16505ee1db).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505ee1db,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16505ee1db,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part07.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16505ee1db,12373).
xc_kb_names(a65b16505ee1db,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16505ee1db,[]).
x_comment(x_StuffType,"A collection of collections.  Each instance of #$StuffType is a collection that is stuff-like in at least one respect. A collection <code>COL</code> is stuff-like just in case there is some sense of 'part' according to which every part of an instance of <code>COL</code> is itself an instance of <code>COL</code>. More precisely, for a collection to be an instance of #$StuffType it is sufficient that there be some spec-pred <code>PARTPRED</code> of #$properParts (that is, some predicate <code>PARTPRED</code> for which<code> (#$genlPreds PARTPRED #$properParts)</code> holds), such that if <code>(#$isa OBJECT1 COL)</code> and <code>(PARTPRED OBJECT1 OBJECT2)</code>, then <code>(#$isa OBJECT2 COL)</code>. Here are two examples.  Consider #$Breathing. Take an instance of that, say a ten minute long period in which a person is breathing. Imagine some two minute snippet of that, one of its #$properTimeSlices (a spec-pred of #$properParts). That, too, is an instance of #$Breathing. So #$Breathing is a #$StuffType, since all #$properTimeSlices of an instance of #$Breathing are also instances of #$Breathing.\n<p>\nConsider #$Water. Take any instance of #$Water -- say the water in the Pacific Ocean. Now take any portion of that water -- say a handful of it that a person scoops up near Honolulu, one of its #$properPhysicalPortions (a spec-pred of #$properParts). That handful is itself an instance of #$Water. Hence #$Water is a #$StuffType, in virtue of the fact that all #$properPhysicalPortions of all instances #$Water are themselves instances of #$Water.\n<p>\nOther examples are: #$AspatialInformationStore, which is stuff-like with respect #$containsInformation; #$CharacterString, which is stuff-like with respect to #$subCharacterStrings; and #$List, which is stuff-like with respect to #$subLists. These examples are somewhat exceptional -- most #$StuffTypes are like the examples of #$Breathing and #$Water.  See #$ObjectType, for the contrasting (but not disjoint) notion of being object-like.") :- x_cid(a65b16505ee1dc).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505ee1dc,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16505ee1dc,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part07.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16505ee1dc,12374).
xc_kb_names(a65b16505ee1dc,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16505ee1dc,[]).
x_comment(x_ExistingStuffType,"A collection of collections, and a specialization of #$TemporalStuffType.  Each instance of #$ExistingStuffType is a collection of things (including portions of things) which are both temporally and spatially stufflike.  Division in time or space does not destroy the stufflike quality of the object (down to a certain granularity).\n<p>\n<code>(#$isa STUFFTYPE #$ExistingStuffType)</code> implies both (i) for most instances <code>STUFF</code> of <code>STUFFTYPE</code>, for any proper physical part (see #$properPhysicalDecompositions) <code>PART</code> of <code>STUFF</code>, <code>PART</code> is also an instance of <code>STUFFTYPE</code> and (ii) for all instances <code>STUFF</code> of <code>STUFFTYPE</code>, for most proper physical parts <code>PART</code> of <code>STUFF</code>, <code>PART</code> is also an instance of <code>STUFFTYPE</code>.\n<p>\nFor example, every piece of wood is temporally stufflike: if W-168 is a piece of wood during 1996, then it's also a piece of wood for the one-minute time-slice 9:05am 7/7/96.  It's also spatially stufflike: if we take that piece of wood W-168 and cut it in half, we have two things which are both pieces of wood.  Since every piece of wood is both temporally and spatially stufflike, #$Wood is an instance of #$ExistingStuffType.  Other instances of #$ExistingStuffType include the collections #$IceCream, #$Diamond, #$WaxedPaper, and #$StriatedMuscle. See the comment for #$StuffType to learn more about the distinctions between, and the need for, these four collections: #$StuffType, #$ObjectType and #$ExistingObjectType.") :- x_cid(a65b16505ee1dd).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505ee1dd,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16505ee1dd,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part07.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16505ee1dd,12379).
xc_kb_names(a65b16505ee1dd,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16505ee1dd,[]).
x_comment(x_stufflikeWRTPred,"This predicate relates collections to the parthood relationships by which the collection is deemed \"stuff-like\".\n<p>\n<code>(#$stufflikeWRTPred STUFFTYPE PARTHOODPRED)</code> means that if <code>STUFF</code> is an instance of <code>STUFFTYPE</code>, <code>(PARTHOODPRED STUFF STUFFPART)</code>, and <code>STUFFPART</code> is above the granularity level for <code>STUFFTYPE</code>, then <code>STUFFPART</code> is also an instance of <code>STUFFTYPE</code>.\n<p>\nFor instance, if one takes a proper temporal slice (see #$properTimeSlices) of an instance of #$Sightseeing, that temporal slice will also be an instance of #$Sightseeing (if it meets granularity requirements). Hence, (#$stufflikeWRTPred #$Sightseeing #$properTimeSlices).  In fact, for any instance, <code>TST</code>, of #$TemporalStuffType it will be the case that <code>(#$stufflikeWRTPred TST #$properTimeSlices)</code> and for any instance of #$ExistingStuffType, <code>EST</code>, it will be the case that (#$stufflikeWRTPred EST #$properPhysicalDecompositions).") :- x_cid(a65b16505ee1de).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505ee1de,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16505ee1de,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part07.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16505ee1de,12384).
xc_kb_names(a65b16505ee1de,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16505ee1de,[]).
