x_comment('x_nameString-Plural',"This predicate should be used for names of individuals that trigger plural verb agreement, such as (the) \"Oakland Raiders\".  The \"the\" part should be left out, because these names can sometimes appear without \"the\", as in \"How about those Raiders?\" and \"a Raiders fan\".  In other words, the string should be an N-bar, in the sense that it is compatible with a preceding determiner.  This predicate should NOT be used with apparently plural names like \"Abbott Laboratories\", because these trigger *singular* verb agreement, e.g. \"Abbott Laboratories is/*are working on a cure for cancer.\"") :- x_cid(a65b16505ee230).
