x_comment(x_NonInitialCollection,"A specialization of both #$TimeDependentCollection and #$FirstOrderCollection (qq.v.).  Each instance NIC of #$NonInitialCollection is a collection such that nothing can be an instance of NIC at the start of the thing's existence.  Thus nothing can be an instance of NIC for its entire existence.  Instanceship in NIC is typically \"acquired\" at some point in time T after the would-be instance INST comes into existence, where T might occur either during or after INST's existence (i.e. \"posthumously\").  #$NonInitialCollection is agnostic regarding whether INST is an instance of NIC \"intermittently\" (see #$IntermittentCollection).  Examples of non-initial collections are #$AdultAnimal, #$Veterinarian, and #$MinedArea.") :- x_cid(a65b16505ee319).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505ee319,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
