xc_mapping_rows(a65b16505ee31a,[]).
x_comment(x_TerminalNonInitialCollection,"A specialization of #$NonInitialCollection  (q.v.).  Each instance EDTC of #$TerminalNonInitialCollection is a collection such that: (i) a thing can be an instance of EDTC only while it is also an instance of #$SomethingExisting, (ii) once a thing becomes an instance of EDTC it necessarily remains so until such time as it is no longer an instance of #$SomethingExisting, (iii) nothing can be an instance of EDTC for the entire time during which it is an instance of #$SomethingExisting.  It follows from these conditions that (iv) nothing starts out as an instance of EDTC and (v) any instance of EDTC ceases to be such when it ceases to be an instance of #$SomethingExisting.  An example of an #$TerminalNonInitialCollection is (#$GraduateFn #$College), the collection of college graduates.  Cf. #$InitialCollection.") :- x_cid(a65b16505ee31b).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505ee31b,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16505ee31b,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part07.krf').
