x_comment(x_sitHasUnitOfCountInRoleInSubSitOfType,"<code>(#$sitHasUnitOfCountInRoleInSubSitOfType SITUATION COUNT-QTY ROLE SIT-TYPE)</code> means that the instance <code>SITUATION</code> of #$Situation is such that there are a total number of <code>N</code> instances of <code>TYPE</code> that play the role <code>ROLE</code> in instances of <code>SIT-TYPE</code> that are sub-situations of <code>SITUATION</code>, where <code>N</code> is the number such that <code>(#$isACountOfQuantity COUNT-QTY N)</code> and <code>TYPE</code> is the collection such that <code>(#$isACountOfType COUNT-QTY TYPE)</code>.  For example, <code>(#$sitHasUnitOfCountInRoleInSubSitOfType BobEatingBreakfast-212 ((#$UnitOfCountFn #$Doughnut) 3) #$consumedObject #$EatingEvent)</code> means that a total of 3 donughts are eaten (play the #$consumedObject role in an instance of #$EatingEvent) in the course of (i.e., these eating-events are #$subSituations of) BobEatingBreakfast-212.  <code>(#$sitHasUnitOfCountInRoleInSubSitOfType BobEatingBreakfast-352 ((#$UnitOfCountFn #$Doughnut) 0) #$consumedObject #$EatingEvent)</code> means that no donughts are eaten in the course of BobEatingBreakfast-352, <code>(#$sitHasUnitOfCountInRoleInSubSitOfType BobsDiet-517 ((#$UnitOfCountFn #$Doughnut) 40) #$consumedObject #$EatingEvent)</code> means that 40 doughnuts are eaten in the course of BobsDiet-517,and so forth.") :- x_cid(a65b16505ee371).
