x_comment(x_relationNotExistsExists,"A ternary #$RuleMacroPredicate that can be used to state that a given binary predicate stands in a certain relation to two collections.  <code>(#$relationNotExistsExists BINPRED COL1 COL2)</code> means that for any instance <code>INST1</code> of <code>COL1</code>, no instance <code>INST2</code> of <code>COL2</code> is such that <code>(BINPRED INST1 INST2)</code> holds.  It is equivalent to (and can thus be used in effect as shorthand for) the more complex form:\n<p>\n<pre>\n  (#$not\n    (#$and\n      (#$isa ?INST1 COL1)\n      (BINPRED INST1 INST2)\n      (#$isa ?INST2 COL2)))\n</pre>\n<p>\nSo #$relationNotExistsExists (and its defining axiom; see #$expansion) enables this common type of rule to be stated more tersely.\n<p>\nFor example, '(#$relationNotExistsExists #$performedBy #$Hunting #$Herbivore)' means that no herbivore hunts animals.") :- x_cid(a65b16505ee3db).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505ee3db,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16505ee3db,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part07.krf').
