x_comment(x_CyclicalProcessType,"The collection of all cyclical event types.  An event type <code>EVT-TYPE</code> is considered cyclical in the requisite sense if its instances 1) decompose into stages, or \"scenes\" and 2) \"spawn\" subsequent instances of <code>EVT-TYPE</code>.  This notion of \"spawning\" can be understood in terms of one event bringing about a state that serves as sufficient intitial conditions for the other to begin.  Accordingly, cyclical process types all feature a focal input/output class; that is, for any instance <code>EVT</code> of <code>EVT-TYPE</code>, there is some type <code>TYPE</code> such that one or more instances of <code>TYPE</code> are inputs, and by virtue of the way <code>EVT</code>, one or more instances of <code>TYPE</code> are outputs that are situated so as to become inputs to subsequent instances of <code>EVT-TYPE</code>.  To relate a cyclical process to its focal input/output type, use #$cyclicalProcessTypeFocus.") :- x_cid(a65b16505ee3e3).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505ee3e3,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
