x_comment(x_multipleChoiceOptionFullLabel,"A predicate used to represent informal features common to the presentation of multiple choice questions.  Specifically, in human-targeted representations of questions, options are typically given an index (often a numeral or a letter) followed by an string that expresses the content of the answer.  <code>(#$multipleChoiceOptionIndexLabel OPTION DESC)</code> identifies the string <code>DESC</code> as the full string (index + answer) assigned to <code>OPTION</code>.  For example, if <code>OPTION</code> appears (or is intended to appear) in text as \"iv. Meoisis II\" this would be represented as <code>(#$multipleChoiceOptionIndexLabel OPTION. \"iv. Meoisis II\")</code>.  See also #$multipleChoiceOptionIndexLabel.") :- x_cid(a65b16505ee407).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505ee407,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
