x_comment(x_ActivationOfEnzymeOfTypeFn,"A collection-denoting function used to represent the class of 'activations' of a given type of enzyme.  Where MOL-TYPE is a class of #$EnzymeMolecule, (#$ActivationOfEnzymeOfTypeFn MOL-TYPE) denotes the class of all occurrences in which an instance of MOL-TYPE is rendered 'active' in the sense of being enabled to catalyze certain types of chemical reactions particular to the class of enzyme.  In most cases, an instance of (#$ActivationOfEnzymeOfTypeFn MOL-TYPE) will consist in a #$ChemicalObjectUnbindingEvent where the #$EnzymeMolecule is chemically unbound from an 'inactivation factor' (see #$inactivationFactorForEnzyme) which otherwise blocks it from catalyzing the necessary reactions, followed immediately by a #$ChemicalObjectBindingEvent wherein the #$EnzymeMolecule is bound to an 'activaton factor' (see #$activationFactorForEnzyme) which enables it to catalyze the necessary reactions.  Often, the activation and inactivation components are both #$Nucleosides.") :- x_cid(a65b16505ee48c).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505ee48c,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16505ee48c,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part07.krf').
