x_comment(x_enzymeTypeActivatedInActivationType,"The corresponding predicate of #$ActivationOfEnzymeOfTypeFn.  Where MOL-TYPE is a class of #$EnzymeMolecule, (#$enzymeTypeActivatedInActivationType MOL-TYPE ACTIVATION-TYPE) means that ACTIVATION-TYPE is the class of all occurrences in which an instance of MOL-TYPE is rendered 'active' in the sense of being enabled to catalyze certain types of chemical reactions particular to the class of enzyme.  In most cases, an instance of ACTIVATION-TYPE will consist in a #$ChemicalObjectUnbindingEvent where the #$EnzymeMolecule is chemically unbound from an 'inactivation factor' (see #$inactivationFactorForEnzyme) which otherwise blocks it from catalyzing the necessary reactions, followed immediately by a #$ChemicalObjectBindingEvent wherein the #$EnzymeMolecule is bound to an 'activaton factor' (see #$activationFactorForEnzyme) which enables it to catalyze the necessary reactions.  Often, the activation and inactivation components are both #$Nucleosides.") :- x_cid(a65b16505ee48d).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505ee48d,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
