x_comment(x_cellularProcessTypeFromSignalTypeToResponseType,"The corresponding predicate (#$functionCorrespondingPredicate-Canonical) of #$CellularSignalToResponseProcessTypeFn.  Where SIGNAL-TYPE is a specialization of an 'organism-wide' dispersal of a substance composed of instances of some kind of signal molecule such as #$EpinephrineMolecule (said dispersal type will often be represented using #$IntercellularMediumReleaseOfChemicalObjectTypeFn) and RESPONSE-TYPE is a kind of cellular level response (a specialization of #$BiologicalProcess-CellularLevel),(#$cellularProcessTypeFromSignalTypeToResponseType SIGNAL-TYPE RESPONSE-TYPE PROCESS-TYPE) means that PROCESS-TYPE is the collection of all instances #$CellularSignalingProcess-SignalToResponse which begin with an instance of SIGNAL-TYPE and conclude with many cells undergoing a response of RESPONSE-TYPE.") :- x_cid(a65b16505ee4bc).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505ee4bc,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
