x_comment(x_CoilTightening,"The collection of events which consist of the tightening of a coil.  The coil may have a fixed center or a fixed axis.  Non-fixed points engage in spiral motion about the axis of rotation.  The process is reversed by #$CoilLoosening.  There is a mechanical limit to the amount of #$CoilTightening which can be done, which in some cases is easy to reach.  Winding a #$Wristwatch is an example of #$CoilTightening.  #$CoilTightening is differentiated from #$Reeling in, in that in #$CoilTightening the object is in a tighter coil after the #$CoilTightening process, whereas when reeling in the coil remains about the same tightness, but a greater perportion of the object is in the coil.  #$CoilTightening takes energy to tighten some objects beyond their rest state, but releases energy when tightening back to the rest state after forcefully being uncoiled.  Making a coil of rope from an uncoiled rope by pulling it onto a spinning reel is #$Reeling; tightening that coil is #$CoilTightening.") :- x_cid(a65b16505ee4e0).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505ee4e0,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
