x_comment(x_TemporallyQualifiableRelation,"The collection of all #$Relations whose extentions (see #$relationExtension) change, at least somewhat, over time.  A relation <code>RELN</code> is an instance of #$TemporallyQualifiableRelation if and only if there is sequence <code>SEQ</code> and times <code>T1</code> and <code>T2</code> such that <code>RELN</code> holds among <code>SEQ</code> at <code>T1</code> but not at <code>T2</code>.  \n<p>\nNote that <code>RELN</code> might nevertheless hold of <i>some</i> sequences eternally.  An example of such a relation is #$isa.  On the one hand, the sentence\n<pre>\n  (#$isa #$GeorgeWBush #$UnitedStatesPresident)\n</pre>\nis true at some times and false at others, and so requires temporal qualification.    On the other hand, the sentence\n<pre>\n  (#$isa #$UnitedStatesPresident #$FirstOrderCollection)\n</pre>\nis true eternally and requires no temporal qualification.\n<p>\nIf a given temporally-qualifiable relation holds of <i>no</i> sequences eternally (e.g. #$likesAsFriend), it is an instance of the specialization #$TimeDependentRelation (q.v.).\n<p>\nCf. #$TimeIndependentRelation.") :- x_cid(a65b16505ee4fb).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505ee4fb,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16505ee4fb,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part07.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16505ee4fb,13276).
