x_comment('x_Only-TC-Fn',"The function that corresponds to the predicate, #$only-TC, <code>(#$Only-TC-Fn PRED)</code> denotes the instance <code>SPEC-PRED</code> of #$TernaryPredicate such that <code>(#$only-TC PRED SPEC-PRED)</code>, where <code>PRED</code> is an instance of #$CapabilityPredicate-TypeLevel. <code>SPEC-PRED</code> is a more restrictive version of that <code>Pred</code>.  In particular, each instance <code>CPTL</code> of #$CapabilityPredicate-TypeLevel has the following semantics: <code>(CPTL TYPE SIT-TYPE ROLE)</code> holds iff every instance of <code>TYPE</code> has the relevant capability (curried into <code>CPTL</code>) of playing the role <code>ROLE</code> in instances of <code>SIT-TYPE</code>; however <code>(#$only-TC CPTL RCPTL)</code> identifies <code>RCPTL</code> as the ternary predicate that restricts this capability to <i>only</i> instances of <code>TYPE</code>.  Thus <code>(RCPTL TYPE SIT-TYPE ROLE)</code> holds just in case <code>(CPTL TYPE SIT-TYPE ROLE)</code> and for no collections <code>COL</code>, <code>(CPTL COL SIT-TYPE ROLE)</code> holds unless <code>COL</code> is a specialization of <code>TYPE</code>.") :- x_cid(a65b16505ee500).
