x_comment(x_CanonicallyTemporallyIndexedDBTable,"A subcollection of #$DatabaseTable. Each #$CanonicallyTemporallyIndexedDBTable <code>TABLE</code> has two columns, <code>A</code> and <code>B</code>, specified by (#$temporalTranslationColumns <code>TABLE</code> <code>A</code> <code>B</code>). Their datatypes are timestamp, and the values within a row, R, for <code>A</code> and <code>B</code> respectively state the starting and ending times of any propositions that are translations of sequences of cells in R. In CycL translations of DB table contents, the microtheory component of the translation (see the instances of #$DBTable-ContentMtRelationship) is (#$MtSpace MT (#$MtTimeWithGranularityDimFn (#$TimeIntervalInclusiveFn TRANS(A) TRANS(B)) TimePoint)), where MT is the #$contentMt for <code>TABLE</code>, and TRANS(A) and TRANS(B) are direct translations from the database's timestamp type into a CycL #$Date. Contrast with #$NonCanonicallyTemporallyIndexedDBTable.") :- x_cid(a65b16505ee539).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505ee539,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
