x_comment(x_systemControls,"A specialization of #$systemComponents, <code>(#$systemControls SYSTEM CONTROL)</code> means that <code>CONTROL</code> is a component of <code>SYSTEM</code> that plays the role of a control, in a very general sense.  In a mechanical system, <code>CONTROL</code> might be a physical knob or button that an operator uses, or it might be a device (such as spring-based thermostat in a car) that reacts when conditions are \"right\", thereby allowing certain sub-routines to proceed.  In a biological system, <code>CONTROL</code> might be a biological analogue to an internal device, or it might be a configuration within a biological object that must be attained for certain biological functions to proceed normally.") :- x_cid(a65b16505ee5bb).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505ee5bb,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
