x_comment(x_RuleAssertionBoundAntecedentFn,"An instance of #$EvaluatableFunction.  #$RuleAssertionBoundAntecedentFn takes a (quoted) instance of #$CycLRuleAssertion and a list of bindings, and returns a (quoted) instance of #$CycLSentence-Askable that is the antecedent of the rule, with variables replaced with bindings from the list (in canonical order).  For example,  <code>(#$RuleAssertionBoundAntecedentFn (#$ist #$BaseKB (#$implies (#$isa ?MIC #$Microtheory)\n               (#$genlMt ?MIC #$BaseKB))) (#$TheList #$BiologyMt))</code> evaluates to <code>(#$isa #$BiologyMt #$Microtheory)</code>.  For a related function that takes a rule sentence and evaluates to its (unbound) antecedent, see #$RuleSentenceAntecedentFn.") :- x_cid(a65b16505ee5ca).
