x_comment(x_otherwiseDerivable,"A specialization of #$rejectedSentence, <code>(#$otherwiseDerivable SENTENCE)</code> means that the #$CycLSentence <code>SENTENCE</code> is false, and has a rejected proof via a rule for which the non-0 arguments in <code>SENTENCE</code> form an exception.  Specifically, there is a #$CycLRuleAssertion <code>RULE</code> for which some list of bindings </code>BINDINGS-LIST</code> is abnormal (i.e., <code>(#$abnormal RULE BINDINGS-LIST)</code>, such that substituting the appropriate bindings from <code>BINDINGS-LIST</code> for the variables in <code>RULE</code> results in a rule sentence whose antecedent is true.  Yet, because the list is #$abnormal for the rule, <code>SENTENCE</code>, which is the consequent that results from this substitution, is rejected.") :- x_cid(a65b16505ee5cc).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505ee5cc,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
