x_comment('x_QueryRelaxationStrategy-RemoveLiteralViaSpecifiedOrder',"This is a collection of iterative modification strategies.  By definition instances of this collection never apply unless their associated query has been run.  In this case the strategy is to successively remove literals, in the order specified, until the query returns results or you get to the end of the specified order -- i.e. you run out of literals to remove.  In general,  after the initial query is run, the applicability condition on the instance of the strategy is checked and if the query plus result set satisfies the condition, then the strategy is executed and the query rerun.  This continues recursively until the condition fails or the end of the ordering is reached.  All results from all iterations are compiled, filtered according to any result filters, and presented as the binding set for the iterated query sequence.") :- x_cid(a65b16505ee5ce).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505ee5ce,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16505ee5ce,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part07.krf').
