x_comment(x_ApplyFunctionRecursivelyFn,"(#$ApplyFunctionRecursivelyFn LIST SEED FN) returns the result of applying FN, an evaluatable function, first to the first item in LIST and SEED, then to the second item in LIST and the result of the first application, and so on, for every item in LIST.  For example, (#$ApplyFunctionRecursivelyFn (#$TheList 2 4 6 8) 1 #$TimesFn)) = 384. By definition, if ARGS is empty, the result is SEED.  Every member of LIST and SEED must be a valid argument for FN.  This is currently only defined for functions with an arity less than 3.  Note that if FN is a unary function, this simply results in the value you would get by applying FN to the last item in LIST.") :- x_cid(a65b16505ee6af).
