x_comment(x_CellularCommunication,"An important concept in molecular signaling in cells.  Generally speaking, a cellular signaling event begins with a general release or dispersion of many instances of a type of signal molecule, such as epinephrine (#$EpinephrineMolecule) into the intercellular medium, usually through release into the #$Bloodstream (see IntercellularMediumReleaseOfChemicalObjectTypeFn).  Instances of the signal molecule type either penetrate cells by diffusion through the phospholipid bilayer to bind with intracellular receptor molecules in the cellular cytoplasm, or bind to membrane receptors.  In the latter case, the mebranal binding of a signal molecule is invariably the first step in what is commonly known as a 'transduction path' or 'transduction pathway' (#$CellSignalingProcess-LocalizedToSingleCell) wherein a train of characteristic protein activations will be triggered.  Either as the result of the signal molecule bindings within cellular cytoplasms, or the triggering of parallel transduction paths within cells, many cells will undergo cellular-level morphological or metabolic changes (#$BiologicalProcess-CellularLevel) which en masse constitute a cellular response that terminates the signaling process.") :- x_cid(a65b16505ee6fb).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505ee6fb,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16505ee6fb,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part07.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16505ee6fb,13825).
xc_kb_names(a65b16505ee6fb,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16505ee6fb,[]).
x_comment(x_chemicalObjectsOfTypeAreSecondMessengersInSignalProcess,"Where PROCESS is an instance of #$CellularSignalingProcess-SignalToResponse and OBJ-TYPE is a kind of #$ChemicalObject, (#$chemicalObjectsOfTypeAreSecondMessengersInSignalProcess PROCESS OBJ-TYPE) means that instances of OBJ-TYPE play the role of 'second messengers' with respect to transduction pathways (#$CellSignalingProcess-LocalizedToSingleCell) occurring within PROCESS.") :- x_cid(a65b16505ee6fc).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505ee6fc,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16505ee6fc,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part07.krf').
