x_comment(x_sustainsPeakDuringSubSituation,"(#$sustainsPeakDuringSubSituation COMP-QUANT-PRED ROLE THING SUB-SIT SIT) means that for the ROLE-PLAYER that plays the role ROLE during SUB-SIT, (COMP-QUANT-PRED ROLE-PLAYER THING QUANT) is such that QUANT first reaches its highest values during SUB-SIT relative to all other unsubsumed sub-situations of SIT.\n<p>\nFor example, (#$sustainsPeakDuringSubSituation #$productionRateOfRegion #$eventOccursAt  #$PetroleumProduct  #$TerroristAttack-November-4-1979-Tehran-Iran #$IranHostageCrisis) means that, since #$TerroristAttack-November-4-1979-Tehran-Iran occurs at #$Iran, there is a value QUANT such that (#$productionRateOfRegion #$Iran #$PetroleumProduct QUANT)is first true during the #$TerroristAttack-November-4-1979-Tehran-Iran and during every other unsubsumed sub-event of #$IranHostageCrisis (#$productionRateOfRegion #$Iran #$PetroleumProduct OTHER-QUANT) is such that OTHER-QUANT is less than or equal to QUANT.") :- x_cid(a65b16505ee809).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505ee809,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16505ee809,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part07.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16505ee809,14098).
