x_comment(x_reachesPeakDuringSubSituationType,"(#$reachesPeakDuringSubSituationType\nCOMP-QUANT-PRED ROLE THING SUB-SIT-TYPE SIT-TYPE) means that for the ROLE-PLAYER that plays the role ROLE during any instance of SUB-SIT-TYPE that is a sub-situation of SIT  (an instance of SIT-TYPE), (COMP-QUANT-PRED ROLE-PLAYER THING QUANT) is such that QUANT first reaches its highest values during SUB-SIT relative to all other unsubsumed sub-situations of SIT.\n<p>\nFor example, (#$reachesPeakDuringSubSituationType\n #$amountPresentAt #$objectActedOn #$Shampoo (#$ApplyingStuffFn #$Shampoo) #$WashingHair) means that, since in any instance APP of (#$ApplyingStuffFn #$Shampoo) that is a sub-event of some instance WASH of #$WashingHair the #$objectActedOn is some instance HOH #$HairOnHead, there is a value QUANT such that (#$amountPresentAt #$Shampoo QUANT) is first true immediately after some phase of APP and during every other unsubsumed sub-event of  WASH (#$amountPresentAt #$Shampoo OTHER-QUANT) is such that OTHER-QUANT is less than or equal to QUANT.") :- x_cid(a65b16505ee80b).
