x_comment(x_CorrectingAnErrorInSomething,"The collection of events in which some error or other is corrected in something. This includes removing bugs from computer code, correcting typos in printed works, etc. Note that the thing corrected must have some existence before the correction and continue to exist after the correction. Hence, a school teacher's correction of a student's verbal pronunciation is not an instance of this collection because the teacher's example of how to correctly pronounce the words is not strictly a correction in this sense, rather it is a demonstration -- the original utterance can not be corrected and the teacher's demonstration is no guarantee that the student's behavior is corrected. Whether strict identity is maintained is dependent on the type of thing corrected, but continuity is required.") :- x_cid(a65b16505ee942).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505ee942,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
