x_comment(x_typeTypicallyIncludesType,"(#$typeTypicallyIncludesType TYPE1 TYPE2) means that instances of TYPE1 typically include some instance of TYPE2 either as a physical part (#$physicalParts) or as something it spatially contains (#$spatiallyIncludes).  This is meant to be somewhat weaker than the normal \"default\" assumption of normal conditions that would be appropriate to say that cars have wheels, doors have handles, etc.  This also covers cases where, while you might expect some TYPE1 to include some TYPE2, encountering one that lacked it would not entirely surprise you.  E.g. there is typically gas in cars, staples in staplers, ink in a writing pen, etc.") :- x_cid(a65b16505ee949).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505ee949,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
