x_comment(x_mainFunctionalComponent,"A predicate that relates objects to parts of it which are its main functional components.\n<code>(#$mainFunctionalComponent WHOLE PART)</code> means that <code>WHOLE</code> is at least partially made of <code>PART</code> (<code>(#$physicalParts WHOLE PART)</code> holds), and (as a default) the purpose or function of <code>WHOLE</code> derives from the physical properties of <code>PART</code>.  For example a medication may have certain active ingredients.  Many, if not most, of the properties of the whole medication may be very different than the properties of the active ingredients -- e.g. the medication is pill-shaped, has a sweet coating, is made mostly of inert materials, etc.  In a case such as that, the pill stands in the #$mainFunctionalComponent relationship to the portion of drug that is the active ingredient.  Accordingly, #$activeIngredients is a specialization of this predicate.") :- x_cid(a65b16505ee950).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505ee950,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
