xc_mapping_rows(a65b16505ee950,[]).
x_comment(x_packagedProductTypePrimaryProductType,"(#$packagedProductTypePrimaryProductType TYPE1 TYPE2) means that all instances of the product type TYPE1 have some portion of TYPE2 as their primary product.  For example, the collection of boxes of staples have the individual staples/rows of staples as their primary product.  Note this does not entail that instances of TYPE1 are primarily composed of TYPE2 as the volume or mass of the packaging materials of TYPE1 may exceed that of the primary product it wraps.  Typically TYPE2 will be an instance of #$ExistingStuffType, but this is not required.") :- x_cid(a65b16505ee951).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505ee951,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
