x_comment(x_RandomSelectionEvent,"Instances of #$RandomSelectionEvent are events in which one or more items from among a group of candidates is randomly chosen for, or happens to become subject to, a different outcome than the others.  Note that instances may involve, but do not necessarily involve purposeful action on the part of an agent.  Choosing a playing card from a shuffled (randomized) deck would be an instance of #$RandomSelectionEvent, but so would the ''choice'' of heads or tails for a lost coin that fell onto the ground.") :- x_cid(a65b16505ee978).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505ee978,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
