x_comment(x_relationInstanceNotExists,"A ternary #$RuleMacroPredicate that can be used to state that a given binary predicate stands in a certain relation to a thing, INST1, and some collection.  <code>(#$relationInstanceNotExists BINPRED INST1 COL2)</code> means that no instance <code>INST2</code> of <code>COL2</code> is such that <code>(BINPRED INST1 INST2)</code> holds.  It is equivalent to (and can thus be used in effect as shorthand for) the more complex form:\n<p>\n<pre>\n  (#$not\n    (#$and\n      (BINPRED INST1 INST2)\n      (#$isa ?INST2 COL2)))\n</pre>\n<p>\nSo #$relationInstanceNotExists (and its defining axiom; see #$expansion) enables this common type of rule to be stated more tersely.\n<p>\nFor example, '(#$relationInstanceNotExists #$owns #$Pittman #$Diamond-Gem)' means that #$Pittman owns no diamonds.") :- x_cid(a65b16505ee988).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505ee988,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16505ee988,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part07.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16505ee988,14508).
xc_kb_names(a65b16505ee988,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16505ee988,[]).
x_comment(x_relationNotExistsInstance,"A ternary #$RuleMacroPredicate that can be used to state that a given binary predicate stands in a certain relation to a thing, INST2, and some collection.  <code>(#$relationNotExistsInstance BINPRED COL1 INST2)</code> means that no instance <code>INST1</code> of <code>COL1</code> is such that <code>(BINPRED INST1 INST2)</code> holds.  It is equivalent to (and can thus be used in effect as shorthand for) the more complex form:\n<p>\n<pre>\n  (#$not\n    (#$and\n      (BINPRED INST1 INST2)\n      (#$isa ?INST1 COL1)))\n</pre>\n<p>\nSo #$relationNotExistsInstance (and its defining axiom; see #$expansion) enables this common type of rule to be stated more tersely.\n<p>\nFor example, '(#$relationNotExistsInstance #$performedBy #$BalletDancing #$Pittman)' means that #$Pittman does not perform any ballet dancing.") :- x_cid(a65b16505ee989).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505ee989,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16505ee989,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part07.krf').
