x_comment(x_objectFoundInLocation,"A #$CoexistingObjectsPredicate and specialization of #$inRegion (q.v.).  <code>(#$objectFoundInLocation OBJ LOC)</code> means that <code>OBJ</code> has the location <code>LOC</code>, in the sense that at least some part of <code>OBJ</code> is at <code>LOC</code> (as long as <code>LOC</code> itself is not part of  <code>OBJ</code>).\n<p>\n<code>OBJ</code> might or might not be a physical part (see #$physicalDecompositions) of <code>LOC</code>.  Thus, both (#$objectFoundInLocation #$MountEverest #$HimalayaMountains) and (#$parts #$HimalayaMountains #$MountEverest) are true, and both (#$objectFoundInLocation #$PietaStatue-Michelangelo #$StPetersBasilica) and (#$not (#$parts #$StPetersBasilica #$PietaStatue-Michelangelo)) are true.\n<p>\nHowever, <code>LOC</code> must <i>not</i> be a proper part of <code>OBJ</code>: (#$objectFoundInLocation #$HimalayaMountains #$MountEverest) is false.") :- x_cid(a65b16505ee9b1).
