x_comment(x_haveThisInCommon,"A predicate used to identify what facts are commonly true of distinct objects, by relating ojects in a set or collection to a sentence template into which terms denoting those objects can be substituted, producing a true sentence in each case. <code>(#$haveThisInCommon SET FORMULA)</code> means that substituting each element of SET in for the designated meta-variable :TERM in FORMULA will result in a #$CycLSentence-Askable that is #$True.  For example, <code>(#$haveThisInCommon (#$TheSet #$Dog #$Cat #$Emu) (#$and (#$isa :TERM #$FirstOrderCollection) (#$genls :TERM #$Animal)))</code> means that replacing #$Dog, #$Cat, and #$Emu for :TERM in the arg2 will result in three sentences, (#$and (#$isa #$Dog #$FirstOrderCollection) (#$genls #$Dog #$Animal)), (#$and (#$isa #$Cat #$FirstOrderCollection) (#$genls #$Cat #$Animal)), and (#$and (#$isa #$Emu #$FirstOrderCollection) (#$genls #$Emu #$Animal)) that are all true.") :- x_cid(a65b16505ee9ec).
