x_comment(x_situationTypeForServiceType,"(#$situationTypeForServiceType  AGREE-TYPE SIT-TYPE) means that it is a requirement of any instance of AGREE-TYPE that there be appropriately related situations of SIT-TYPE.  How these situations are related to the service provided depends on the type of service.  For example, if one has subscribed to an email service, one should be able to log in, retrieve email, send email, etc.  In general, SIT-TYPE refers to a collection of situations which the service enables and the user of the service plays some role in making come about.  contrast this with (#$ServicesForAgreementTypeFn  AGREE-TYPE) which refers to the collection of services provided by the agreement, but which are performed by the service provider like \"setting up the customer's account on the server\" and so forth.") :- x_cid(a65b16505eea48).
