x_comment(x_superEventTypes,"A #$FirstOrderCollectionPredicate that is a specialization of #$temporallySubsumedBy-TypeType and #$normalWholeTypeForPartType (qq.v),  and is a type-level inverse correlate of #$subEvents (q.v.).  This predicate is used to state that events of one given type always have events of another given type as superevents.  <code>(#$superEventTypes SUBTYPE SUPERTYPE)</code> means that for every instance <code>SUBINST</code> of <code>SUBTYPE</code>, there is an instance <code>SUPERINST</code> of <code>SUPERTYPE</code>, such that <code>(#$subEvents SUPERINST SUBINST)</code>.  For example, (#$superEventTypes #$Sentencing-Legal #$Trial-Criminal) means that every legal sentencing is a subevent of a criminal trial.  \n<p>\nSee also #$subEventTypes; and note that <code>(#$subEventTypes SUPERTYPE SUBTYPE)</code> is neither necessary nor sufficient for <code>(#$superEventTypes SUBTYPE SUPERTYPE)</code>.") :- x_cid(a65b16505eeac3).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505eeac3,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
