x_comment('x_partwiseDisjoint-TypeType',"A first-order collection predicate and a specialization of #$disjointWith (q.v.).  <code>(#$partwiseDisjoint-TypeType TYPE1 TYPE1)</code> means that no instances of <code>TYPE1</code> and <code>TYPE2</code> share any parts.  I.e., if <code>I1</code> and <code>I2</code> are instances of <code>ITYPE1</code> and <code>ITYPE2</code> respectively, then there are no individuals <code>I</code> such that both <code>(#$parts I1 I)</code> and <code>(#$parts I2 I)</code>.  For example (#$partwiseDisjoint-TypeType #$NFLPreSeason #$NFLPostSeason) is true because there is no part of any instance of #$NFLPreSeason that is also a part of some instance of #$NFLPostSeason.") :- x_cid(a65b16505eead2).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505eead2,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
