x_comment(x_StandardCodingLibrary,"The collection of all standard coding libraries.  A standard library is conventionally made available for every implementation of a range of programming languages.  In some cases, the library is described in the language specification; in other cases, the contents are determined by informal practices of the programming commmunity.  Most standard libraries include definitions for at least commonly-used algorithms, data astructures (lists, trees, hash tables), and interactions with the host platform, including input/output and operating system calls.  Depending on the constructs made available by the host language(s), a standard library may also include subroutines, macro definitions, class definitions, global variables, and templates.  http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Standard_Library") :- x_cid(a65b16505eeada).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505eeada,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
