x_comment(x_ProteinMoleculeTypeByChemicalCompoundType,"A type-level collection. Each instance is a collection of #$Molecules characterized by the fact that all of its instances are molecules of a #$ProteinMoleculeOrProteinComplex, and all are of the same #$ChemicalSubstanceType.  Cf. the more specific collection #$ProteinMoleculeTypeByChemicalSpecies, which is a collection whose instances all share the same chemical formula and structure.  Note that proteins, with their large complex molecules, are often given the same name despite subtle variations in structure.  The collection containing all the variants would be an instance of  #$ProteinMoleculeTypeByChemicalCompoundType, while only particular variants would be instances of #$ProteinMoleculeTypeByChemicalSpecies.  For example, #$AdenylylCyclaseMolecule has ten known variants in mammals that differ in their sequence of anmino acids and are coded for by different genes.  It is therefore an instance of #$ProteinMoleculeTypeByChemicalCompoundType.") :- x_cid(a65b16505eeb53).
