x_comment('x_ControlUnit-Computational',"A collection of #$ComputerHardwareComponents, each of which manages certain key components of a computing architecture.  Specifically, the #$ControlUnit reads the code for the next instruction from the cell indicated by the #$ComputerProgramCounter, decodes the numerical code for the instruction into a set of commands or signals for each of the other target systems, increments the #$ComputerProgramCounter so that it points to the next instruction, reads whatever data the instruction requires from cells in memory (or perhaps from an input device), provides the necessary data to an #$Arithmetic-LogicUnit or #$ComputerMemoryRegister, instructs the hardware to perform the specified operation (if necessary), writes the result from the #$Arithmetic-LogicUnit back to #$ComputerMemoryRegisters or an output device, and then iterates the process for the succeeding code instruction, until all instructions have been read.") :- x_cid(a65b16505eeb73).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505eeb73,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16505eeb73,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part07.krf').
