x_comment(x_NocardiaBrasiliensis,"A collection of #$Bacterium that may cause a superficial skin #$Infection in humans.  Usually, the route of infection occurs atfer some type of outdoor activity that results in a minor trauma to the skin (i.e. a thorn prick).  The infection commonly produces a localized pustule.  If they gain access to subcutaneous tissues, an infection similar to the one caused by Actinomudra Madurae may occur.") :- x_cid(a65b16505eebe9).
