x_comment(x_PasteurellaMultocida,"This species under the genus #$Pasteurella occurs worldwide in the respiratory and gastrointestinal tract of domesticated and wild animals.  These #$ProkaryoticCells are the most\ncommon #$Organism-Whole found in human wounds inflicted by cats and\ndogs.  Infection occurs at the site of the wound usually within 24 hours.  Typically the infection takes the form of cellulitis with a well-defined erythematous border.  They also commonly cause hemorrhagic septicemia in a variety of animals.") :- x_cid(a65b16505eebf1).
