x_comment(x_enzymeTypeInactivatedInInactivationType,"The corresponding predicate of #$InactivationOfEnzymeOfTypeFn.  Where MOL-TYPE is a class of #$EnzymeMolecule, (#$enzymeTypeInactivatedInInactivationType MOL-TYPE INACTIVATION-TYPE) means that INACTIVATION-TYPE is the class of all occurrences in which an instance of MOL-TYPE is rendered 'inactive' in the sense of becoming unable to catalyze certain types of chemical reactions particular to the class of enzyme.  In most cases, an instance of INACTIVATION-TYPE will consist in a #$ChemicalObjectBindingEvent where the #$EnzymeMolecule is chemically bound to an 'inactivation factor' (see #$inactivationFactorForEnzyme) which blocks it from catalyzing the necessary reactions, preceded by a #$ChemicalObjectUnbindingEvent wherein the #$EnzymeMolecule is unbound from an 'activaton factor' (see #$activationFactorForEnzyme) for the necessary reactions.  Often, the activation and inactivation components are both #$Nucleosides.") :- x_cid(a65b16505eec18).
