x_comment(x_physicalSchemaUsesLogicalSchemaFromPhyscialSchema,"(#$physicalSchemaUsesLogicalSchemaFromPhyscialSchema PS1 PS2 LS) means that PS1 uses the same encoding and decoding statements as PS2 with respect to the logical fields in LS.  This is typically used in the context of SKSI mappings to triple stores.  Asserting this of a pair of physical schemas and a logical schema that corresponds to an #$SKSISupportedOWLProperty will forwardly propagate the encoding and decoding statements that involve PS2 and the subject and object field indexicals of LS into corresponding encoding and decoding statements that reference PS1 and those same logical field indexicals.  This allows us to define in a general way a relationship that appears in many different datasets -- e.g. general RDF vocabulary, SKOS vocabulary, FOAF, etc. -- and propagate its encoding and decoding statements to any KS/PS that needs to utilize that vocabulary.") :- x_cid(a65b16505eec7f).
