x_comment(x_activeFormOfReceptor,"The corresponding predicate of #$ActiveFormOfReceptorFn. Where MOL-TYPE is a specialization of #$ReceptorMolecule, (#$activeFormOfReceptor MOL-TYPE ACTIVE-MOL-TYPE) in a given context means that ACTIVE-MOL-TYPE is the collection of all instances of MOL-TYPE that are able to initiate the signal transduction (See #$SignalTransduction-CellularProcess) typical to MOL-TYPE, usually as a result of being activated by ligand binding.") :- x_cid(a65b16505eec8f).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505eec8f,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16505eec8f,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part07.krf').
