x_comment(x_ReceptorLigandComplexTypeFn,"Where RTYPE is a specialization of #$ReceptorMolecule and LTYPE is a specialization of #$BiochemicalSignalingObject, (#$ReceptorLigandComplexTypeFn RTYPE LTYPE) denotes the collection of all instances of RTYPE that are in a state of being bound to a ligand of type LTYPE. In many cases, such a complex is in an active state and can initiate a signal transduction pathway leading to a cellular response. However, depending on the type of ligand and the type of receptor, the complex may be inactive or less active than the unbound form of the receptor.") :- x_cid(a65b16505eecaa).
