x_comment(x_TrabecularBoneTissue,"One of two types of bone tissue.  Trabecular bone, also called spongy bone or cancellous bone, is found in the interior of bones (see #$Bone-BodyPart) and is surrounded by #$CorticalBoneTissue.  In the human skeleton, trabecular bone is found at the ends of long bones.  It is softer and less dense than cortical bone, and is composed of a network of trabeculae, or small approximately cylindrical units.") :- x_cid(a65b16505eed03).
