x_comment(x_onlyBiologicalObjectTypeSecretesType,"<code>(#$onlyBiologicalObjectTypeSecretesType BLO-TYPE SECRETION-TYPE)</code> means that only instances of <code>BLO-TYPE</code> (a specialization of #$BiologicalLivingObject) are sources (during instances of #$SecretionEvent) of instances of <code>SECRETION-TYPE</code> (a specialization of #$PartiallyTangible, and typically a specialization of #$Secretion-Bodily).  \n<p>\nFor example, all of the following are true:\n<p>\n(#$onlyBiologicalObjectTypeSecretesType #$IsletsOfLangerhans #$Insulin)<br>\n(#$onlyBiologicalObjectTypeSecretesType #$Thyroid #$ThyroidHormone) <br>\n(#$onlyBiologicalObjectTypeSecretesType #$TearDuct #$LacrimalFluid)\n<p>\nWhenever it is the case that <code>(#$biologicalObjectTypeSecretesType BLO-TYPE SECRETION-TYPE)</code>, there is some type of #$SecretionEvent during which among the outputs created (see #$outputsCreated and #$outputsCreated-TypeType) are instances of <code>SECRETION-TYPE</code>, and during which only instances of <code>BLO-TYPE</code> are the doers.\n<p>\nIt is often the case that instances of <code>SECRETION-TYPE</code> can be synthesized, and thus are sometimes produced by means other than a secretion event.") :- x_cid(a65b16505eed76).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505eed76,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16505eed76,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part07.krf').
