x_comment(x_WriteFileFn,"#$WriteFileFn writes data to the specified file or input/output device.  The first argument specifies a handle to a file or I/O device (which must be created with write access).  The second argument is a pointer to the buffer containing the data to be written to the file or device.  The third argument specifies the number of bytes to be written.  The fourth (optional) argument specifies a pointer to the variable that receives the number of bytes written when using a synchronous arg1 parameter (NULL should be given as the argument here if the operation is asynchronous).  The fifth, optional argument specifies a pointer to an overlapped structure.") :- x_cid(a65b16505eedbe).
