x_comment(x_averageRateOfQuantityChange,"#$averageRateOfQuantityChange relates an instance of\n#$QuantityChangeEvent to the average rate at which the relevant quantity\nchanged during that event.  (#$averageRateOfQuantityChange <code>QUANTITY-CHANGE</code> <code>RATE</code>) can be computed by dividing the amount of change (see #$quantityChangeAmount) by the #$duration of <code>QUANTITY-CHANGE</code>.  (For any given sub-interval of the time during which <code>QUANTITY-CHANGE</code> occurs, the rate of change may be lesser or greater.)  Note that for #$DecreaseEvent instances, the #$averageRateOfQuantityChange will be negative, and for #$IncreaseEvent instances, it will be positive.") :- x_cid(a65b16505eedc0).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505eedc0,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
