x_comment(x_DynamicEquilibrium,"#$DynamicEquilibrium is a collection of events whose focal characteristic is an equilibrium in some measurable quantity (such as the temperature of the body, the amount of calcium in the bloodstream, or the fraction of poolgoers who are actually in the water), the value of which can be stated using some #$QuantitySlot.  The predicate #$equilibriumTypeWRTSlot relates a type of equilibrium to the #$QuantitySlot giving the value of the quantity in equilibrium.  Given an instance DYN of #$DynamicEquilibrium, the value of this slot S may remain unchanged or may shift, but the important characteristic of dynamic equilibria is that each has sub-events which oppose each other: one set of sub-events acts to increase the value of S and one set acts to decrease it.  Any instance DYN of #$DynamicEquilibrium has at least two cotemporal sub-events (see #$cotemporalProperSubEvents), one of which is an instance of INC and the other an instance of DEC, where INC is a class of increases in S (see #$IncreaseEvent) and DEC is a class of decreases in S (see #$DecreaseEvent).") :- x_cid(a65b16505eedcc).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505eedcc,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16505eedcc,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part07.krf').
