x_comment(x_Collision,"An instance of #$TemporalObjectType and a specialization of #$ContinuousPhysicalContactSituation and #$Translation-LocationChange.  Each instance of #$Collision is an event in which two or more #$PartiallyTangibles bump into each other.  Each instance of #$Collision is immediately preceded by an #$Approaching, during which at least one of the #$objectsInContact during the #$Collision is moving toward the location at which the collision takes place.  (Some of the objects in contact during the colliding may already be occupying that location immediately before contact.)  The #$Collision begins once the objects begin to be in contact, and ends once they are no longer in contact (think of two billiard balls bouncing off each other), <i>or</i> when the objects have come to rest in a stable contact position (think of an asteroid smashing into the earth and coming to rest at the bottom of the crater it has created).") :- x_cid(a65b16505eedf7).
