x_comment(x_FiltrationAtRenalCorpuscle,"Instances are processes in which water and small molecules pass from the #$Bloodstream into the #$BowmansCapsule of a #$Nephron.  It is the first step in the production of #$Urine (see #$UrineProduction-Mammalian).  The initial filtrate generated in this way is quite dilute and contains substances that need to stay in the body, as well as substances that should be excreted.  Subsequent steps in urine production involve the reabsorption of most of the water, selective reabsorption of certain substances to be retained, active secretion of certain substances into the urine that is forming, and finally the exit of the urine from the #$Kidney.") :- x_cid(a65b16505eee09).
