x_comment(x_BoneRemodeling,"In the vertebrate skeleton, bones are constantly being remodeled.  At multiple sites throughout the #$SkeletalSystem, specialized cells called #$Osteoclasts dissolve small regions of the extracellular matrix of bone (see #$BoneResorption).  In areas where bone has been resorbed, other cells called #$Osteoblasts secrete #$Osteoid in the gaps left. This will become mineralized, forming new bone to replace what was removed.") :- x_cid(a65b16505eee4a).
