x_comment(x_BoneResorption,"In the vertebrate skeleton, bones are constantly being remodeled.  #$BoneResorption is one part of this process, in which a small piece of the extracellular matrix of bone is dissolved.  This is typically done by #$Osteoclasts. In an area where bone has been resorbed, some time later (how long depends on the species) #$Osteoid will be laid down by #$Osteoblasts.  This will become mineralized, forming new bone to replace what was removed.") :- x_cid(a65b16505eee4d).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505eee4d,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
