x_comment(x_BoneFormationInRemodeling,"In the vertebrate skeleton, bones are constantly being remodeled.  #$BoneFormationInRemodeling is one part of this process, which occurs in an area where bone had previously been resorbed (See #$BoneResorption).  Bone formation is iniiated by #$Osteoblasts which lay down #$Osteoid (unmineralized bone matrix) in the areas which will receive the new bone.  This will become mineralized, forming new bone to replace what was removed.") :- x_cid(a65b16505eee4f).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505eee4f,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
