x_comment(x_Syncytium,"The collection of all large, multinuclear, cell-like structures filled with #$Cytoplasm.  A #$Syncytium may be a cell with many nuclei (see #$PolynuclearCell) which forms either by fusion of cells with fewer nuclei or by incomplete #$Cytokinesis, or may be also be structure composed of individual cells with interconnected cytoplasm, such as #$CardiacMuscle tissue.  In the latter, specialized cell to cell junctions allow free exchange of ions and allow the cells to function as one unit.  Note that syncytia may form by the fusion of cells which are genetically different, as occurs in fungi.") :- x_cid(a65b16505eee87).
