x_comment('x_partSynthesizesProtein-TypeType',"(#$partSynthesizesProtein-TypeType PARTTYPE PROTEINTYPE) states that instances of PARTTYPE produce portions of PROTEINTYPE biosynthetically.  PARTTYPE must be specific enough with respect to its species, stage of development, etc. so that every instance can typically be expected to synthesize PROTEINTYPE, but exceptions can apply in unusual conditions.  In the case where some gene directly codes for PROTEINTYPE, this means that instances of PARTTYPE express that gene.  Note that some kinds of protein are produced by post-translational modification.  In that case, such modifications are (typically) performed within instances of PARTTYPE.") :- x_cid(a65b16505eeed2).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505eeed2,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
