x_comment(x_cellTypeExpressesGene,"(#$cellTypeExpressesGene CELLTYPE GENE) states that instances of CELLTYPE typically produce the products of GENE via biosynthesis.  CELLTYPE must be specific enough with respect to its species, cell lineage, stage of development, etc. so that every instance can typically be expected to synthesize GENE's product.  This entails that GENE is transcribed into mRNA (see #$Transcription-DNAToRNA) and, if GENE's ultimate product is a protein, that mRNA is translated (see #$Translation-RNAToProtein) into a protein prouduct.") :- x_cid(a65b16505eeed4).
