x_comment(x_setOrCollectionSignifiedForCodeVarType,"(#$setOrCollectionSignifiedForCodeVarType VAR-TYPE SIGNIFIED-TYPE) means that when a variable VAR is declared with the #$CodeVariableType VAR-TYPE as the type specifier (see #$variableTypeSpecifier), and VAR appears in the argument list of a function call (#$actualArgumentListOfFunctionInvocation), the value assigned to VAR's position in any execution of that function call (#$argNValueAssignedFunctionCalledInExecution) will be interpreted as an input of type SIGNIFIED-TYPE for purposes of executing the function.  Among other things, this means that if the function requires an input type that is in fact disjoint with SIGNFIED-TYPE, execution of the function will end in an error condition.") :- x_cid(a65b16505eeee9).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505eeee9,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
