x_comment(x_SpecifiedPhysicalGeneType,"Each instance of #$SpecifiedPhysicalGeneType is a specialization of #$Gene-HereditaryUnit (and thus a collection of segments of DNA) comprising instances that are locationally and functionally the same, more or less. If GENE-TYPE is an instance of  #$SpecifiedPhysicalGeneType, all of its instances belong to organisms of the same species.  There may be allelic differences between the instances that render them non-identical.  More specifically, if GENE-TYPE is an instance of #$SpecifiedPhysicalGeneType, every instance of GENE-TYPE is found in nearly the same location along a #$DNAMolecule that is part of a chromosome in the cell in which it occurs, and each is found on the ''same-numbered'' chromosome in its cell. Also, the instances of GENE-TYPE have high similarity in their sequences of nucleotide base pairs. Finally, the biochemical product each instance of GENE-TYPE expresses (either a #$PeptideMolecule or an #$RNAMolecule) is substantially the same.  Note, however, that mutation and other chromosomal events might result in instances of GENE-TYPE which are broken in some way, thus violating some of these requirements.") :- x_cid(a65b16505eeefc).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505eeefc,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16505eeefc,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part07.krf').
