x_comment(x_partTypeExpressesGene,"(#$partTypeExpressesGene PARTTYPE GENETYPE) states that instances of PARTTYPE typically produce the products of GENE via biosynthesis.  If PARTTYPE is multicellular, this means that there are cells within PARTTYPE which express GENETYPE.  PARTTYPE must be specific enough with respect to its species, stage of development, etc. so that every instance can typically be expected to synthesize one or more of GENETYPE's products.") :- x_cid(a65b16505eef19).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505eef19,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
