xc_mapping_rows(a65b16505eef1a,[]).
x_comment(x_tissueTypeExpressesGene,"(#$tissueTypeExpressesGene TISSUETYPE GENETYPE) states that instances of TISSUETYPE typically produce the products of GENETYPE (a #$GeneTypeBySpeciesAndProductFamily) via biosynthesis.  This entails that GENETYPE is expressed by some of the cells in each instance of TISSUETYPE.  TISSUETYPE must be specific enough with respect to its species, stage of development, etc. so that every instance can typically be expected to synthesize one of GENETYPE's products.") :- x_cid(a65b16505eef1b).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505eef1b,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
