x_comment('x_fosters-BioProcessTypeBioProcessType',"A #$TransitiveBinaryPredicate that relates types of biological processes to other types of biological processes, where instances of the latter types are fostered by instances of the former types. <code>(#$fosters-BioProcessTypeBioProcessType P-TYPE1 P-TYPE2)</code> means that the kind of #$Situation <code>P-TYPE1</code> fosters the kind of #$Situation <code>P-TYPE2</code>.  Fostering is a looser relation than causation: if <code>P-TYPE1</code> causes <code>P-TYPE2</code> (#$causes-SitTypeSitType), it certainly fosters it; but a situation-type can foster another without being a cause of it.  While it isn't necessarily the case when <code>(#$fosters-BioProcessTypeBioProcessType P-TYPE1 P-TYPE2)</code> that the occurrence of an instance of <code>P-TYPE1</code> is typically associated with the occurrence of an instance of <code>P-TYPE2</code>, it will be the case that the occurrence of an instance of <code>P-TYPE1</code> is one of the most promising ways of bringing about an occurrence of an instance of <code>P-TYPE2</code>.") :- x_cid(a65b16505eef8c).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505eef8c,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16505eef8c,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part07.krf').
