x_comment(x_functionCallYieldsNthArgumentOfFunctionCall,"(#$functionCallYieldsNthArgumentOfFunctionCall SUPER-CALL N SUB-CALL) means that SUB-CALL is a #$ComputerFunctionInvocation-Executable that is used to give the value which is supplied as the Nth parameter value for the function called in super-call.  More specifically, it means that the specification of SUPER-CALL is such that whatever value which is returned by the #$codingFunctionInvoked in SUB-CALL on the #$actualArgumentListOfFunctionInvocation supplied to SUB-CALL is specified as the Nth argument value for the function called (the #$codingFunctionInvoked in SUPER-CALL.  #$functionCallYieldsNthArgumentOfFunctionCall is the corresponding predicate (#$functionCorrespondingPredicate-Canonical) of #$FunctionCallForNthArgumentOfFunctionCallFn.") :- x_cid(a65b16505eef8f).
