x_comment(x_positivelyDependsOn,"(#$positivelyDependsOn SET DEP-PRED INDEP-PRED) means that the second arguments to DEP-PRED are positively dependent on those for INDEP-PRED, when elements of ?SET appear in the arg1 position.  In other words, given the range of bindings for DEP-VAL and INDEP-VAL in (#$and (#$elementOf X SET)(DEP-PRED X DEP-VAL) (INDEP-PRED X INDEP-VAL)), whenever INDEP-VAL is high for a particular X, DEP-VAL will also be high and whenever INDEP-VAL is low, DEP-VAL will be low.   Unlike the more general #$positivelyCorrelatedWith, #$positivelyDependsOn means that there is some causal link from INDEP-PRED affecting arg2 values for ?DEP-PRED.  See also #$dependsOn-Pairwise.") :- x_cid(a65b16505eef94).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505eef94,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16505eef94,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part07.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16505eef94,16302).
