x_comment(x_playsRoleInTypeWithFrequency,"(#$playsRoleInTypeWithFrequency THING EVENT-TYPE ROLE FREQ) means that THING (or instances of THING, if THING is a collection) plays ROLE in instances of EVENT-TYPE at the rate FREQ.  For example,\n<p>\n(#$playsRoleInTypeWithFrequency #$Cheerleader #$Cheering #$performedBy #$Daily)\n</p>\nmeans that cheerleaders cheer on a daily basis.  Similarly,\n<p>\n(#$playsRoleInTypeWithFrequency  (#$SubcollectionOfWithRelationToFn (#$GameFn #$CollegeFootball-CW) #$competingAgents (#$CollegeFootballTeamFn #$UniversityOfTexasAtAustin)) #$CollegeFootballSeason #$properSubEventTypes #$Weekly)\n</p>\nmeans that games involving the Texas Longhorns football team occur weekly throughout any college football season.  Also,\n<p>\n(#$playsRoleInTypeWithFrequency #$BarackObama (#$GameFn #$Basketball-TheGame) #$participatingPlayers #$Weekly)\n</p>\nmeans that Barack Obama plays basketball weekly.\n<p>\nThis predicate ahs two significant typed specializations, #$playsRoleInTypeWithFrequency and #$typePlaysRoleInTypeWithFrequency (qq.v).") :- x_cid(a65b16505eef97).
