x_comment(x_CollectionOfValuesForFunctionFn,"#$CollectionOfValuesForFunctionFn is a collection denoting function that takes an individual denoting function, a collection, TYPE, and an integer representing an arg position of the function, ARG-NUM, to the collection of values returned by FUNCTION by the instances of TYPE in ARG-NUM.  For instance, (#$CollectionOfValuesForFunctionFn #$GovernmentFn  #$City  1) denotes the subcollection of the range of #$GovernmentFn such that each corresponding element in the domain is an instance of #$City -- i.e. the collection of city governments.  For binary or higher arity functions, the other argument places are not restricted.  E.g.,  (#$CollectionOfValuesForFunctionFn #$StreetNamedFn #$MetropolitanArea  1) refers to the collection of streets in instances of #$MetropolitanArea  while (#$CollectionOfValuesForFunctionFn #$StreetNamedFn (StringOfMaximumLengthFn 6) 2) is the collection of streets that can be referred to by strings with a maximum length of 6.  In set-theoretic terms, for any FUNCTION, COLL, NUM (#$CollectionOfValuesForFunctionFn FUNCTION COLL NUM) denotes the maximal subcollection of the range of COLL such that every NUMth element in the domain of FUNCTION is an instance of COLL.") :- x_cid(a65b16505eeff1).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505eeff1,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16505eeff1,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part07.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16505eeff1,16432).
