x_comment(x_BoneFormation,"The collection of events in which bone (hard, mineralized tissue) is formed.  Bone can be formed during the growth and development of #$Vertebrates (see #$BoneFormationDuringGrowth).  It also forms during healing of injuries to bones (see #$BoneFormationInFractureRepair).  Bone forms during the ongoing process of skeletal remodeling (see #$BoneFormationInRemodeling). Finally, bone can form in places where it shouldn't, in response to disease or injury (see #$EctopicBoneFormation).\n<p>\nBone formation is one part of a complex process resulting in the production of a mature instance of #$Bone-BodyPart, such as a particular #$Femur or #$Clavicle.  For that process, see #$BoneBodyPartGrowthAndDevelopment.") :- x_cid(a65b16505ef014).
