x_comment('x_inRooted-PassesThrough',"Assume for the sake of explanation that the orientation of OBJ1 is vertical.  Given that, (#$inRooted-PassesThrough OBJ1 OBJ2) means that OBJ1 in is embedded into OBJ2 in such a way so that the top of OBJ1 is sticks out from the top surface of OBJ2 and the bottom of OBJ1 is sticks out from the bottom surface of OBJ2.  If OBJ1 were to be removed from OBJ2, a hole that goes completely through OBJ2 would be present.  This entails that the length of OBJ1 is greater than the thickness or height of OBJ2.  For example, consider a nail that is put completely through a board.  In that case, the nail would be #$inRooted-PassesThrough the board.") :- x_cid(a65b16505ef058).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505ef058,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16505ef058,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part07.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16505ef058,16540).
xc_kb_names(a65b16505ef058,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16505ef058,[]).
x_comment('x_in-RootedCompletelyFlush',"Assume for the sake of explanation that the orientation of OBJ1 is vertical.  Given that, (#$in-RootedCompletelyFlush OBJ1 OBJ2) means that OBJ1 in is embedded into OBJ2 in such a way so that the top of OBJ1 is flush with the top surface of OBJ2 and the bottom of OBJ1 is flush with the bottom surface of OBJ2.  If OBJ1 were to be removed from OBJ2, a hole that goes completely through OBJ2 would be present.  If (#$connectedPerpendicularlyTo OBJ1 OBJ2) also holds, then the length of OBJ1 is equal to the thickness or height of OBJ2.  For example, consider a nail that is put completely through a board.  If you were to snip the bottom and the top of the nail flush with the bottom and the top of the board, respectively, then the resulting nail portion would be #$in-RootedCompletelyFlush in the board.") :- x_cid(a65b16505ef059).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505ef059,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
