x_comment(x_relationBetweenQuantitySlotsForObjectTypes,"(#$relationBetweenQuantitySlotsForObjectTypes OBJ-TYPE1 OBJ-TYPE2 BIN-PRED SLOT-1 COMP-PRED-1 SLOT-2 COMP-PRED-2 ) means that when INST-1 and INST-2 (instances of OBJ-TYPE1 and OBJ-TYPE2 respectively) stand in BIN-PRED such that (BIN-PRED INST-1 INST-2), then when the values for SLOT-1 for INST-1 COMP-PRED-1 (are greater, less, etc.) then the values for SLOT-2 for INST-2 will be COMP-PRED-1 (greater, less, etc.).  For example if a wing of an airplane is rigidly connected to the fuselage (#$connectedTo-Rigidly), then if the altitude of the fuselage goes up, then the altitude of the wing will go up -- (#$relationBetweenQuantitySlotsForObjectTypes #$AirplaneFuselage  #$AirplaneWing #$connectedTo-Rigidly #$altitudeAboveGround #$greaterThan #$altitudeAboveGround #$greaterThan).") :- x_cid(a65b16505ef05f).
