x_comment(x_QPQuantityFn,"<code>(#$QPQuantityFn SCALAR-QUANT-TYPE)</code> is a\nfunction-denoting function which returns a temporally qualifiable function when given a specialization of #$ScalarQuantity as an argument. <code>((#$QPQuantityFn SCALAR-QUANT-TYPE) THING)</code> is the quantity of <code>SCALAR-QUANT-TYPE</code> that <code>THING</code> has, whether or not that quantity is measured or even measurable.  For example, ((#$QPQuantityFn #$Mass) #$EiffelTower) denotes a mass: namely, the mass of the Eiffel Tower.  Functions denoted by #$QPQuantityFn are typically used in conjunction with #$valueOf (q.v.). For example, (#$valueOf ((#$QPQuantityFn #$Mass) #$EiffelTower) (#$MetricTon 10100)) is true.") :- x_cid(a65b16505ef11f).
