x_comment(x_isaConstraintForQuantityBasedFormulaSlot,"(#$isaConstraintForQuantityBasedFormulaSlot QBF QUANTITY COLL) means that the thing standing in arg1 of the slot associated with quantity when applying QBF must be an instance of COLL.  If the quantity is implictly restricted to certain types of entities, then COLL = that type.  E.g. If (#$unitSlotsForFormula QBF (#$AreaFn (#$The #$RightTriangle)) #$areaOfObject), then (#$isaConstraintForQuantityBasedFormulaSlot QBF (#$AreaFn (#$The #$RightTriangle)) #$RightTriangle).  If the quantity type is unrestricted, then the thing standing in arg1 of the associated slot must satisfy the relevant #$arg1Isa constraints of that slot --  e.g. if (#$unitSlotsForFormula QBF (#$The #$Area) #$areaOfObject), then (#$isaConstraintForQuantityBasedFormulaSlot QBF (#$The #$Area) #$PolyDimensionalThing).") :- x_cid(a65b16505ef151).
