x_comment(x_ExampleAntecedentFormulaForEquationFn,"(#$ExampleAntecedentFormulaForEquationFn QBF QUANTITY) denotes a characteristic sentence that objects mapped to the example instances involved must meet in order for the equation to be applicable in the context of QBF an instance of #$QuantityBasedFormula.  The QUANTITY argument denotes the quantity on the left hand side of the equation (a lone quantity that is the first argument to a #$numericallyEquals formula) that acts as a filter to filter out the quantity attribution which would end up in the consequent of a rule constructed with the resulting formula.  For example, the result of evaluating (#$ExampleAntecedentFormulaForEquationFn QBF (#$The #$Area)) where the equation associated with QBF is (#$The #$Area) = (#$The #$Length) x (#$The #$Width), would be the following conjunction (#$and (#$lengthOfObject (#$The #$SpatialThing) (#$The #$Length)) (#$widthOfObject (#$The #$SpatialThing) (#$The #$Width))).") :- x_cid(a65b16505ef1bc).
