x_comment(x_RenalAbsorptionFromGlomerularFiltrate,"Instances are processes in which substances are selectively re-absorbed from the pro-urine, or initial filtrate, during urine production.  Urine production is a two stage process: first, fluid is removed from the #$Bloodstream via simple filtration (see #$FiltrationAtRenalCorpuscle).  This step is not very selective; essentially all molecules below a certain size are allowed to enter the kidney.  As the pro-urine moves through the #$Nephron and collecting ducts, various substances are absorbed back into the #$Bloodstream through a variety of means, some active and some passive.") :- x_cid(a65b16505ef1c6).
