x_comment(x_BinaryCompositionPredicateFn,"<code>(#$BinaryCompositionPredicateFn PRED-1 PRED-2)</code> designates the binary predicate that is the composition of the binary predicates <code>PRED-1</code> and <code>PRED-2</code>. \n<p>\n<code>((#$BinaryCompositionPredicateFn PRED-1 PRED-2) X Z)</code> is true if and only if there is something, <code>Y</code>, such that <code>(PRED-1 X Y)</code> and <code>(PRED-2 Y Z)</code>. For example, ((#$BinaryCompositionPredicateFn #$mother #$nameString) #$GeorgeWBush \"Barbara Bush\"), since (#$mother #$GeorgeWBush #$BarbaraBush) and (#$nameString #$BarbaraBush \"Barbara Bush\"). The function corresponding to this predicate is #$predicateIsPredicateCompositionOf.") :- x_cid(a65b16505ef1fb).
