x_comment('x_coefficientOfFriction-Kinetic',"When two surfaces are in contact and relative motion, the frictional resistance is almost uniform over a wide range of low speeds.  This resistance is characterized by the kinetic coefficient of friction.  The kinetic coefficient is typically less than the coefficient of static friction (see #$coefficientOfFriction-Static). <code>(#$coefficientOfFriction-Kinetic OBJ1 OBJ2 NUM)</code> means that <code>NUM</code> is the ratio of the frictional resistance force (see #$FrictionVector) to the normal force which presses the surfaces of <code>OBJ1</code> and <code>OBJ2</code> together.  See also #$coefficientOfFriction") :- x_cid(a65b16505ef264).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505ef264,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
