x_comment(x_intendedConsequenceTypeOfSubEventType,"<code>(#$intendedConsequenceTypeOfSubEventType EVENT-TYPE SUB-EVENT-TYPE ROLE1 INTENDED-EVENT-TYPE ROLE2)</code> means that during an instance <code>EVENT</code> of <code>EVENT-TYPE</code>, if an instance <code>SUB-EVENT</code> of <code>SUB-EVENT-TYPE</code> is a sub-event of <code>EVENT</code>, whatever plays <code>ROLE1</code> in <code>SUB-EVENT</code> is indended to play the role <code>ROLE2</code> in an instance of <code>INTENDED-EVENT-TYPE</code>.  For example, (#$intendedConsequenceTypeOfSubEventType #$KillingThroughPoisoning #$Poisoning #$bodilyDoer #$Dying #$doneBy) means that during a killing by poisoning event, whoever is poisoned is also intended to die.") :- x_cid(a65b16505ef358).
