x_comment(x_areaOfSmallestFlowXZCrosssection,"(#$areaOfSmallestFlowXZCrosssection OBJ AREA) means that AREA is the area of the smallest XZ cross-section area associated with OBJ that would impede the flow of something (e.g. a fluid, a signal, etc.).  For objects not connected to other objects whose length from side to side at each point along the X, Y, or Z axes is the same, this is equivalent to the area of the XZ crosssection of the object itself.  For objects connected to another object at the top or bottom (along the Y axis) of the XZ axes, this area is the area of the smallest XZ crossection of the associated joint of the connected objects.  For the purposes of this relation the X axis is defined as the width of an object when the length is the vertical Y axis.  The Z axis would then be its depth.  For objects with no intrinsic orientation (e.g. a portion of rubber tubing), by fiat the Y axis is the axis associated with its longest side.") :- x_cid(a65b16505ef3b9).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505ef3b9,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
