x_comment(x_GenericCausationPredicate,"The subcollection of #$CausationPredicate whose instances serve to relate causes (or cause-types) to effects (or effect-types) without any further semantic entailment as to how the causation comes about, whether it is indirect or direct, how likely the effect-type is to come about as a consequence of a cause (or cause-type), etc.  A canonical example is #$causes-SitTypeSitType, which relates to situation-types in a generic cause/effect way.  A canonical counter-example is #$pathogenCausesCondition, which relates a physiological condition to a pathogen that is responsible for that condition by virtue of how it interacts with its host.  #$GenericCausationPredicate is a #$completelyAssertedCollection.") :- x_cid(a65b16505ef408).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505ef408,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
