x_comment(x_equationPermutations,"(#$equationPermutations EQUATION PERMUTATION) means that PERMUTATION is an equivalent form of EQUATION that consists of an equality statement (using #$numericallyEquals) that has some term involved in EQUATION in the \"left hand side\".  For example, if EQUATION = (#$numericallyEquals AREA (#$TimesFn LENGTH WIDTH)), then values for PERMUTATION would include (#$numericallyEquals LENGTH (#$QuotientFn AREA WIDTH)), (#$numericallyEquals WIDTH (#$QuotientFn AREA LENGTH)).  Note that when EQUATION is itself an equality statement with exactly one term in the \"left hand side\", EQUATION is itself a valid value for PERMUTATION.") :- x_cid(a65b16505ef434).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505ef434,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
