x_comment('x_substanceInducesProteinMolecule-TypeType',"(#$substanceInducesProteinMolecule-TypeType SUBSTANCETYPE PROTEINTYPE) states that, in some unspecified cellular environment, quantities of SUBSTANCETYPE trigger or speed up the biosynthesis of PROTEINTYPE.  That is to say that there is some cellular situation in which the presence of SUBSTANCETYPE causes the initiation or the increase in transcription of the gene or genes coding for PROTEINTYPE and the subsequent translation of mRNA to produce PROTEINTYPE, or to produce a precursor of the protein that is then post-translationally modified to result in PROTEINTYPE.") :- x_cid(a65b16505ef4db).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505ef4db,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
