x_comment(x_functionTypePredictsPointFromPoints,"(#$functionTypePredictsPointFromPoints   FUNC-TYPE THING DEP-VALUE1 INDEP-VALUE1 DEP-VALUE2 INDEP-VALUE2 DEP-VALUE3 INDEP-VALUE3) means that a function of type FUNC-TYPE predicts that, given that that the quantitative value of something is the dependent DEP-VALUE1 when it has the corresponding independent value INDEP-VALUE1, and is VALUE2 when it has the corresponding INDEP-VALUE2, the quantitative value will be VALUE3 when it has the corresponding INDEP-VALUE3.\n<p>\nFor example, the independent values might be dates, and the dependent values might be stock prices.  In that case, (#$functionTypePredictsPointFromPoints FUNC-TYPE STOCK VALUE1 DATE1 VALUE2 DATE2 VALUE3 DATE3) would mean that a function of type FUNC-TYPE predicts that the value of STOCK will be VALUE3 on DATE3, given that it is  VALUE1 on DATE1 and VALUE2 on DATE2.") :- x_cid(a65b16505ef4e1).
