x_comment(x_SubQuantityFromSlotFn,"<code>(#$SubQuantityFromSlotFn SLOT)</code> denotes the collection of quantities that are the quantities measured by SLOT.  The resulting quantity type will be a subcollection of the #$arg2Isa of the quantity slot in arg1 of this function.  Note that although the results of this function are often extensionally equivalent to the #$arg2Isa quantity type of the slot, these collection are useful ways to distinguish collections of quantities based on intensional features such as the relationship used to attribute the quantity.  E.g. it is useful to distinguish the gate voltage (#$SubQuantityFromSlotFn #$gateVoltageToSource) from the drain voltage (#$SubQuantityFromSlotFn  drainVoltageToSource).") :- x_cid(a65b16505ef599).
