x_comment(x_relationBetweenQuantitySlotsForColl,"(#$relationBetweenQuantitySlotsForColl  COLL QUANT-PRED-1 COMP-PRED-1 QUANT-PRED-2 COMP-PRED-2 THING) means that instances of COLL whose values for QUANT-PRED-1 are COMP-PRED-1 (more, less, etc.) than those values for other instances of COLL are associated with correspondingly COMP-PRED-2 (more, less, etc.) values for QUANT-PRED-2 relative to THING.  THING is often a collection of slots that must remain constant for the relationship to hold (Note these slots may be filled by the same or a different object).  For example, a rectangle with a greater length than another rectangle has a greater area all other things being equal (#$relationBetweenQuantitySlotsForColl  #$Rectangle #$lengthOfObject #$greaterThan #$areaOfObject #$greaterThan (#$TheCollection #$lengthOfObject #$areaOfObject #$heightOfObject))") :- x_cid(a65b16505ef5b1).
