x_comment(x_silkNAF,"A unary #$KBDependentRelation (q.v.) that takes instances of #$CycLSentence as arguments.  <code>(#$silkNAF SENTENCE)</code> means that <code>SENTENCE</code> is not currently \"known\" by the Cyc system to be true.  More precisely, the inference engine cannot prove <code>SENTENCE</code> using all possible inference capabilities and the current state of the knowledge base.  This predicate corresponds to the \"naf\" operator in the SILK langage. <code>SENTENCE</code> might actually be known to be false, or its truth-value might be simply unknown in the present sense.  <p>Note that, as a KB dependent relation, #$silkNAF is #$notAssertible (q.v.).") :- x_cid(a65b16505ef64b).
