x_comment(x_rHsOfFormulasHasOperatorAtDepth,"(#$rHsOfFormulasHasOperatorAtDepth QBF RHS LHS OPERATOR DEPTH DEPTH-ARG DEPTH-ARG-NUM) means that the quantity based formula QBF has the RHS and LHS associated with its #$equationFormFor (either a directly asserted formula or a permutation -- #$equationPermutations).  Furthermore, the RHS has OPERATOR at DEPTH and DEPTH-ARG is one of the non-operator arguments at that depth in DEPTH-ARG-NUM place.  DEPTH is represented as an integer.  A DEPTH of 1 means that the argument and associated operator are direct arguments of the RHS.  A DEPTH of 2 means that that OPERATOR and DEPTH-ARG are arguments to an argument of the RHS.  Note that by convention the LHS is always a single depth term.") :- x_cid(a65b16505ef64e).
