x_comment(x_GProteinMolecule,"A important specialization of #$EnzymeMolecule.  A #$GProteinMolecule functions as a molecular implementation of a boolean, which is either 'on' or 'off' depending on whether it is bound to a #$GuanosineDiphosphate (GDP) or a #$GuanosineTriphosphate (GTP) (hence the name 'G-Protein').  If it is 'on', i.e., activated, a #$GProteinMolecule is able to in turn catalyze additional reactions of a particular class in a cellular transduction pathway.  #$GProteinMolecules play important roles in human vision and olfactory systems.") :- x_cid(a65b16505ef6a4).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505ef6a4,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
