x_comment(x_many,"An instance of #$GeneralizedQuantifier.  <code>(#$many SETORCOL1 SETORCOL2)</code> means that many things are instances of both <code>SETORCOL1</code> and <code>SETORCOL2</code>.  What counts as \"many\" can vary greatly with context; thus it is difficult to give this quantifier a precise definition.  However, we can pin down certain of its logical features, e.g.:\n<pre>\n(#$transitiveViaArg #$many #$subsetOf 2).\n</pre>\nIt is also important to note that #$many is the contradictory predicate (see #$contradictoryPreds) of #$few (q.v.).") :- x_cid(a65b16505ef71b).
