x_comment(x_instanceMaximizedWithRespectToTopLevelInstancesOfType,"(#$instanceMaximizedWithRespectToTopLevelInstancesOfType SIT SUBSIT-TYPE) means that SIT properly subsumes as many 'unembedded' instances of SUBSIT-TYPE as the situation context allows (where 'unembedded' means that for each instance of SUBSIT-TYPE subsumed, there is not other instance of SUBSIT-TYPE that subsumes it and that SIT in turn subsumes - see #$topLevelInstanceOfTypeInSit).  Specifically, if SIT is an instance of SIT-TYPE, and it is known that (#$maximalNumberOfTopLevelInstancesOfTypeInSitType SIT-TYPE SUBSIT-TYPE N), then from (#$instanceMaximizedWithRespectToTopLevelInstancesOfType SIT SUBSIT-TYPE) it follows that there are exactly N instances SUBSIT of SUBSIT-TYPE such that (#$topLevelInstanceOfTypeInSit SIT SUBSIT-TYPE SUBSIT).") :- x_cid(a65b16505ef72e).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505ef72e,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
