x_comment(x_HomologousChromosomePair,"The collection of all homologous pairs of chromosomes.  Each #$HomologousChromosomePair consists of two #$EukaryoticChromosomes that are parts of the same #$Cell, contain genes for the same proteins, and whose DNA sequences are, though not identical, substantially similar to each other.  The members of a #$HomologousChromosomePair, like any chromosome in a eukaryotic cell, will be #$UnduplicatedChromosomes at the beginning of #$InterphaseOfEukaryoticCellCycle, and #$DuplicatedChromosomes at the end of #$InterphaseOfEukaryoticCellCycle. During #$ProphaseI of #$Meiosis, the two members of the pair will join together to form a #$Tetrad-Chromosomal.") :- x_cid(a65b16505ef762).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505ef762,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
