x_comment(x_arg7Genl,"A binary #$ArgGenlPredicate (q.v.).  <code>(#$arg7Genl RELN COL)</code>  means that semantic well-formedness requires that anything given as the seventh argument to <code>RELN</code> must be a subcollection of <code>COL</code>.  That is,  <code>(RELN ARG1 ARG2 ARG3 ARG4 ARG5 ARG6 ARG7 ...)</code> is semantically well-formed only if <code>(#$genls ARG7 COL)</code> holds.  For an explanation of semantic well-formedness, see  #$CycLExpression-Assertible and its specializations.  See #$argGenl for a  similar but more flexible ternary predicate.") :- x_cid(a65b16505ef763).
