x_comment(x_DisjointMedicalSituationType,"An instance of #$SiblingDisjointCollectionType.  This is the collection of medical situation types that are sibling disjoint with each other.  Note: this collection should not include all surgical procedure types even those thought to be \"natural\" kinds because some procedure types share instances with others even though they don't stand in a genls relationship.  E.g.\n\n<pre>\n   (#$SubcollectionOfWithRelationToTypeFn #$HeartValveProcedure-Surgical #$objectActedOn #$AorticValve)</pre> \n\nis not a specialization of #$HeartValveRepair-SurgicalProcedure   -- there are aortic valve procedures that are not repairs.  but clearly the two collections are not disjoint.<br><br>\n\nIn cases like the example above, one should assert as instances of DisjointSurgicalProcedureType those collections which will give the greatest coverage without falsehood and assert individual disjointness assertions to cover any gaps.") :- x_cid(a65b16505ef78a).
