x_comment(x_plausibleQueryPredicateVariablizedArgPositionWithMacro,"A predicate used to generate plausible questions from text. <code>\n(#$plausibleQueryPredicateVariablizedArgPositionWithMacro BINARY-PRED BINARY-PRED-ARG-POSITION RULE-MACRO)</code> means that in the question-suggestion context at hand, it is reasonable to suggest a query of the form <code>(RULE-MACRO BINARY-PRED ARG3 ARG4)</code>, where <code>PRED-ARG-POSITION</code> designates, by reference to the argument-positions defined for <code>BINARY-PRED</code>, the argument position in which a variable appears.  For example, <code>\n(#$plausibleQueryPredicateVariablizedArgPositionWithMacro #$likesAsFriend 1 #$relationAllExists)</code> means that <code>(#$relationAllExists #$likesAsFriend ?WHO #$BillClinton)</code> is a plausible question in the question-suggestion context at hand.") :- x_cid(a65b16505ef790).
