x_comment(x_constraintVersionOf,"(#$constraintVersionOf KNOWLEDGE-PRED CONSTRAINT-PRED) means that CONSTRAINT-PRED is the \"constraint\" correlate to KNOWLEDGE-PRED in the operative context.  This means that unlike KNOWLEDGE-PRED whose assertion in a context means that the described relationship holds, the assertions of CONSTRAINT-PRED in a context means that it a condition of model validity or model goodness, etc. that the described relationship holds, but there is no assumption that it in fact holds.  This predicate faciliates the conversion of KNOWLEDGE-PRED assertions in some strong assumptions Mt -- an Mt that describes an ideal situation or model, to the domain Mt where they are interpreted as constraints on the model as opposed to a description of how the model actually is.") :- x_cid(a65b16505ef866).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505ef866,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
