xc_mapping_rows(a65b16505ef866,[]).
x_comment(x_idealWorldMicrotheoryMt,"(#$idealWorldMicrotheoryMt IDEAL-MT CONSTRAINT-MT) means that IDEAL-MT has declarative statements that describe an ideal situation, model, or graph in the sense that its statements describe relationships that would hold in the \"best case\" or only in valid models, etc. CONSTRAINT-MT is a real world/model constraint MT where the ideal statements in IDEAL-MT have been converted into constraints in the model via #$constraintVersionOf.  E.g. if (#$constraintVersionOf PRED CONSTRAINT-PRED) holds in CONSTRAINT-MT and (#$idealWorldMicrotheoryMt IDEAL-MT CONSTRAINT-MT), then assertions of the form (ist IDEAL-MT (PRED ARG1, ... ARGN)) can be automatically converted into assertions of the form (ist CONSTRAINT-MT (CONSTRAINT-PRED ARG1, ... ARGN)).") :- x_cid(a65b16505ef867).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505ef867,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
