x_comment(x_incompatibleMemoryManagementFunctions,"Where FN and COMP-FN are #$complementaryMemoryManagementFunctions, (#$incompatibleMemoryManagementFunctions FN COMP-FN) means that if the member of the pair which is a #$MemoryAllocationFunction is used in a program to allocate a block of memory, using the complementary member of the pair (the #$MemoryDeallocationFunction) to deallocate that same block of memory in the same program will create a specification such that executions of the program will be liable to a number of #$UndesirableProgramActions, with types including #$ProgramActionWitoutInternalTerminationProvision, #$DataCorruption-ProgramAction, and #$ArbitraryCodeExecution.") :- x_cid(a65b16505ef89d).
