x_comment(x_setOfFirstDerivativePointsBasedOnSetOfPoints,"<code>(#$setOfFirstDerivativePointsBasedOnSetOfPoints SET-OF-POINTS FUNCTION-TYPE SET-OF-DERIVATIVE-POINTS)</code> means that if one takes <code>SET-OF-POINTS</code> and generates a curve <code>C</code> from it using an instance of <code>FUNCTION-TYPE</code>, then <code>SET-OF-DERIVATIVE-POINTS</code> is the set of points on the first derivative of <code>C</code> with respect to the values of the points in <code>SET-OF-POINTS</code>.  For example, <code>(#$setOfFirstDerivativePointsBasedOnSetOfPoints (#$TheSet (#$The2DPoint A B) (#$The2DPoint C D)) #$CubicSpline 2  (#$TheSet (#$The2DPoint P B) (#$The2DPoint Q D)))</code> would mean <code>(#$TheSet (#$The2DPoint P B) (#$The2DPoint Q D))</code> are points on the line defined by the equation for the first derivative with respect to Y (i.e. the arg 2 value of #$The2DPoint) of the curve produced by cubic spline interpolation on <code>(#$TheSet (#$The2DPoint A B) (#$The2DPoint C D))</code>.") :- x_cid(a65b16505ef8a4).
