x_comment(x_MapFunctionOverListUntil,"This function applies a unary (evaluatable) function <code>F</code> to each element in a given list <code>L</code> until the input satisfies a certain test condition, at which point the list of results (up to and including the result of the succesfull input) is returned.  If no element of <code>L</code> satisfies the test condition, no value is returned.<p>\nFor example, asking:\n<pre>  \n  (#$evaluate ?VAR        \n     (#$MapFunctionOverListUntil #$SquaredFn (#$TheList 1 2 3 4 5)                                   \n                                 (#$Kappa (?X) (#$greaterThan (#$SquaredFn ?X) 7))))\n</pre>\nwill return the binding (#$TheList 1 4 9) for <code>?VAR</code>, because applying #$SquaredFn to 1 yields 1, which is less than 7, applying $SquaredFn to 2 yields 4, which is also less than 7, but applying #$SquaredFn to 3 yields 9, which is greater than 7.  Since applying #$SquaredFn to 3  yields a result that satisfies the test condition, it is not necessary to calculate the result of applying #$SquaredFn to 4 or 5.  Instead, upon applying #$SquaredFn to 3 and determining that the result passes the test condition, the function evaluation halts and returns (#$TheList 1 4 9) as a binding for <code>?VAR</code>.\n<p>\nC.f. the similar function #$MapFunctionOverListUntilResult.") :- x_cid(a65b16505ef8b0).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505ef8b0,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16505ef8b0,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part07.krf').
