x_comment(x_SituationTopicSetFn,"(#$SituationTopicSetFn SET PRED-SET) denotes the situation type in which all of the members of SET stand in some relationship (or an instance of the member does) to some predicate in PRED-SET and the corresponding situations are importantly linked to each other (often by one of the preds in PRED-SET).  For example, (#$SituationTopicSetFn (#$TheSet #$Horse #$Person) (#$TheSet #$transporter #$on-Physical)), strictly speaking, denotes the collection of situations in which a horse plays some role either on something or being ridden or as the transporter in an event and a person is either a transporter or either on something or something is on him and these individuals and the situations they are in are linked in some important but unspecified way.  There typically will be a useful subset of that collection of situations as many will be highly unlikely --  A man being the transporter in an event where the horse is riding him is one of those unlikely instances of this -- that can be generated through additional assertions on the collection.") :- x_cid(a65b16505ef912).
