x_comment(x_CellularSignalToResponseProcessTypeFn,"A #$CollectionDenotingFunction used for representing important specializations of #$CellularCommunication.  Where SIGNAL-TYPE is a specialization of an 'organism-wide' dispersal of a substance composed of instances of some kind of signal molecule such as #$EpinephrineMolecule (said dispersal type will often be represented using #$IntercellularMediumReleaseOfChemicalObjectTypeFn) and RESPONSE-TYPE is a kind of cellular level response (a specialization of #$BiologicalProcess-CellularLevel), (#$CellularSignalToResponseProcessTypeFn SIGNAL-TYPE RESPONSE-TYPE) denotes the collection of all instances of #$CellularCommunication which begin with an instance of SIGNAL-TYPE and conclude with many cells undergoing a response of RESPONSE-TYPE.") :- x_cid(a65b16505ef93c).
