x_comment('x_statementOutputsToStatement-Transitive',"This is the transitive generalization of #$statementOutputsDirectlyToStatement.  (#$statementOutputsToStatement-Transitive OUTPUTS INPUTS) means that OUTPUTS and INPUTS are both part of a common #$ComputerProgram-CWIS with a control structure such that between OUTPUTS and INPUTS there is discernable one or more specified 'hand-offs' in which a value is passed from one statement to the next in virtue of the outputting statement specifying an operation that ends with the value being attached to a certain expression, while the inputting statement specifies some use of that value via a reference to the same expression.  In other words, (#$statementOutputsToStatement-Transitive OUTPUTS INPUTS) means that OUTPUTS and INPUTS are both part of a program with at least one possible execution thread such that executing INPUTS will involve using a value determined by a chain of operations, one of which is specified by OUTPUTS.  Note that this does not entail that the same expression is used throughout the chain of operations, or that a single value is transmitted as a constant through the chain, or that the dependency obtains for every possible execution of the program.") :- x_cid(a65b16505ef941).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505ef941,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
