x_comment(x_IonChannel,"Each instance of #$IonChannel is a #$ProteinMoleculeOrProteinComplex that naturally occurs as part of the membranes living cells and is involved in regulating the voltage gradient across the plasma membrane.  Ion channels form aqueous pores through lipid, hydrophobic biological membranes (the #$CellMembrane as well as those of certain #$Organelles), through which various #$Ions can pass.  #$IonChannels are usually specific for particular types of ions.  Some #$IonChannels are open all the time, while others can open and close in response to stimuli such as a change in cell potential (see #$VoltageGatedIonChannel), the binding of a signal molecule (see #$LigandGatedIonChannel), temperature changes, and other stimuli.") :- x_cid(a65b16505ef9e7).
