x_comment('x_IntervalTypeBetweenFn-Inclusive',"A binary function that takes two instances of #$ConventionallyClassifiedTimeIntervalSeries and returns the collection of #$ConventionallyClassifiedTimeIntervalSeries whose instances are the continuous time intervals between the starting point of instances of the first argument to the ending point of the next occurring instance of the second argument.  E.g. (#$IntervalTypeBetweenFn-Inclusive (#$TimeOfWeekFn #$Monday #$TimeOfDay-10AM) (#$TimeOfWeekFn #$Tuesday #$TimeOfDay-11AM)) denotes the collection of continuous time intervals that start on the first moment of a Monday at 10am and run through the last moment of the 11th hour of the next occurring Tuesday.  Note that if all instances of one interval type of either argument subsume some instance of the interval type of the other, the result is reduced to the subsuming type E.g. if the first argument is #$Monday and the second is #$TimeOfDay-11AM, the result is equivalent to #$Monday since every Monday subsumes some instance of #$TimeOfDay-11AM.  This is required by the intended interpretation that the instances of each returned interval type are all the same length and subsume some instance of each of the arguments.  The function is undefined for arguments for which there is no corresponding continuous interval type calculable according this definition.") :- x_cid(a65b16505efac2).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505efac2,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16505efac2,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part07.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16505efac2,19441).
xc_kb_names(a65b16505efac2,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16505efac2,[]).
x_comment('x_VendorHardwareModel-Specification',"A subcollection of #$ComponentConfigurationSpecification.  Each instance of This collection is a specification that outlines the allowable components and configurations of a particular procurable component  -- that is, it provides the legal builds that you can specify from the vendor.  Typically these are provided by the vendor.  For example, some instances of #$VendorHardwareModel-Specification provide the legal builds for certain computer servers.  In that case, the fully specified server that is procured from the vendor is an instantiation of one of these specifications.  This is disjoint with #$HardwareComponentSpecification which are specifications that specify additional configuration details that are post vendor delivery and relate to the particular role the component will play in the system in which it is installed.") :- x_cid(a65b16505efac3).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505efac3,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16505efac3,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part07.krf').
