x_comment(x_MRFluentProperty,"The following comment is from #$MRSharedOntology as defined in OWL. \n\n<blockquote> A fluent property (e.g., hasSpouse) is a function that when applied to appropriate arguments results in a term that is a fluent.  For example, the fluent property hasSpouse is a function that when applied to arguments of type person results in a fluent, e.g., has Spouse(PersonA, PersonB). \n<p>         \nInformally, one often talks about a fluent property as a predicate that when applied to arguments results in a sentence with a truth value.  Such common usage is, strictly speaking, incorrect.  Nevertheless, this usage is reflected in our making Fluent a subclass of GeneralizedStatement and FluentProperty a subclass of GeneralizedProperty, which facilitates using such tools as the Protege ontology browser.</blockquote>\n\n") :- x_cid(a65b16505efad2).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505efad2,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16505efad2,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part07.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16505efad2,19457).
xc_kb_names(a65b16505efad2,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16505efad2,[]).
