x_comment(x_mrMaximallyHoldsThroughout,"An instance of both #$TemporalPredicate and #$ModalPredicate that is used to state that a given sentence is true at every moment during some #$TimeInterval, but not true throughout any other larger, containing time interval.  <code>(#$mrMaximallyHoldsThroughout SENT INTERVAL)</code> means that <code>SENT</code> is true all throughout <code>INTERVAL</code>, and for any other interval <code>LARGER-INTERVAL</code> that properly contains <code>INTERVAL</code>, <code>SENT</code> is not true throughout it. This predicate is a mirror of the #$owl:ObjectProperty, maximallyHoldsThroughout, in the #$MR2011Ontology.  Although the intent of this predicate is to have instances of #$TimeInterval as arg2, the digested document content we will need to import may have other sorts of things in that argument position, so the second argument is left lightly constrained.") :- x_cid(a65b16505efb0d).
