x_comment(x_mrClippedBackward,"An instance of both #$TemporalPredicate and #$ModalPredicate that is used to state that a given sentence is true all throughout some #$TimeInterval, but was not true before it.  <code>(#$mrClippedBackward SENT INTERVAL)</code> means that <code>SENT</code> is true throughout <code>INTERVAL</code>, but is not true at the time point immediately preceding <code>INTERVAL</code>. This predicate is a mirror of the #$owl:ObjectProperty, clippedBackward, in the #$MR2011Ontology.  Although the intent of this predicate is to have instances of #$ContinuousTimeInterval as arg2, the digested document content we will need to import may have other sorts of things in that argument position, so the second argument is left lightly constrained.") :- x_cid(a65b16505efb0e).
