x_comment(x_mrMinimallyHoldsWithin,"An instance of both #$TemporalPredicate and #$ModalPredicate that is used to state that a given sentence is true during at least part of some #$TimeInterval, but not true during part of some smaller, contained interval. <code>(#$mrMinimallyHoldsWithin SENT INTERVAL)</code> means that <code>SENT</code> is true during a period contained by <code>INTERVAL</code>, and for any other smaller interval, <code>SMALL-INTERVAL</code>, if it is properly contained by <code>INTERVAL</code>, <code>SENT</code> is not true during at least some part of <code>SMALL-INTERVAL</code>. This predicate is a mirror of the #$owl:ObjectProperty, minimallyHoldsWithin, in the #$MR2011Ontology.  Although the intent of this predicate is to have instances of #$ContinuousTimeInterval as arg2, the digested document content we will need to import may have other sorts of things in that argument position, so the second argument is left lightly constrained.") :- x_cid(a65b16505efb10).
