x_comment(x_mrOccursOver,"An instance of #$TemporalPredicate that is used to state that a given event occurs during some #$TimeInterval.  <code>(#$mrOccursOver EVENT INTERVAL)</code> means that <code>EVENT</code> happens thoughout <code>INTERVAL</code>. This predicate is a mirror of the #$owl:ObjectProperty, occursOver, in the #$MR2011Ontology.  Although the intent of this predicate is to have instances of #$TimeInterval as arg2, the digested document content we will need to import may have other sorts of things in that argument position, so the second argument is left lightly constrained.\n<p>\nThe comment from the OWL ontology file follows: \n<p>\noccursOver(Event, TimeInterval) is true if Event occurs over TimeInterval.  When Event is solid, this means that Event occurs over no interval I such that I properly contains TimeInterval.  When Event is liquid, Event may also occur over such an interval I.") :- x_cid(a65b16505efb12).
