x_comment(x_MRGeneralizedStatement,"Supporting vocabulary for Erudite's Machine Reading project. The following comment is from nary.owl. <blockquote> A logical statement with a predicate and one or more arguments.  Only the subclasses of GeneralizedStatement are intended to be instantiated. Every subclass C of GeneralizedStatement should (in a conforming implementation) be an instance of the metaclass StatementClass [see #$MRStatementClass].  The predicate of an instance of C is accessible via nary:predicate or (when all instances of C are intended to share a common predicate) via C's property hasStatementClassPredicate.  Each subclass C is to have an arity (greater than zero) determined by the number of hasStatementClassArgumentAccessor property values specified for C.  The arguments of an instance of any given GeneralizedStatement subclass C may be accessed via C's hasStatementClassArgumentAccessor property.  A given GeneralizedProperty P should have at least one argument. In contrast to rdf:Statement (and rdf:Property), any argument may be literal-valued (e.g., string-valued).</blockquote>") :- x_cid(a65b16505efb39).
