x_comment('x_evolutionarySuccessor-SitType',"<code>(#$evolutionarySuccessor-SitType SITTYPE1 SITTYPE2)</code> states that the type of #$Situation, <code>SITTYPE2</code>, arose through the process of evolution from the type of #$Situation, <code>SITTYPE1</code>.  For example, some surmise that #$EukaryoticCellDivision evolved from #$ProkaryoticCellDivision.   Any  relationship between instances of <code>SITTYPE1</code> and instances of <code>SITTYPE2</code> is indirect and separated by long periods of time, so that e.g., today's prokaryotic cell divisions have no evolutionary relationship to today's eukaryotic cell divisions.  Rather, if that hypothesis is correct, prokaryotic cell divisions occurring a very long time ago changed gradually over many generation as genetic material of those organisms changed, eventually taking on the characteristics of eukaryotic cell division.") :- x_cid(a65b16505efbd2).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505efbd2,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
