x_comment('x_inheritRolePlayersOfType-SubSitTypeToSomeStepOfMajorStep',"(#$inheritRolePlayersOfType-SubSitTypeToSubSitType  SIT-TYPE SUBSIT-TYPE1 ROLE1 SUBSIT-TYPE2 ROLE2 TYPE) means that if SIT-TYPE is such that (#$properSubSituationTypes SIT-TYPE SUBSIT-TYPE1) and (#$properSubSituationTypes SIT-TYPE SUBSIT-TYPE2), and (#$isa SIT SIT-TYPE), and (#$isa SUB1 SUBSIT-TYPE1) and (#$isa SUB2 SUBSIT-TYPE2) and (#$subSituations SIT SUB1) and (#$subSituations SIT SUB2), then for any INST such that (#$isa INST TYPE) and such that (ROLE1 SUB1 INST), (ROLE2 SUB2 INST).  The vernacular sense of the predicate is that, in a situtation type featuring SUBSIT-TYPE1 and SUBSIT-TYPE2 as #$properSubSituationTypes, whatever instance of TYPE plays ROLE1 in the sub-situation that is an instance of SUBSIT-TYPE1 in an instance of the situation type also plays the role ROLE2 in the instance of SUBSIT-TYPE2.") :- x_cid(a65b16505efbe0).
