x_comment('x_inheritRolePlayersOfType-SubSitTypeToSomeStepOfMajorStep',"An instance of #$RuleMacroPredicate used to tersely represent/reason about role-inheritance relations at a high-level of description.\n<code>(#$inheritRolePlayersOfType-SubSitTypeToSomeStepOfMajorStep SCRIPT SIT-TYPE ROLE1 MAJOR-STEP ROLE2 TYPE)</code> means that objects of type <code>TYPE</code> that play the role <code>ROLE1</code> in events of type <code>SIT-TYPE</code> that are scenes in an instance of <code>SCRIPT</code> will also play the role <code>ROLE2</code> in some #$subEvents of <code>MAJOR-STEP</code>, a \"major step\" of <code>SCRIPT</code>.  To be a major step in this context is to be part of a specified decomposition of <code>SCRIPT</code> into stages, via the #$coveringOfEventType relation.  As such, <code>(#$inheritRolePlayersOfType-SubSitTypeToSomeStepOfMajorStep SCRIPT SIT-TYPE ROLE1 MAJOR-STEP ROLE2 TYPE)</code> is equivalent to \n<code>(#$inheritRolePlayersOfType-SubSitTypeToSubSitType  SCRIPT SIT-TYPE ROLE1 MAJOR-STEP SUB-EVENT-ROLE2 TYPE)</code> with the additional constraints that <code>(#$roleHasSubEventsVersion ROLE2 SUB-EVENT-ROLE2)</code> and <code>(#$thereExists ?DECOMPOSITION (#$and (#$coveringOfEventType SCRIPT ?DECOMPOSITION) (#$memberOfList MAJOR-STEP ?DECOMPOSITION)))</code>.") :- x_cid(a65b16505efbe9).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505efbe9,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16505efbe9,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part07.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16505efbe9,19766).
