x_comment(x_nearestRequiredActorSlots,"<code>(#$nearestRequiredActorSlots EVT-TYPE ACTOR-SLOT)</code> means that the instance <code>ACTOR-SLOT</code> of #$ActorSlot has a value for every instance of the event-type <code>EVT-TYPE</code> (hence, <code>(#$requiredActorSlots EVT-TYPE ACTOR-SLOT)</code> holds), but that it is a \"nearest\" such actor slot -- i.e., though there may be a proper generalization of <code>ACTOR-SLOT</code> that is also required for <code>EVT-TYPE</code>, there are no proper specializations of <code>ACTOR-SLOT</code> that are required.  Hence querying for the values of <code>ACTOR-SLOT</code> will result in a list of actor-slots that, given Cyc's current state of understanding, will be sufficient for specifying all of the actors in a given instance of <code>EVT-TYPE</code>.") :- x_cid(a65b16505efc2e).
