x_comment(x_seat,"<code>(#$seat SITTING SEATING-DEVICE)</code> identifies <code>SITTING-DEVICE</code> as the instance of #$SeatingDevice that being used normally as a seat in <code>SITTING</code>, an instance of #$SittingOnSomething.  That is, not only is <code>SEATING-DEVICE</code> the #$supportingObject, but the #$SeatingDeviceSeat of <code>SEATING-DEVICE</code> is occupied by the animal sitting.  Not that not every instance of #$SittingOnSomething will have a #$seat, though it will have a #$supportingObject (e.g., sitting on the floor, sitting on the arm of a chair, etc.).") :- x_cid(a65b16505efccd).
