x_comment(x_connectedByFactSet,"<code>(#$connectedByFactSet SET-OF-THINGS SET-OF-SENTENCES)</code> means that the facts (represented as CycLSentences) in <code>SET-OF-SENTENCES</code> jointly serve to relate the elements of <code>SET-OF-THINGS</code>.  For example, <code>(#$connectedByFactSet (#$TheSet #$KevinBacon #$HerbertRoss) (#$TheSet (#$movieActors #$Footloose-TheMovie #$KevinBacon) (#$movieDirectors #$Footloose-TheMovie #$HerbertRoss)))</code> means that Kevin Bacon and Herbert Ross are connected by the chain: Kevin Bacon acted in <i>Footloose</i>, which Ross directed.  See also #$relatedToVia.") :- x_cid(a65b16505efcde).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505efcde,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16505efcde,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part07.krf').
