x_comment(x_PathSurface,"The collection of all path surfaces, the part of a #$Path-Customary where the actual movement along the path ordinarily or is intended to take place, and by virtue of which the path is considered to be a path.  For example a given #$Highway may have any number of parts, such as layers of concrete, dirt, and gravel, or steel beams and support columns in places where the highway is raised.  But only the road surface of the highway is where one would customarily travel when using the highway as a path.  Similarly, a blood vessel is a path, but it is the inner surface of the vessel where the flow of blood normally takes place, not the outer surface.") :- x_cid(a65b16505efd09).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505efd09,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16505efd09,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part07.krf').
