xc_mapping_rows(a65b16505efd09,[]).
x_comment(x_motionFocallyInvolvesPathSurfacesOf,"<code>(#$motionFocallyInvolvesPathSurfacesOf MOVEMENT OBJECT)</code> means that <code>MOVEMENT</code>, an instance of #$Movement-TranslationEvent, is a movement focally involving the use of <code>OBJECT</code>, an instance of #$PathArtifact, as a #$motionPathway-Partial, where that use consists, in large part, of sub-events in which one or more instances of #$PathSurface that are a physical part of <code>OBJECT</code> play the role of #$motionPathway-Complete.  Positive examples include the use of a ramp to perform a bicycle or skateboard jump, which involves riding up the ramp surface; and walking up a staircase, which requires stepping on the top-surface of one or more steps.  A negative example would be jumping down from the top of a ramp or from the top of a staircase.") :- x_cid(a65b16505efd0a).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505efd0a,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
