x_comment(x_Standing,"The collection of events in which the #$bodilyDoer is an animal that is supporting its own weight by standing on at least one extended leg. To count as standing, the event must be a continuous standing, and not a translocation via ambulation, nor an event in which one remains in place but moves ones legs so as to temporarily remove support (such as hopping up and down and jogging in place).  A borderline case of standing would be a gradual replacement of one leg (or set of legs) in the supporting role with another leg (or set of legs), while support is constantly maintained and while remaining in place.  One can still be standing with assistance, (such as using a cane or holding a rail), so long as the assistance does not entirely replace the support provided by the legs.  To represent a non-supporting \"standing,\" such as an astronaut in zero-gravity who appears to be standing, use the more general (#$InPositionFn #$UprightPosture).  To represent a motionless standing, use the more specific #$StandingStill.") :- x_cid(a65b16505efd22).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505efd22,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
