x_comment(x_ShapingSubtractively,"A collection of #$PurposefulActions; a subcollection of #$ShapingSomething. In each #$ShapingSubtractively, an agent intentionally forms some piece of solid material into a different shape by removing one or more #$physicalPortions of the #$objectActedOn.  The intended product may be a new kind of thing (as when, during sewing, one cuts out a sleeve piece from a piece of fabric), or it may merely be shorter (as when one cuts off the bottom of a flower stem when arranging a bouquet) or smoother (as when one sands a piece of furniture) than the original.  In all cases the final product will be less massive than, but made out of the same material as, the original.") :- x_cid(a65b16505efd3c).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505efd3c,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16505efd3c,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part07.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16505efd3c,20120).
xc_kb_names(a65b16505efd3c,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16505efd3c,[]).
x_comment(x_CuttingInPieces,"The collection of all cutting events [#$CuttingSomething] which are composed of repeated cuttings in which there is a complete separation [#$Separation-Complete].  As a result, several (or many more) distinct connected objects are created.  The pieces may be of similar or vastly dissimilar size.  For example, instances of #$DrillingSomething and #$SawingSomething have important subevents which are instances of #$CuttingInPieces, since small pieces (e.g. sawdust) are removed from the larger piece.") :- x_cid(a65b16505efd3d).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505efd3d,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16505efd3d,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part07.krf').
