x_comment(x_ProjectTypeFn,"<code>(#$ProjectTypeFn ACTIVITY-TYPE)</code> denotes a class of actions, each instance of which is a complete project composed primarily of subevents which are instances of <code>ACTIVITY-TYPE</code>.  For example, (#$ProjectTypeFn #$Sewing) is the class of actions in which a whole sewing project is finished.  Instances of #$Sewing might merely be steps in some larger #$MakingSomething event, and have no finished product as their #$outputsCreated.  Instances of (#$ProjectTypeFn #$Sewing), however, typically have an (intended) output which is a completed garment, a finished surgical suture, a completed quilt, or some other final artifact created mostly by sewing.") :- x_cid(a65b16505efd4e).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505efd4e,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16505efd4e,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part07.krf').
