x_comment(x_CircularSawBlade,"The collection of blades for many types of #$PowerSaws.   Each is relatively flat and circular in shape.  A hole at the center allows the blade to be mounted on the arbor of the saw, which transmits the spinning force from the motor to the blade when the saw is turned on.  When optimized for cutting wood or plastic, blades will be made of #$Steel and have teeth all around the perimeter.  Blades optimized for cutting metal may be made of an abrasive composite material that is gradually worn away as the blade is used.  Blades optimized for cutting masonry may be made of steel, but have an abrasive coating at the cutting edge.  Many configurations of rotary blades exist. ") :- x_cid(a65b16505efd64).
