x_comment(x_Backsaw,"A type of #$HandSaw.  The teeth of a #$Backsaw are angled back toward the handle of the saw, so that the saw cuts on the pull stroke.  The blades of #$Backsaws are typically thinner and stiffer than blades of other #$HandSaws, because the tension created when pulling on the blade keeps it straight and unbent.  Backsaws may have a stiffening spine of thicker metal opposite the cutting edge, but not all do; some have cutting teeth on both edges.") :- x_cid(a65b16505efd69).
