x_comment(x_generateIsaRuleForSubcollectionInvolving,"(#$generateIsaRuleForSubcollectionInvolving  PRED) means that when PRED occurs in arg2 of one of the four main ternary subcollection functions (#$SubcollectionOfWithRelationFromTypeFn, #$SubcollectionOfWithRelationFromFn, #$SubcollectionOfWithRelationToTypeFn, #$SubcollectionOfWithRelationToFn), an expansion rule concluding to #$isa and that function term and the appropriate collection backchain required meta information should be asserted onto the subcollection.  Typically this is only asserted onto binary predicates that cannot be solved by removal only -- e.g. require SKSI or transformation.") :- x_cid(a65b16505efd90).
