x_comment(x_characteristicSuperEventTypes,"A specialization of #$superEventTypes, <code>(#$characteristicSuperEventTypes EVT-TYPE SUPER-EVT-TYPE)</code> means that events of type <code>EVT-TYPE</code> are characterized by virtue of being sub-events of an overarching instance of <code>SUPER-EVT-TYPE</code>.  That is, a common-sense characterization or description of an event of type <code>EVT-TYPE</code> would (as a default) involve mentioning its belonging to <code>SUPER-EVT-TYPE</code> sub-events.  For example, while both of the following sentences are true,<p><code>(#$superEventTypes #$ConditioningBeer #$Brewing)</code></p> <p><code>(#$superEventTypes #$ConditioningBeer #$IntelligentAgentActivity)</code></p> only #$Brewing is such that it is characteristic of #$ConditioningBeer in the relevant sense, and so <p><code>(#$characteristicSuperEventTypes #$ConditioningBeer #$Brewing)</code>.</p> holds.") :- x_cid(a65b16505efdc9).
