x_comment(x_SewingPattern,"Instances of this collection are groups of outlines and other information, typically printed on tissue paper, that show the shape of the parts that can be cut out of sheet-like material, such as fabric, and assembled to make a completed textile artifact.  The user of the pattern lays out each pattern piece on the fabric to be used, affixing them with pins, and uses them as a guide to cut each piece out of the fabric with scissors. Additional information may be present on a pattern piece, such as fold lines, stitching lines, button locations, center line of the body, etc. ") :- x_cid(a65b16505efdcf).
