x_comment(x_SewingPatternPiece,"Each instance of this collection is the outline, typically printed on tissue paper, of one type of part that can be cut out of sheet-like material, such as fabric, and assembled with other parts to make a completed textile artifact.  Given a particular pattern piece of a particular design, that piece may be used to cut several parts that will make up the whole.  For example, a collar piece may be used to cut the top surface of the collar, the bottom surface, and the interfacing.  Additional information may be present on a pattern piece, such as fold lines, stitching lines, button locations, center line of the body, etc. ") :- x_cid(a65b16505efdd6).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505efdd6,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
