x_comment('x_Interfacing-Cloth',"The collection of all cloth that is either a) intended to be used as interfacing, or b) is serving as interfacing.  Interfacing is used to stiffen parts of textile products, such as the collars and waistbands of garments. It is generally hidden, sandwiched between layers of the main fabric the item is made of.  Although often an interfacing piece is created from fabric intended to be used for that purpose, it is possible to use any stiff fabric as interfacing.") :- x_cid(a65b16505efdd8).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505efdd8,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
