x_comment(x_PotentialEnergy,"Potential energy is stored energy. It is the energy embodied in an object or system by virtue of its position or arrangement of its parts. In mechanical terms, the potential energy of an object is a measure of the work that had to be expended to bring the object from a ground state to another state. For example, the work performed to raise a block with mass, <code>m</code>, a fixed height, <code>h</code>, above the ground increases the potential energy of the block by the quantity <code>m*g*h</code>, where <code>g</code> is the acceleration due to gravity. See also #$PotentialEnergyFunction.") :- x_cid(a65b16505efe13).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505efe13,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16505efe13,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part07.krf').
