x_comment(x_HeterotrophicNutrientAssimilation,"A specialization of #$BiologicalEnergyTransferEvent.  Each instance of #$HeterotrophicNutrientAssimilation is a process in which a single organism acquires energy and carbon in the form of organic compounds made by some other organism.  There are a variety of ways of doing so.  Heterotrophic micro-organisms may live in the bodies of hosts and absorb some of the host's organic molecules, or they may acquire such molecules from dead organisms or shed parts.  #$Animals may eat and then digest the entire bodies of other organisms, or their parts (e.g., instances of #$Leaf) or their products (e.g., #$Milk). ") :- x_cid(a65b16505efe17).
