x_comment(x_OrganismNutrientAssimilation,"A specialization of #$BiologicalEnergyTransferEvent.  Each instance of #$OrganismNutrientAssimilation is the process in which a single organism acquires energy and converts it into energy-containing organic molecules needed for life.  Every organism is doing this, either continuously or repeatedly throughout its life.  Some organisms (#$Autotrophs) are able to create energy-containing molecules from inorganic raw materials through the use of #$SolarEnergy or #$ChemicalEnergy.  Others (#$Heterotrophs) must consume energy-containing carbon compounds created by another organism.  There may be periods in an organism's life when it gets energy from stored reserves, such as the seed and early seedling stages of a #$PhotosyntheticPlant, before it is able to perform photosynthesis.") :- x_cid(a65b16505efe2c).
