x_comment(x_frequencyOfPartTypePerArea,"A predicate for stating the frequency or density with which a type of #$PartiallyTangible is present as a part of some other #$PartiallyTangible, as a function of its area. Specifically, <code>(#$frequencyOfPartTypePerArea OBJ PARTTYPE AREAFREQUENCY)</code> states that <code>OBJ</code> has instances of <code>PARTTYPE</code> as parts, and they are distributed over the surface of <code>OBJ</code> at a frequency of <code>AREAFREQUENCY</code>.  For example, (#$frequencyOfPartTypePerArea Leaf001 #$Chloroplast ((#$PerFn (#$UnitOfCountFn #$Chloroplast) (#$UnitProductFn (#$Milli #$Meter) (#$Milli #$Meter))) 1000) states that Leaf001 has 1000 #$Chloroplasts for each square millimeter of its area.") :- x_cid(a65b16505efe39).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505efe39,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
