x_comment(x_RollingOnASurface,"A specialization of #$Motion-SolidAgainstSolid (q.v.).  Each instance of #$RollingOnASurface is a process of moving along a surface in which the #$objectMoving rotates while it translates.   For example, what a car's tires do when the car is being driven is an instance of #$RollingOnASurface.  Points on the #$objectMoving become flush with (see #$flushSurfaces) the #$motionPathway-Complete for a brief period (depending on speed, diameter, surface rolled on, deformability of roller, and pressure) and then move perpendicularly away as the object moves along.  The #$objectMoving in a #$RollingOnASurface moves along the surface without #$Sliding-Generic.") :- x_cid(a65b16505efe81).
