x_comment(x_mtForField,"<code>(#$mtForField MT FIELD)</code> means that <code>MT</code>, an instance of #$TheoryMicrotheory and #$GeneralMicrotheory, is the most general microtheory appropriate for representing the propositions distinctive to <code>FIELD</code>, a #$FieldOfStudy.  A field may have many sub-fields, and the distinctive propositions of those sub-fields (which may be mutually inconsistent or incommensurable) should not go in the #$mtForField for the \"parent\" field, but in more specialized #$mtForField microtheories for the specific sub-fields.") :- x_cid(a65b16505efead).
