x_comment(x_partwiseDisjoint,"<code>(#$partwiseDisjoint I1 I2)</code> means that <code>I1</code> and <code>I2</code> do not share any parts. I.e., there are no individuals <code>I</code> such that <code>(#$parts I1 I)</code> and <code>(#$parts I2 I)</code>.  For example (#$partwiseDisjoint #$Alaska-State #$Italy) is true because there is no instance of #$Individual that is a #$parts of both #$Alaska-State and #$Italy.  Similarly, an event during which Barack Obama brushes his teeth is #$partwiseDisjoint with an event during which John McCain brushes his teeth, even if they occur simultaneously: neither of these #$BrushingOnesTeeth events shares a part with the other.") :- x_cid(a65b16505efeb0).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505efeb0,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
