x_comment(x_PeptideMoleculeTypeByPeptideFamily,"A type-level collection. Each instance is a collection PEPTIDE-MOL-FAMILY of #$PeptideMolecules characterized by the fact that all of its instances are molecules derived by transcribing (see #$Transcription-DNAToRNA) and optionally translating (see #$Translation-RNAToProtein) a segment of DNA (an instance of #$Gene-HereditaryUnit) which is a physical instantiation (see #$instantiationOfGene-GIS) of an instance of some #$GeneTypeByProductFamily. Note that instances of each PEPTIDE-MOL-FAMILY are actual #$PeptideMolecules, but they are not necessarily all identical.  Sources of variation are as follows: a) Instances of this collection are collections of molecules created in the cells of organisms belonging to different species.  They are grouped together because they share most of their amino acid sequences and are presumably descended from common \"ancestor peptides\". b) Alternative splicing occurs frequently.  This means that the same segment of DNA can produce RNA that is spliced (see #$RNASplicingProcess) in different ways to produce messenger RNAs that code for very different proteins.  However, even within a single species, each of these splice variants shares large subregions containing identical amino acid sequences.") :- x_cid(a65b16505eff13).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505eff13,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16505eff13,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part07.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16505eff13,20604).
xc_kb_names(a65b16505eff13,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16505eff13,[]).
x_comment(x_GeneTypeByProductFamily,"A collection of collections of #$GeneticInformationStructures. Each instance GIS-TYPE of this collection is often called a \"gene family.\"  Genes that share nucelotide sequences are often grouped into families, and these familes can and do cross species lines.  If the genes in an instance of #$GeneTypeByProductFamily encode peptides, there will be a corresponding instance of #$PeptideMoleculeTypeByPeptideFamily that those peptide molecules are instances of.  ") :- x_cid(a65b16505eff14).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505eff14,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16505eff14,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part07.krf').
