x_comment(x_FilteringOfSolarRadiationByEarthsAtmosphere,"An instance of #$TemporalStuffType and a specialization of #$ElectromagneticRadiationFilteringProcess.  Each instance of #$FilteringOfSolarRadiationByEarthsAtmosphere is an event in which some instance of #$SolarRadiation passes through a portion of #$TheEarthsAtmosphere.  Radiation that penetrates will typically have a different #$IrradianceDistribution than the entering radiation, because some #$wavelengths have been absorbed (see #$ElectromagneticRadiationAbsorption) by the molecules that make up the atmosphere.  The deeper radiation penetrates, the more is absorbed. ") :- x_cid(a65b16505eff8f).
