x_comment(x_PhotonAbsorption,"A specialization of #$AbsorptionEvent.  Instances are events in which a single quantum of #$ElectromagneticRadiation (a #$Photon) is absorbed by a #$ChemicalObject.  Rather than being destroyed, the energy is converted to a different form, depending on the #$wavelength (and thus energy embodied) of the #$Photon.  For example, #$Photons of #$VisibleLight typically are captured as an increase in the excitation state of an electron in the #$ChemicalObject. ") :- x_cid(a65b16505eff99).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505eff99,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
