x_comment('x_complementaryPreds-Incapability',"(#$complementaryPreds-Incapability INST-CAP-PRED TYPE-INCAP-PRED) means that INST-CAP-PRED is the #$CapabilityPredicate-InstanceLevel that complements the #$IncapabilityPredicate-TypeLevel TYPE-INCAP-PRED.  An instance-level capability predicate restricts its first argument to #$Individuals, whereas a type-level incapability predicate restricts its first argument to #$Collections.  What makes the two predicates complementary is that the second predicate is a way of stating incapacity for types such that the capacity involved is expressed at the instance level using the first.") :- x_cid(a65b16505effa6).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505effa6,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
