x_comment(x_TypeIncapableFn,"TypeIncapableFn takes an instance-level #$CapabilityPredicate and returns a type-level predicate that is used to state the corresponding INcapability for selected collections.  That is, where CAP-PRED is a #$CapabilityPredicate-InstanceLevel, and SIT-TYPE and ROLE are, respectively, a situation type and role that are admitted arg2 and adimitted arg 3 for CAP-PRED, ((#$TypeIncapableFn CAP-PRED) AGENT-TYPE SIT-TYPE ROLE) means that there is NO instance INST of AGENT-TYPE such that (CAP-PRED INST SIT-TYPE ROLE).  Thus, for example, ((#$TypeIncapableFn #$behaviorCapable) #$FlightlessBird #$Flying #$bodilyDoer) means that no #$FlightlessBird is #$behaviorCapable of playing the role of #$bodilyDoer in #$Flying events.") :- x_cid(a65b16505effa7).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505effa7,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
