x_comment(x_typeIncapable,"The corresponding predicate (#$functionCorrespondingPredicate-Canonical) of #$TypeIncapableFn.  (#$typeIncapable CAP-PRED TYPE-INCAP-PRED) means that TYPE-INCAP-PRED is a type-level predicate that is used to state the INcapability complementing CAP-PRED for selected collections.  That is, where CAP-PRED is a #$CapabilityPredicate-InstanceLevel, and SIT-TYPE and ROLE are, respectively, a situation type and role that are admitted arg2 and adimitted arg 3 for CAP-PRED, (typeIncapable CAP-PRED TYPE-INCAP-PRED) means that TYPE-INCAP-PRED is a predicate such that (TYPE-INCAP-PRED AGENT-TYPE SIT-TYPE ROLE) means there is NO instance INST of AGENT-TYPE such that (CAP-PRED INST SIT-TYPE ROLE).") :- x_cid(a65b16505effa8).
