x_comment(x_partTypeSupportsCapability,"Where TYPE-CAP-PRED is the type-level #$correspondingPreds-Capability of CAP-PRED, (#$partTypeSupportsCapability PART-TYPE CAP-PRED SIT-TYPE ROLE) means that, for any type of system SYSTEM-TYPE such that (#$functionallyImportantPhysicalPartTypeOfWholeType SYSTEM-TYPE PART-TYPE), (TYPE-CAP-PRED SYSTEM-TYPE SIT-TYPE ROLE). Intuitively, (#$partTypeSupportsCapability PART-TYPE CAP-PRED SIT-TYPE ROLE) means that PART-TYPE supports the ability to play ROLE in situations of type SIT-TYPE in any type of system where instances of PART-TYPE are important functional components. Thus, e.g., (#$partTypeSupportsCapability Heart behaviorCapable (CirculationFn Blood) bodilyDoer) means that #$Hearts support systems that include them as important functional components (e.g. Vertebrates) in being #$bodilyDoer of (#$CirculationFn Blood), and logically entails that ((#$TypeCapableFn #$behaviorCapable) #$Vertebrate (#$CirculationFn #$Blood) #$bodilyDoer), provided (#$functionallyImportantPhysicalPartTypeOfWholeType #$Vertebrate #$Heart) is known or provable.") :- x_cid(a65b16505effb0).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505effb0,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16505effb0,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part07.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16505effb0,20762).
xc_kb_names(a65b16505effb0,[]).
