x_comment(x_partTypeSupportsCapabilityInType,"Where TYPE-CAP-PRED is the type-level #$correspondingPreds-Capability of CAP-PRED, (#$partTypeSupportsCapabilityInType PART-TYPE CAP-PRED SIT-TYPE ROLE AGT-TYPE) means that, if there is systemtype SYSTEM-TYPE such that (#$functionallyImportantPhysicalPartTypeOfWholeType SYSTEM-TYPE PART-TYPE) and (#$genls AGT-TYPE SYSTEM-TYPE), then (TYPE-CAP-PRED AGT-TYPE SIT-TYPE ROLE).Intuitively, (#$partTypeSupportsCapabilityInType PART-TYPE CAP-PRED SIT-TYPE ROLE AGT-TYPE) means that instances of PART-TYPE are functionally integrated into all instances of some parent class of AGT-TYPE, but that instances of PART-TYPE support an ability in instances of AGT-TYPE to play ROLE in instances of SIT-TYPE that is not necessarily shared by all instances of the parent class.") :- x_cid(a65b16505effb1).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505effb1,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
