x_comment(x_paulingElectronegativityOfType,"<code>(#$paulingElectronegativityOfType ELEMENT-TYPE POSNUM)</code> states that the type of element, <code>ELEMENT-TYPE</code>, has an electronegativity of <code>POSNUM</code> on the Pauling scale (a unitless scale).  This value is a measure of how strongly atoms of that type attract #$Electrons (or electron density). In a #$ChemicalInteractions between atoms of differing electronegativities, typically the one that is an instance of the type with the higher value will attract electrons more strongly.  However, for a particular #$Atom, actual electronegativity increases at higher oxidation states (when the atom has partially or completely donated electron(s) to a neighboring chemical object).") :- x_cid(a65b16505effd7).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505effd7,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16505effd7,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part07.krf').
