x_comment(x_coveringOfEventType,"<code>(#$coveringOfEventType EVT-TYPE LIST-OF-EVT-TYPES)</code> means that:  <p> (1) for each instance <code>EVT</code> of <code>EVT-TYPE</code>, there exists some instance of each element of <code>LIST-OF-EVT-TYPES</code> that is a proper sub-situation of <code>EVT</code>;  <p> (2) there is no further sub-situation of <code>EVT</code> that is not spatiotemporally subsumed by some instance of some element of <code>LIST-OF-EVT-TYPES</code>; <p> (3) an instance of the first element of <code>LIST-OF-EVT-TYPES</code> starts at the starting of <code>EVT</code>; <p> (4) after the first element of <code>LIST-OF-EVT-TYPES</code>, each subsequent element of <code>LIST-OF-EVT-TYPES</code> is such that the instance of it that is a sub-event of <code>EVT</code> starts after the start of the instance of the prior element in <code>LIST-OF-EVT-TYPES</code> that is a sub-event of <code>EVT</code>.   <p> Thus, for example, consider the claim (#$coveringOfEventType #$NFLSeason (#$TheList #$NFLPreSeason #$NFLRegularSeason #$NFLPostSeason)).  This means that (#$properSubEventTypes #$NFLSeason #$NFLPreSeason), (#$properSubEventTypes #$NFLSeason #$NFLRegularSeason and (#$properSubEventTypes #$NFLSeason #$NFLPostSeason).  Further, for any instance of #$NFLSeason <b>NFL-Season-001</b>, there is no sub-event of <b>NFLSeason-001</b> that is not spatiotemporally subsumed by some instance of some element of (#$TheList #$NFLPreSeason #$NFLRegularSeason #$NFLPostSeason)).  It also entails that there is an instance of #$NFLPreSeason, <b>NFLPreSeason-001</b>, that is the first proper sub-situation of <b>NFLSeason-001</b> .  Finally, it entails that some instance  <b>NFLRegularSeason-001</b> of  #$NFLRegularSeason is a proper sub-event of  <b>NFLSeason-001</b> which starts after the start of <b>NFLPreSeason-001</b>, and  some instance  <b>NFLPostSeason-001</b> of  #$NFLPostSeason is a proper sub-event of  <b>NFLSeason-001</b> which starts after the end of <b>NLRegularSeason-001</b>.") :- x_cid(a65b16505f001b).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505f001b,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16505f001b,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part07.krf').
