x_comment(x_perRatioCol,"The corresponding predicate\n(#$functionCorrespondingPredicate-Canonical) of #$PerRatioColFn.  Where NUMERATOR-TYPE and DENOMINATOR-TYPE are both instances of\n#$InterconvertibleUnitType, (#$perRatioCol NUMERATOR-TYPE\nDENOMINATOR-TYPE COL) means that COL is the collection of all scalar quantities that can be represented as a\nratio where the numerator is measured by units of the first type and\nthe denominator is measured by units of the second type.  Thus,\ne.g. (#$PerRatioColFn #$UnitOfMoney #$UnitOfVolume) would represent\nthe collection of all quantities measuring a unit of money per unit\nvolume, such as ((#$PerFn #$Dollar-UnitedStates #$Barrel-UnitOfVolume) 108),\n((#$PerFn #$Ruble-Russia #$Liter) 100), ((#$PerFn #$Rupee-Nepal\n#$Gallon-Imperial) 52.8), and so on. ") :- x_cid(a65b16505f0042).
