x_comment(x_metaphorFoundedOnSimilarity,"<code>(#$metaphorFoundedOnSimilarity METAPHOR  BASIS-SENTENCE THING-SENTENCE)</code> means that the metaphor <code>METAPHOR</code> is applicable because of the the similarity between the basis and that to which the metaphor applies that is expressed by the pair of sentences <code>BASIS-SENTENCE</code> (about the basis) and <code>EXTENDED-SENTENCE</code>.  In general, <code>BASIS-SENTENCE</code> and <code>EXTENDED-SENTENCE</code> will differ only in that <code>BASIS-SENTENCE</code>mentions the metaphor's basis where <code>EXTENDED-SENTENCE</code> mentions that to which <code>METAPHOR</code> is applicable.  Cf. #$metaphorGroundsOutInFacts.") :- x_cid(a65b16505f0055).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505f0055,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16505f0055,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part07.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16505f0055,20945).
xc_kb_names(a65b16505f0055,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16505f0055,[]).
x_comment(x_metaphorGroundsOutInFacts,"<code>(#$metaphorGroundsOutInFacts METAPHOR BASIS-SENTENCE THING-SENTENCE1 ... )</code> means that the metaphor <code>METAPHOR</code> is applicable because of a similarity between the basis and that to which the metaphor applies that is based on the truth of <code>BASIS-SENTENCE</code> (about the basis) and <code>EXTENDED-SENTENCE</code>. In general, <code>BASIS-SENTENCE</code> (about the basis) and <code>EXTENDED-SENTENCE</code> differ in more ways than that just <code>BASIS-SENTENCE</code> mentions the metaphor's basis where <code>EXTENDED-SENTENCE</code> mentions that to which <code>METAPHOR</code> is applicable. Cf. #$metaphorFoundedOnSimilarity.") :- x_cid(a65b16505f0056).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505f0056,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16505f0056,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part07.krf').
