x_comment(x_PerRatioColFn,"A CollectionDenotingFunction that returns collection instances of QuantityType that are specializations of RatioQuantity. Specifically, where NUMERATOR-TYPE and DENOMINATOR-TYPE are both instances of #$InterconvertibleUnitType, (#$PerRatioColFn NUMERATOR-TYPE DENOMINATOR-TYPE) denotes all scalar quantities that can be represented as a ratio where the numerator is measured by units of the first type and the denominator is measured by units of the second type.  Thus, e.g. (#$PerRatioColFn #$UnitOfMoney #$UnitOfVolume) would represent the collection of all quantities measuring a unit of money per unit volume, such as ((#$PerFn #$Dollar-UnitedStates #$Barrel-UnitOfVolume) 108), ((#$PerFn #$Ruble-Russia #$Liter) 100), ((#$PerFn #$Rupee-Nepal #$Gallon-Imperial) 52.8), and so on. ") :- x_cid(a65b16505f007a).
