x_comment('x_in-EmbeddedInFluidMatrix',"A #$ConnectionPredicate and specialization of #$sticksInto (q.v.) that relates #$PartiallyTangibles to the #$FluidTangibleThing matrices in which they are embedded. Note that <code>(#$in-EmbeddedInFluidMatrix OBJ MATRIX)</code> does not mean that OBJ is #$in-ImmersedGeneric in <code>MATRIX</code>, nor that it is wet in any appreciable way. Such embeddings have many of the properties associated with #$in-Rooted, except that one of the associated objects is technically a fluid. Most instances of #$in-EmbeddedInFluidMatrix relations occur at the molecular level (e.g., #$Molecules and #$MacromolecularComplexes embedded in #$CellularMembranes), but probably not all (e.g. #$Cells in an #$ExtracellularMatrix).") :- x_cid(a65b16505f007c).
