x_comment(x_awayFromLocation,"The predicate #$awayFromLocation is used to indicate a location away from which something moves in a particular movement.  <code>(#$awayFromLocation MOVE LOC)</code> means that, when movement ends, each #$objectMoving in <code>MOVE</code> (a #$Movement-TranslationEvent) is found further from <code>LOC</code> than it was when the event <code>MOVE</code> started. <code>LOC</code> may be, but is not necessarily, the starting location of each #$objectMoving in that event.  For that stronger meaning, see the spec-predicate #$fromLocation.  See also #$motionPathway-Complete, #$pathConnects.") :- x_cid(a65b16505f00b8).
