x_comment(x_OrganicFuelMolecule,"A collection of #$Molecules.  Instances of #$OrganicFuelMolecule are molecules of #$OrganicCompounds that are rich in bonds between #$Carbon and #$Hydrogen #$Atoms. When these molecules are oxidized, the high potential energy of the electrons in the C-H bonds is set free when new, lower-energy bonds form, and can be harnessed to do work or released as heat.  Examples include molecules of substances used as fuels for machines or industrial processes, like (#$MoleculeFn #$Propane), as well as molecules used by living cells to do work, such as (#$MoleculeFn #$CarbohydrateStuff) and (#$MoleculeFn #$Lipid). ") :- x_cid(a65b16505f00ba).
