x_comment(x_fieldPrinciples,"<code>(#$fieldPrinciples FIELD PROPOSITION)</code> means that the instance <code>PROPOSITION</code> of #$Proposition is one of the principles of <code>FIELD</code>, an instance of #$FieldOfStudy.  #$fieldPrinciples holds not of just any proposition that the practitioners of <code>FIELD</code> are likely to assent to (e.g., That Paris is a city in France, does not qualify as a principle of any field; it's just something everybody knows.); rather a principle is held up by the practitioners as an established truth that explains some aspect of the phenomena of interest to the field.  The body of such principles for a field (plus its corollaries) in some loose sense comprises \"the prevalent theory\" of a field.") :- x_cid(a65b16505f00bc).
