x_comment(x_electronegativityOfType,"(#$electronegativityOfType ELEMENT VALUE) indicates the ability of an atom in a molecule to attract electrons to itself.  The relative electronegativities of two atoms sharing a bond indicate whether that bond would be non-polar, polar covalent, or ionic.  An atom with high #$ionizationEnergy and very negative #$electronAffinityOfType would be very electronegative.  Values of #$electronegativityOfType range from 0.7 to 4.0.") :- x_cid(a65b16505f00ce).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505f00ce,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
