x_comment(x_InvasionOfCellByVirusTypeFn,"<code>(#$InvasionOfCellByVirusTypeFn VIRUS-TYPE)</code> denotes the collection of instances of #$ViralInvasionOfCell in which an individual cell is invaded by a virus of type <code>VIRUS-TYPE</code>. Thus, <code>(#$InvasionOfCellByVirusTypeFn #$HumanImmunodeficiencyVirus)</code> denotes the collection of events in which an individual cell is invaded by an instance of the #$HumanImmunodeficiencyVirus. Note that, although a cell may be invaded/infected by a particular virus, it usually does not have the associated #$ViralInfection, this is something contracted by a host organism as a whole, and it usually involves many millions of #$ViralInvasionOfCell subevents (except when the host is itself a microorganism).") :- x_cid(a65b16505f00d6).
