x_comment(x_emergentPartType,"<code>(#$emergentPartType WHOLE-TYPE PART-TYPE EMERGENT-PART-TYPE)</code> means that whenever any instance <code>PART</code> of <code>PART-TYPE</code> is part of any instance <code>WHOLE</code> of <code>WHOLE-TYPE</code>, then some <code>EMERGENT-PART</code> (an instance of <code>EMERGENT-PART</code>) is also part of <code>WHOLE</code> because <code>PART</code> is <code>PART</code> of <code>WHOLE</code>.  In other words, as parts of instances of <code>WHOLE-TYPE</code>, instances of <code>EMERGENT-PART-TYPE</code> <i>covary with</i> and <i>depend on</i> (in a non-causal sense of \"dependence\") instances of <code>PART-TYPE</code> (although instances of <code>PART-TYPE</code> are not necessary for instances of <code>EMERGENT-PART-TYPE</code>, even as parts of <code>WHOLE-TYPE</code>) Cf. the more specific predicate, #$supervenientPartType.") :- x_cid(a65b16505f0125).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505f0125,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16505f0125,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part07.krf').
