x_comment(x_supervenientPartType,"<code>(#$supervenientPartType WHOLE-TYPE PART-TYPE SV-PART-TYPE)</code> means that whenever any instance <code>PART</code> of <code>PART-TYPE</code> is part of any instance <code>WHOLE</code> of <code>WHOLE-TYPE</code>, then some <code>SV-PART</code> (an instance of <code>SV-PART</code>) is also part of <code>WHOLE</code> because <code>PART</code> is <code>PART</code> of <code>WHOLE</code>, and, further: <code>WHOLE</code> is not reducible to <code>PART</code>.  In other words, as parts of instances of <code>WHOLE-TYPE</code>, instances of <code>SV-PART-TYPE</code> <i>covary with</i>, <i>depend on</i> (in a non-causal sense of \"dependence\") and <i>are not reducible to</i> instances of <code>PART-TYPE</code> (although instances of <code>PART-TYPE</code> are not necessary for instances of <code>SV-PART-TYPE</code>, even as parts of <code>WHOLE-TYPE</code>) Cf. the more general predicate, #$emergentPartType.") :- x_cid(a65b16505f0126).
