x_comment(x_EnzymeMoleculeTypeByReactionType,"A collection of collections. Each instance is a collection of #$EnzymeMolecules  such that its instances are characteristically capable of catalyzing some instance of #$SpecifiedChemicalInteractionType. For example, #$ProteinKinaseMolecule, the collection of enzyme molecules that can catalyze phosphorylation of protein molecules, is an instance.  It is not necessary that instances of instances resemble each other in their chemical formula or structure. There are many different types of #$ProteinKinaseMolecule that occur in different organisms or have different roles within the same organism.  Other instances of #$EnzymeMoleculeTypeByReactionType may be more consistent in the structure of their instances; in those cases, they should also be instances of #$ProteinMoleculeTypeByChemicalCompoundType or #$ProteinMoleculeTypeByChemicalSpecies.  For example, #$AdenylylCyclaseMolecule has ten known variants in mammals that differ in their sequence of anmino acids and are coded for by different genes, but they all share similarities in structure.  It is therefore also an instance of #$ProteinMoleculeTypeByChemicalCompoundType.") :- x_cid(a65b16505f0130).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505f0130,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16505f0130,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part07.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16505f0130,21191).
xc_kb_names(a65b16505f0130,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16505f0130,[]).
x_comment(x_EventTypeGrainFn,"A #$ReifiableFunction and #$GenlsPreservingSubcollectionDenotingFunction, which maps from specializations of #$Event which are #$TemporalStuffType to the \"grain\" or \"granule\" of that type of event. <code>(#$EventTypeGrainFn EVENT-TYPE)</code> denotes a specialization of <code>EVENT-TYPE</code> whose instances can't be spatiotemporally subdivided without rendering them no longer instances of <code>EVENT-TYPE</code>. For example, (#$EventTypeGrainFn #$Glycolysis) is the class of #$Glycolysis reactions which are \"one pass\" all the way through the event, and in which the actors are individual #$ChemicalObjects, not masses of them. ") :- x_cid(a65b16505f0131).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505f0131,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
