x_comment('x_emergentPartType-Causal',"<code>(#$emergentPartType-Causal WHOLE-TYPE PART-TYPE EMERGENT-PART-TYPE)</code> means that whenever any instance <code>PART</code> of <code>PART-TYPE</code> is part of any instance <code>WHOLE</code> of <code>WHOLE-TYPE</code>, then some <code>EMERGENT-PART</code> (an instance of <code>EMERGENT-PART</code>) is also caused to be part of <code>WHOLE</code> because <code>PART</code> is <code>PART</code> of <code>WHOLE</code>.  In other words, as parts of instances of <code>WHOLE-TYPE</code>, instances of <code>EMERGENT-PART-TYPE</code> <i>covary with</i> and are <i>caused by</i> instances of <code>PART-TYPE</code> (although instances of <code>PART-TYPE</code> are not necessary for instances of <code>EMERGENT-PART-TYPE</code>, even as parts of <code>WHOLE-TYPE</code>) Cf. the more general predicate, #$emergentPartType.") :- x_cid(a65b16505f014b).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505f014b,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16505f014b,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part07.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16505f014b,21236).
xc_kb_names(a65b16505f014b,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16505f014b,[]).
x_comment(x_subSitTypeMakesTypeAvailableForParticipationInSitType,"<code>(#$subSitTypeMakesTypeAvailableForParticipationInSitType SCRIPT SCENE-1 TYPE SCENE-2)</code> means that in events of type <code>SCRIPT</code>, sub-events of type <code>SCENE-1</code> are such that they make objects of type <code>TYPE</code> available for playing a role \"downstream\" in events of type <code>SCENE-2</code>.  <code>SCENE-1</code> can make <code>TYPE</code> available by creating instances of <code>TYPE</code> or generally having instance of <code>TYPE</code> play an #$outputs role, or by transforming an object so that it becomes of type <code>TYPE</code>, or by changing some property of an object of type <code>TYPE</code> so that it is suitable for playing the appropriate role in <code>SCENE-2</code>.") :- x_cid(a65b16505f014c).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505f014c,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16505f014c,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part07.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16505f014c,21237).
xc_kb_names(a65b16505f014c,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16505f014c,[]).
x_comment('x_emergentProperty-AllExistsExists-Causal',"(#$emergentProperty-AllExistsExists-Causal TYPE BASE-PRED BASE-COL E-PRED E-COL) means that whenever any instance INS of TYPE bears the relation BASE-PRED to some instance B-INS of BASE-COL (i.e. (BASE-PRED INS B-INS) is true), that causes INS to also beas the relation E-PRED to some instance E-INS of E-COL (i.e. for some instance E-INS of E-COL (E-PRED INS E-INS) is true).  In other words, the truth of:  <p> <code> (thereExists ?Y <br> (and <br> (isa ?Y BASE-COL) <br> (B-PRED INS ?Y)))   </code><p> <i>causes</i> the truth of  <p> <code>   (thereExists ?X  <br>   (and <br>      (isa ?X E-COL)   <br>   (E-PRED INS ?X))) </code>  Cf. the more general predicate, #$emergentProperty-AllExistsExists.") :- x_cid(a65b16505f014d).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505f014d,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16505f014d,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part07.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16505f014d,21238).
