x_comment('x_emergentProperty-AllExistsExists',"(#$emergentProperty-AllExistsExists TYPE BASE-PRED BASE-COL E-PRED E-COL) means that whenever any instance INS of TYPE bears the relation BASE-PRED to some instance B-INS of BASE-COL (i.e. (BASE-PRED INS B-INS) is true), then INS also bears the relation E-PRED to some instance E-INS of E-COL (i.e. for some instance E-INS of E-COL (E-PRED INS E-INS) is true) because (BASE-PRED INS B-INS) is true.  In other words, the truth of: <p> <code>   (thereExists ?X  <br>   (and <br>      (isa ?X E-COL)   <br>   (E-PRED INS ?X))) </code><p> <i>covaries</i> with and <i>depends</i> on (in a possibly non-causal sense of \"dependence\") the truth of  <p> <code> (thereExists ?Y <br> (and <br> (isa ?Y BASE-COL) <br> (B-PRED INS ?Y)))   </code><p> However, the truth of the latter need not be necessary for the truth of the former.   Cf. the more specific predicate, #$supervenientProperty-AllExistsExists.") :- x_cid(a65b16505f014e).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505f014e,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16505f014e,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part07.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16505f014e,21239).
xc_kb_names(a65b16505f014e,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16505f014e,[]).
x_comment('x_supervenientProperty-AllExistsExists',"(#$supervenientProperty-AllExistsExists TYPE BASE-PRED BASE-COL E-PRED E-COL) means that whenever any instance INS of TYPE bears the relation BASE-PRED to some instance B-INS of BASE-COL (i.e. (BASE-PRED INS B-INS) is true), then INS also bears the relation E-PRED to some instance E-INS of E-COL (i.e. for some instance E-INS of E-COL (E-PRED INS E-INS) is true) because (BASE-PRED INS B-INS) is true.  Further: the property INS has in virtue bearing E-PRED to E-INS is not reducible to the property INS has in virtue bearing BASE-PRED to B-INS.  In other words, the truth of: <p> <code>   (thereExists ?X  <br>   (and <br>      (isa ?X E-COL)   <br>   (E-PRED INS ?X))) </code><p> is <i>irreducible to</i>, <i>covaries</i> with, and <i>depends</i> on (in a possibly non-causal sense of \"dependence\") the truth of  <p> <code> (thereExists ?Y <br> (and <br> (isa ?Y BASE-COL) <br> (B-PRED INS ?Y)))   </code><p> However, the truth of the latter need not be necessary for the truth of the former. Cf. the more general predicate, #$emergentProperty-AllExistsExists.") :- x_cid(a65b16505f014f).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505f014f,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
