x_comment(x_cellRecognizedAsTypeInRecognitionEvent,"<code>(cellRecognizedAsTypeInRecognitionEvent RECOG CELL\nCELL-TYPE)</code> means that in #$CellularRecognitionEvent\n<code>RECOG</code>, #$Cell <code>CELL</code> was \"recognized\" as\nbeing of type <code>CELL-TYPE</code>, in the sense that the\n\"recognizing\" cell(s) respond(s) to the cell differentially and in\nthe same manner that they would respond to all other instances of\n<code>CELL-TYPE</code>. Thus, <code>CELL-TYPE</code> should generally\nbe specified as the most general collection of #$Cells with respect to\nwhose instances the differential response of the recognizing #$Cell\nwould be invariant.") :- x_cid(a65b16505f016f).
