x_comment('x_FunctionalGroup-Molecular',"A collection of microscopic-scale objects; a subset of #$ChemicalObject.  Every instance of #$FunctionalGroup-Molecular is a microscopic object whose component atoms are all chemically bonded to each other, and which tend to \"travel as a unit\" when the group is bonded to other atoms to form a complete molecule.   A #$FunctionalGroup-Molecular often acts as a unit in chemical reactions and is of a chemical species whose instances form a standard part of numerous different types chemicals.  Examples: individual #$Nucleotides in a #$DNAMolecule, or phosphate groups (see #$MonophosphateGroup) as part of ATP or in solution.  Counterexample: an ionized molecule.  ") :- x_cid(a65b16505f017f).
