x_comment(x_partTypeSupportsCapabilityInstance,"Where CAPABILITY is an instance of #$Capability, and TYPE-CAP-PRED is the type-level #$correspondingPreds-Capability of CAP-PRED, (#$partTypeSupportsCapabilityInstance PART-TYPE CAP-PRED CAPABILITY) means that, where (#$capabilityToRoleSitType ROLE SIT-TYPE CAPABILITY) and for any type of system SYSTEM-TYPE such that ($#functionallyImportantPhysicalPartTypeOfWholeType SYSTEM-TYPE PART-TYPE), (TYPE-CAP-PRED SYSTEM-TYPE SIT-TYPE ROLE). Intuitively, (#$partTypeSupportsCapabilityInstance PART-TYPE CAP-PRED CAPABILITY) means that, where CAPABILITY is a #$Capability such that the relevant capability relation is underspecified, (i.e., we don't know that CAPABILITY is a fiscal capability, a behavioral capability, an anatomic capability, etc.), instances of PART-TYPE support CAPABILITY in systems that include them as components, so that where CAPABILITY is associated with playing ROLE in instances of SIT-TYPE, (CAP-PRED INST SIT-TYPE ROLE) ordinarily holds for any instance that has an instance of PART-TYPE as a functional part.") :- x_cid(a65b16505f0189).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505f0189,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
