x_comment(x_partTypeSupportsCapabilityInstanceInType,"Where CAPABILITY is an instance of #$Capability, and TYPE-CAP-PRED is the type-level #$correspondingPreds-Capability of CAP-PRED, (#$partTypeSupportsCapabilityInstanceInType PART-TYPE CAP-PRED CAPABILITY AGT-TYPE) means that, where (#$capabilityToRoleSitType ROLE SIT-TYPE CAPABILITY) and for any type of system SYSTEM-TYPE such that (genls SYSTEM-TYPE AGT-TYPE) and such that ($#functionallyImportantPhysicalPartTypeOfWholeType SYSTEM-TYPE PART-TYPE), (TYPE-CAP-PRED SYSTEM-TYPE SIT-TYPE ROLE). Intuitively, (#$partTypeSupportsCapabilityInstanceInType PART-TYPE CAP-PRED CAPABILITY AGT-TYPE) means that, where CAPABILITY is a #$Capability such that the relevant capability relation is underspecified, (i.e., we don't know that CAPABILITY is a fiscal capability, a behavioral capability, an anatomic capability, etc.), instances of PART-TYPE support CAPABILITY in instances of AGT-TYPE that include them as components, so that where CAPABILITY is associated with playing ROLE in instances of SIT-TYPE, (CAP-PRED INST SIT-TYPE ROLE) ordinarily holds for any instance of AGT-TYPE that has an instance of PART-TYPE as a functional part.") :- x_cid(a65b16505f018a).
