x_comment(x_RegulatedTransportSituation,"The collection of all situations in which flows or tranlations of objects or stuffs across a demarcated boundary are preferential, i.e., non-random, relative to type.  Every #$RegulatedTransportSituation features exactly one #$PartiallyTangible object as a #$transportBoundarySystem:  this may consist in a physical barrier that prevents individuals of a certain type from entering or leaving an area, or in a more complex system that effects interdiction partially through signals and information processing on the part of the agents being interdicted.  Every #$RegulatedTransportSituation also features some item or number of items that are permitted to pass through the boundary in question (#$itemAdmitted), and another item or number of items which are not permitted to pass through the boundary in question (#$itemInterdicted).  Assuming the boudary forms an enclosed region the things that are interdicted may be confined within the enclosed area (#$itemContained), or they may be prevented from entering the enclosed area (#$itemExcluded):  likewise instances that are #$itemAdmitted may be #$itemPermittedEntry or #$itemPermittedExit.  Some cases of #$RegulatedTransportSituation are such that some interdicted items may be #$itemContained while others are #$itemExcluded.  Some instances of #$RegulatedTransportSituation may also be such that all instances that are #$itemAdmitted and all instances that are #$itemInterdicted have all salient features in common, i.e., what is being regulated is exclusively the rate of flow of things of a certain type.  It may also be the case that there are two or several types of things such that instances are both admitted and interdicted (contained or excluded) throughout the course of the situation, but at different rates depending on the type.  In the extreme (but not necessarily uncommon) case, a type of thing may be exclusively admitted while another type of thing is exclusively interdicted. It is not out of the question that one and the same object may be both #$itemAdmitted and #$itemInterdicted at different times in the same #$RegulatedTransportSituation:  #$itemAdmitted and #$itemInterdicted are not negation preds.  Situationally, every #$RegulatedTransportSituation includes a (#$GroupFn #$CrossingABorder) that is the situational sum of all the boundary-crossings that happen as part of the situation; likewise a mass #$BoundarySituation that is also a (#$GroupFn #$BoundarySituation):  the situational sum of all interdictions that occur in the course of the #$RegulatedTransportSituation.") :- x_cid(a65b16505f01fc).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505f01fc,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
