x_comment(x_exceptForInArg,"A meta-predicate used to state exceptions to rules encoded as ground atomic formulae via rule macro predicates, <code>(#$exceptFor THING N ASSERTION)</code> means that substituting <code>THING</code> in for the <code>N</code>th argument to the #$assertionSentence <code>SENT</code> of <code>ASSERTION</code> yields a sentence <code>EXCEPTIONAL</code> that is not true, despite the fact that <code>SENT</code> encodes a rule from which <code>EXCEPTIONAL</code> logically follows.  For example, where <code>ASSERTION</code> is an assertion of the sentence, <p><code>((#$TypeCapableFn #$anatomicallyCapableOf) #$Flying-FlappingWings #$Bird #$doneBy)</code>, <p>the assertion, <p><code>(#$exceptForInArg #$Ostrich 2 ASSERTION)</code> <p>means that ostriches are an exception to this rule, i.e., that <p><code>((#$TypeCapableFn #$anatomicallyCapableOf) #$Flying-FlappingWings #$Ostrich #$doneBy)</code> <p>is not true.") :- x_cid(a65b16505f0206).
