x_comment(x_ElectronTransportChain,"A specialization of #$BiochemicalPathway.  Each instance of #$ElectronTransportChain is a sequence of exergonic #$SimpleRedoxReactions in which #$Electrons are passed from a donor to a molecule that is more  electronegative, then from that molecule to the next in the chain (yet more electronegative), until the final electron acceptor receives the electron.  Instead of passing the electron directly to the final acceptor, which would lead to a large release of energy, an #$ElectronTransportChain releases energy in controlled steps, often generating energy containing molecules like #$AdenosineTriphosphate along the way.  #$ElectronTransportChains occur as part of #$CellularRespiration and as part of the #$LightDependentStepOfPhotosynthesis.") :- x_cid(a65b16505f0299).
