x_comment(x_MethodType,"A specialization of #$LearnedActivityType, #$MethodType is the the collection of types of purposeful actions that decompose into a common pattern of sub-event-types and/or role-player types (e.g., instruments) used in the course of the event.  #$MethodType is an instance of #$FacetingBasisCollectionType, which means that ordinarily, an instance of #$MethodType is such by virtue of being a <i>method of</i> doing some class of #$PurposefulAction.  When an instance <code>ACTION-TYPE</code> of #$MethodType requires a high level of skill on the part of the performer, or its sub-event/role-player-type structure is so rigid that minor deviations from that structure would entail a failure to actualize an instance of <code>ACTION-TYPE</code>, then <code>ACTION-TYPE</code> is likely to be an instance of the more specialized #$TechniqueType.") :- x_cid(a65b16505f0343).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505f0343,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
