x_comment(x_FacetingBasisCollectionType,"An instance of #$CollectionType.  Each instance <code>COLL-TYPE</code> of #$FacetingBasisCollectionType is a collection of second order or higher (most of) whose instances <code>COLL</code> are also instances of some instance <code>FACET</code> of #$FacetingCollectionType such that <code>(#$genls FACET COLL-TYPE)</code>.  It is by virtue of this faceting that these <code>COLL</code> collections are instances of <code>COLL-TYPE</code>.  For example, <code>(#$isa #$TechniqueType #$FacetingBasisCollectionType)</code>, because to be an instance of #$TechniqueType (i.e., to be a technique), is to be a collection of events that follow a certain pattern for instantiating some kind of purposeful action, where that pattern requires a certain amount of skill.  More concisely, to be a  technique is to be a technique relative to (a technique <i>for doing</i>) some kind of purposeful action or other. Thus the instances of #$TechniqueType are techniques <i>for</i> sewing, <i>for</i> solving puzzles, <i>for</i> training, etc, and thus, in addition to instantiating #$TehcniqueType, these instances will instantiate a collection that facets sewing, solving puzzles, etc., into distinct techniques.") :- x_cid(a65b16505f0345).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505f0345,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16505f0345,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part07.krf').
