x_comment(x_productOrServiceTypeAssignedCategory,"(#$productOrServiceTypeAssignedCategory INDEP-PROD-TYPE DEP-PROD-TYPE CAT) means that expenses incurred during the provisioning of INDEP-PROD-TYPE involve DEP-PROD-TYPE and are categorized under the cost category CAT.  E.g. Bob's Flower Shop's \"BurstOfColor\" flower product has expenses relating to \"CrystalVase-Product\" which they classify under the\"ContainersAndWrapping\" cost category.  So, when characterizing Bob's expenses you assert \n<pre>\n<code>\n  (productOrServiceTypeAssignedCategory BurstOfColor CrystalVase-Product ContainersAndWrapping)</code></pre>\n\nNote that this representation assumes either a context exclusive to Bob's use of the BurstOfColor product or that BurstOfColor is itself a vendor/provider specific product type.  The relationship is undefined if neither of those contexts of use obtain.") :- x_cid(a65b16505f03c3).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505f03c3,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
