x_comment(x_MarketDataProductWithContentTypeFn,"(#$MarketDataProductWithContentTypeFn COLL) denotes the collection of market data products whose data fields include information pertaining to instances of COLL characterized as attributes of the focal entities of the product (cf. #$marketDataProductAboutAssetType).  More formally, for any COLL, each instance of (#$MarketDataProductWithContentTypeFn COLL), PRODUCT, is such that it has some propositional content type, PROP-TYPE associated with it such that \n<pre>\n   (#$relationAllExists #$propositionalInfoAbout PROP-TYPE COLL)\n</pre>\n\nFurthermore this propositional content characterizes (attributes some properties to) the focal entities -- either directly or indirectly -- of the product.  To put it another way, each instance of (#$MarketDataProductWithContentTypeFn COLL) is a data product that includes information about instances of COLL where that information is used to characterize another entity.\n<br><br>\nFor example, (#$MarketDataProductWithContentTypeFn #$FinancialInstrumentTransaction) is the collection of instances of #$MarketDataProduct-PIT whose instances include information about financial instrument transactions -- e.g. stock and bond sales -- as attributes of particular tradeable securities.  An example of an instance of this collection would be a daily summary from an exchange showing volumes of sales for each ticker symbol.  A negative example would be a simple list of dates of sales with no information linking the sales to particular products or deals. ") :- x_cid(a65b16505f041a).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505f041a,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16505f041a,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part07.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16505f041a,22076).
xc_kb_names(a65b16505f041a,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16505f041a,[]).
