x_comment(x_transportedUpAGradientIn,"(#$transportedUpAGradientIn TRANSPORT ITEM) means that there is a #$TransBoundaryGradient with a #$regionOfHighConcentration HIGH-CON and a #$regionOfLowConcentration LOW-CON such that there is a #$MovementEvent that is a #$properSubEvents of TRANSPORT where ITEM is the #$primaryObjectMoving and where the #$fromLocation is LOW-CON and the #$toLocation is HIGH-CON. Intuitively, (#$transportedUpAGradientIn TRANSPORT ITEM) means that at some point in TRANSPORT, ITEM moves from the low-concentration region to the high-concentration region of a #$TransBoundaryGradient that temporally intersects TRANSPORT.") :- x_cid(a65b16505f0458).
