x_comment(x_ProtonPump,"Instances of #$ProtonPump are #$TransmembraneProteins  in a biological membrane (see #$BiologicalMembrane) that actively move #$Protons across the membrane from the side with a low concentration to the side with a high concentration. In reality, the protons are not free on the high-concentration side, but immediately associate with some other molecule.  E.g., they may associate with molecules of water to form #$HydroniumIons.<p> #$ProtonPumps occur in the membranes of each #$Mitochondrion, where they concentrate protons in the intermembrane space.  They also act to eject protons from #$Osteoclasts in order to acidify a region where bone is to be resorbed.") :- x_cid(a65b16505f049b).
xc_microtheory(a65b16505f049b,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
