x_comment(x_relationExistsManyInstance,"A ternary #$RuleMacroPredicate that can    be used to state that a given binary predicate stands in a certain relationship    with respect to a given collection and a given thing.     (#$relationExistsManyInstance BINPRED COL THING) means that there are many    instances INST(i) of COL such that (BINPRED INST(i) THING) holds.  It is    equivalent to (#$relationExistsRangeInstance BINPRED COL THING #$Many-Quant), and    thus to the more complex form (for which it can in effect be used as shorthand):   <p>(#$thereExistRange #$Many-Quant ?INST(#$and(#$isa ?INST COL2(BINPRED ?INST    THING))) .<p>For example, `(#$relationExistsManyInstance #$genls #$Collection    #$HittingAnObject)' means that there are many collections which generalize to    #$HittingAnObject.  See also #$relationExistsRangeInstance.") :- x_cid(a65b16505f04f5).
