x_comment(x_equationFormFor,"<code>(#$equationFormFor THING EQUATION)</code> means that <code>EQUATION</code> is the form of a mathematical equation that describes important characteristics of <code>THING</code>.  For example, if <code>THING</code> is a physical principle, such as #$NewtonsSecondLaw, then that law, as it is commonly expressed, corresponds to the equation <code>F=ma</code>, where <code>F</code> is the sum of the forces acting on an object, <code>m</code> is its mass and <code>a</code> is its acceleration, so the following is true:  <br> <code>  (equationFormFor             NewtonsSecondLaw                   (numericallyEquals                       (The ForceVector)                 (TimesFn  (The LinearAccelerationVector) (The Mass))))  </code> .") :- x_cid(a65b16505f0568).
